//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//| KMIE_MarketDNA_Lite.mq5                                          |
//| Standalone Gold-only EA. Strict 2-stage flow, nothing else:       |
//|   Market DNA  ->  18-Mind Vote                                    |
//| The 18-Mind Vote's majority direction is the trade signal, gated  |
//| ONLY by a minimum-vote-count threshold (Inp_MindsVoteMinCount).   |
//| 2026-08-20, explicit operator request: M1 3-Bar confirmation      |
//| removed entirely. No confidence grading, no conflict scoring, no  |
//| daily guardrails, no spread guard. Market DNA now classifies 11   |
//| active states (originally an 18-state list; LIQUIDITY_HUNT was    |
//| permanently removed 2026-08-30, UPTREND/DOWNTREND/EXPANSION/      |
//| COMPRESSION removed from the active set 2026-09-08 - see          |
//| ENUM_LITE_DNA's own header comment for the full removal note and  |
//| index-realignment detail) -                                       |
//| same regime NAMES as the real Framework 10C, fresh self-contained |
//| math. Trading can be turned on/off per regime (Market DNA Regime  |
//| Allow-List group below), one switch per regime, all default true. |
//| Self-contained fresh rewrite (no #include of KMIE_* engine files).|
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
#property strict
#property version   "11.00"
#property description "KMIE Market DNA Lite - Gold-only. Basis: 5 completed candles + 1 running candle. Flow: raw OHLC -> Candle Intelligence (aggression/exhaustion/rejection/absorption/buyingStrength/sellingStrength) -> Market DNA (16-state, regime allow-list) -> 18-Mind Vote (min-vote threshold)."

//====================================================================
// INPUTS
//====================================================================
input group "Safety"
input bool   Inp_ExecutionEnabled        = true;    // master switch. false = dashboard only, never sends an order

input group "Symbol Guard"
input string Inp_TradeSymbol             = "";        // explicit symbol to trade. Blank = use whatever chart this EA is attached to instead (original/default behavior). No algorithm/logic depends on which symbol is picked here. 2026-08-22: reverted from "XAUUSD247" - that symbol rejected orders with FIFO_CLOSE (10044), broker doesn't allow trading it as expected.
input string Inp_AllowedSymbolContains   = "XAUUSD";     // EA refuses to run (InitFails) unless the resolved trade symbol contains this substring

input group "Analysis Cycle"
input int    Inp_M1LookbackBars          = 25;      // closed M1 candles pulled once per cycle, shared by all 18 Minds
//--- 2026-09-23, explicit operator request ("currently we are using the 25 Bars for M5 DNA and Minds
//--- votes can you make 15 Bars with same dna and minds algo"): a NEW, DEDICATED M5-only lookback,
//--- deliberately independent of Inp_M1LookbackBars/Inp_MarketDNALookbackCandles and of the per-session
//--- Inp_SessionBarsMinds_*/Inp_SessionBarsDna_* overrides (all of which continue to drive ONLY the M1
//--- side, completely unchanged) - before this input existed, the M5 CopyRates fetch in OnTick() and
//--- EvaluateMarketDnaM5()'s own internal window size both silently reused
//--- ResolveEffectiveMindsLookback()/ResolveEffectiveDnaLookback() (the SAME M1/session-driven values),
//--- so M5 always tracked whatever M1's own bar count happened to be (25 by default). Same DNA/Minds
//--- ALGORITHM either way - only the WINDOW SIZE feeding it changes, per the operator's own "same dna
//--- and minds algo" framing.
input int    Inp_M5DnaMindsLookbackBars  = 15;      // closed M5 candles pulled once per cycle for M5 DNA + M5 18-Mind Vote - independent of the M1 lookback/per-session overrides above

//--- 2026-09-23, M15 PARALLEL PIPELINE: a NEW, DEDICATED M15-only lookback, mirroring
//--- Inp_M5DnaMindsLookbackBars immediately above exactly - fixed at 8 bars, deliberately independent of
//--- Inp_M1LookbackBars/Inp_MarketDNALookbackCandles, of the per-session Inp_SessionBarsMinds_*/
//--- Inp_SessionBarsDna_* overrides (M1-only, unchanged), AND of Inp_M5DnaMindsLookbackBars itself (M15
//--- never reuses M1's OR M5's lookback logic - it gets its own fixed, dedicated window). Same DNA/Minds
//--- ALGORITHM as M1 and M5 either way - only the WINDOW SIZE feeding it differs.
input int    Inp_M15DnaMindsLookbackBars = 8;       // closed M15 candles pulled once per cycle for M15 DNA + M15 18-Mind Vote - independent of the M1/M5 lookbacks above

input group "Market DNA"
input int    Inp_MarketDNALookbackCandles= 5;       // rolling-average window feeding the Market DNA classifier

input group "18-Mind Vote"
input int    Inp_MindsVoteMinCount       = 8;       // winning side must have AT LEAST this many of the 18 Minds agreeing to fire

//--- 2026-08-30, explicit operator request (ADD EMA 20/50 SLOPE TREND MIND): one new additive
//--- Mind - EMA20 vs EMA50 crossover, confirmed by EMA20 slope, gated by ATR-normalized
//--- separation. ATR is NOT its own Mind/vote - it is only an internal volatility-normalization
//--- input to this one Mind (see EvaluateEmaTrendMind()). Both existing vote gates
//--- (Inp_MindsVoteMinCount above, and the Early Re-Entry "9 active voters" literal in
//--- EarlyReEntryEligible()) are DELIBERATELY left unchanged by this addition, per explicit
//--- operator decision - adding a 15th voting Mind mechanically loosens both gates in relative
//--- terms (8/13->8/14 and 9/13->9/14 "active voter" fractions) and lowers the KMIE_LITE_MIND_COUNT
//--- confidence denominator's per-vote weight; this is a known, accepted, and DOCUMENTED side
//--- effect, not an oversight - see this EA's own change-log comment near KMIE_LITE_MIND_COUNT's
//--- definition for the full accounting. Inp_EMAMinGapATR's default (0.5) is chosen conservatively:
//--- it requires the EMA20/EMA50 separation to be at least half of one ATR before treating the
//--- separation as meaningful relative to current volatility, rejecting the common case where the
//--- two EMAs are only fractionally apart (noise-level separation, not a real structural trend).
input group "EMA Trend Mind (2026-08-30)"
input bool   Inp_EMATrendEnabled         = false;   // 2026-09-14, explicit operator request ("EMA 20 and EMA 50 should be inactive"): default changed true->false - this Mind now always reports WAIT (still occupies its array slot/id in the 18-Mind vote, never removed - Inp_MindsVoteMinCount's own semantics are unaffected, the other 17 minds are completely untouched)
input int    Inp_EMAFastPeriod           = 20;      // fast EMA period (bars), closed candles only
input int    Inp_EMASlowPeriod           = 50;      // slow EMA period (bars), closed candles only
input int    Inp_EMASlopeLookback        = 2;        // EMA20 slope = EMA20[0] - EMA20[Inp_EMASlopeLookback], closed candles only
input double Inp_EMAMinGapATR            = 0.5;      // ABS(EMA20-EMA50)/ATR must be >= this for a BUY/SELL vote; see rationale above
input double Inp_EMANeutralGapATR = 0.375; // 2026-09-09, explicit operator request: data-grounded (real ~6-day XAUUSD M1 history, n=4106 readings) threshold for the NEW EMA neutral-market blocker - DELIBERATELY DIFFERENT from Inp_EMAMinGapATR (0.5, the existing "enough separation to vote" threshold) - this is a stricter/narrower/ADDITIONAL condition (normalizedGap<=this AND >=1 crossover in trailing 20 bars), not a duplicate of the existing gate.
input double Inp_EMAExtensionMaxATR = 2.0; // 2026-09-09, explicit operator request (data-grounded: real ~6-day XAUUSD M1 history, n=4288 readings, median=0.87 ATR/p90=2.20 ATR/p99=5.19 ATR - matches existing Inp_FairValueExtensionThresholdATR=2.0 precedent exactly): maximum (price-EMA20)/ATR distance before a directionally-valid trend is classified EMA_TREND_EXTENDED (wait-for-pullback) rather than EMA_TREND_CONTINUATION (safe to confirm). CALIBRATION PARAMETER - operator-adjustable. NOTE 2026-09-11: Inp_EMAExtensionMaxATR is REUSED (not replaced) by the new EMA35-based extension check - see ClassifyEmaEntryState()'s updated header.
input double Inp_EMA35NeutralBandATR = 0.10; // 2026-09-11, explicit operator request (ACTIVE_PING/EMA35 ARCHITECTURE REWIRE): EMA35 neutral corridor threshold (ATR-normalized abs(price-EMA35) distance) - price==EMA35 is unsuitable for M1 (near-never exactly true), so this uses abs(price-EMA35)/ATR<=threshold instead. DELIBERATELY DIFFERENT SCALE from Inp_EMANeutralGapATR (0.375, the OLD EMA20/50-gap-based neutral threshold, now disconnected from any live gate - see ClassifyEmaNeutral()'s updated header). CALIBRATION PARAMETER - operator-adjustable.

//--- 2026-09-18, explicit operator request ("MY OPPORTUNITY CONSUMED IS WORKING ITS TOTALY UPTREND BUT
//--- BOT NOT EXCUTING THE TRADE WHY") - ported into this baseline file from KMIE_MarketDNA_Lite.mq5 -
//--- live-verified root cause: this file's own ACTIVE_PING SIMPLIFIED TO EMA20/50 change (r.active =
//--- r.corridorActive, plus a per-tick crossing flag) narrowed g_activePing.active down to ONLY two
//--- moments - price sitting BETWEEN EMA20/EMA50, or the exact tick price crosses both. A sustained trend
//--- that has ALREADY moved cleanly above (or below) both EMAs and kept running - the "totally uptrend"
//--- case the operator is describing - satisfies NEITHER condition: it isn't inside the corridor (price
//--- is past both lines) and it isn't a fresh cross (that already happened bars ago). Live evidence (from
//--- the original fix, KMIE_MarketDNA_Lite.mq5): 2026-09-18 06:02-06:06 UTC, EMA20=4352.89/EMA50=4349.82,
//--- price running 4353-4359 (confirmed via bars.jsonl - 8 consecutive M1 closes climbing cleanly, not
//--- noise), ACTIVE_PING's own [ACTIVE_PING_ALREADY_FAVORABLE_EXECUTE] log line firing every tick (price
//--- already past its capture trigger) while Entry Approval blocked every single attempt with
//--- reason=OPPORTUNITY_CONSUMED - because g_activePing.active was false the whole time (price above
//--- both EMAs is neither "inside the corridor" nor "crossing this tick"). FIX (confirmed via
//--- AskUserQuestion - widen ACTIVE_PING to also count "price is clearly on the trending side of both
//--- EMAs with a healthy gap" as active): a THIRD condition, r.trendingSideActive - true when refClose is
//--- on the SAME side of BOTH EMA20 and EMA50 (fully above both, or fully below both - never just one),
//--- AND the normalized gap |EMA20-EMA50|/ATR clears Inp_ActivePingTrendingGapATR (a genuine, separated
//--- trend, not two EMAs sitting nearly on top of each other). Reuses r.atr/r.gap/r.normalizedGap - ALL
//--- already computed by ClassifyActivePing() for the corridor/slope checks above, no new calculation
//--- introduced. Default true (safe rollback), threshold default 0.5 - SAME value as the existing
//--- Inp_EMAMinGapATR ("enough separation to vote") for consistency, but a SEPARATE input (never silently
//--- coupled to a different gate's own tuning).
input group "ACTIVE_PING - Trending Side Extension (2026-09-18)"
input bool   Inp_ActivePingTrendingSideEnabled = true;  // ACTIVE_PING is ALSO active when price sits clearly on the trending side of BOTH EMA20 and EMA50 (not just inside the corridor or mid-cross) - fixes OPPORTUNITY_CONSUMED staying stuck during a sustained, already-running trend
input double Inp_ActivePingTrendingGapATR      = 0.5;   // minimum |EMA20-EMA50|/ATR required for the trending-side condition - same threshold Inp_EMAMinGapATR already uses for "genuine separation, not noise", kept as its own input rather than coupled to that gate

//--- 2026-08-30, explicit operator request (ADD NEW MTF ALIGNMENT MIND): one new additive Mind -
//--- "MTF Alignment" (stable id 17, array position 15) - answers "does the M1 directional
//--- environment have confirmation from M5 and M15?", strictly requiring all three timeframes to
//--- agree (3/3) before voting BUY or SELL; any 2/3 or weaker agreement is WAIT by explicit design,
//--- never a majority vote. Deliberately given ITS OWN Inp_MTFEma* inputs below, separate from
//--- Inp_EMAFastPeriod/Inp_EMASlowPeriod (the EMA Trend Mind's own inputs) - retuning one Mind must
//--- never silently retune the other. Same vote-gate accounting note as the EMA Trend Mind addition
//--- above applies here too: Inp_MindsVoteMinCount (8) and the Early Re-Entry "9 active voters"
//--- literal are BOTH deliberately left unchanged - adding this 16th Mind mechanically shifts their
//--- relative strictness again (8/14->8/15, 9/14->9/15) and the KMIE_LITE_MIND_COUNT confidence
//--- denominator; documented, not silently absorbed.
input group "MTF Alignment Mind (2026-08-30)"
input bool   Inp_MTFAlignmentEnabled     = true;    // false = this Mind always reports WAIT (still occupies its array slot/id, never removed)
input int    Inp_MTFEmaFastPeriod        = 20;      // fast EMA period (bars) - applied independently on M1, M5, AND M15, closed candles only
input int    Inp_MTFEmaSlowPeriod        = 50;      // slow EMA period (bars) - applied independently on M1, M5, AND M15, closed candles only
input int    Inp_MTFEmaSlopeLookback     = 2;        // per-timeframe EMA20 slope = EMA20[0] - EMA20[lookback], closed candles only, same lookback used on all 3 timeframes

//--- 2026-08-30, explicit operator request (ABSORPTION MIND - CONTROLLED PRODUCTION
//--- IMPLEMENTATION): one new additive Mind - "Absorption" (stable id 18, array position 16) -
//--- answers "is significant directional effort producing proportional price movement, or is it
//--- being absorbed by opposing activity?", entirely independent of Market DNA/g_dnaState/
//--- g_dnaScore and every other Mind's own result (see EvaluateAbsorptionMind()'s own header for
//--- the full independence proof). Built from a FRESH CopyRates window - deliberately NOT reusing
//--- the pre-existing ci.absorption field (EvaluateMarketDNA()'s Candle Intelligence stage already
//--- has its OWN directionless "effort without progress" scalar, ci.absorption = 100-(netDisplace/
//--- sumRange)*100 - found during this task's own required pre-implementation audit) - that field
//--- feeds Market DNA classification only and is explicitly NOT touched, read, or duplicated by
//--- this Mind, per the explicit operator decision to keep Absorption provably independent rather
//--- than share code with the Market DNA path. Same vote-gate accounting note as the two prior Mind
//--- additions applies here too: Inp_MindsVoteMinCount (8) and the Early Re-Entry "9 active voters"
//--- literal are BOTH deliberately left unchanged - adding this 17th Mind mechanically shifts their
//--- relative strictness again (8/15->8/16, 9/15->9/16) and the KMIE_LITE_MIND_COUNT confidence
//--- denominator; documented, not silently absorbed. Absorption uses the DEFAULT/normal Mind
//--- weight - no special Priority/Running-Candle weighting exists anywhere in this file to give it,
//--- and none is introduced here.
input group "Absorption Mind (2026-08-30)"
input bool   Inp_AbsorptionEnabled              = true;   // false = this Mind always reports WAIT (still occupies its array slot/id, never removed)
input int    Inp_AbsorptionLookback             = 20;      // closed M1 candles evaluated per cycle - same order of magnitude as Liquidity/Memory/Pattern's own 30-bar windows, chosen slightly smaller since Absorption needs recent effort, not a long-run average
input int    Inp_AbsorptionMinSamples           = 10;      // minimum closed candles required before this Mind will produce anything but WAIT - half of Inp_AbsorptionLookback, a conservative floor so a partially-filled window never drives a real vote
input double Inp_AbsorptionEffortThreshold      = 40.0;    // minimum normalized effort score (0..100) required before absorption evidence is even considered - below this, participation is too thin to mean anything (WAIT)
input double Inp_AbsorptionInefficiencyThreshold= 55.0;    // minimum inefficiency score (0..100, = weak response despite the effort present) required for a directional absorption reading - conservative middle-of-range default, tightenable after live calibration
input double Inp_AbsorptionRejectionThreshold   = 50.0;    // minimum dominant-side wick% of the newest closed candle required as rejection evidence - 50% means the wick alone is at least half of that candle's own range
input double Inp_AbsorptionConfirmationThreshold= 60.0;    // final absorptionScore (0..100, the weighted combination) must reach this before the Mind votes BUY/SELL instead of WAIT
input int    Inp_AbsorptionPersistenceCycles    = 2;       // consecutive same-side cycles required for full persistence credit - see EvaluateAbsorptionMind()'s own header; 2 is deliberately low (one confirming repeat), so genuine fast-moving absorption isn't penalized for lack of long history, while still ruling out a single one-off spike (validation Test 11)

//--- 2026-08-31, explicit operator request (FAIR VALUE / VWAP MIND - PRODUCTION IMPLEMENTATION):
//--- one new additive Mind - "Fair Value" (stable id 19, array position 17) - answers "where is
//--- price relative to volume-weighted fair value, and is that value being accepted or rejected?".
//--- PRE-IMPLEMENTATION AUDIT (this task's own required section 2): grepped the entire file for
//--- VWAP/"volume weighted"/"fair value"/"weighted price"/real_volume - NONE exist anywhere in this
//--- codebase. No authoritative VWAP calculation to reuse; this Mind implements its own, entirely
//--- fresh, self-contained. Volume source: MqlRates.tick_volume ONLY (real_volume was checked and
//--- is never used anywhere in this file - MT5's tick_volume is this EA's only available
//--- participation proxy, same conclusion the Absorption Mind's own audit reached one day earlier).
//--- Explicitly NOT "institutional centralized exchange VWAP" - reasoning strings below call it a
//--- "volume-weighted fair value proxy", per explicit instruction. Session boundary: broker/server
//--- time (TimeCurrent(), the SAME clock every existing timestamp in this file already uses via
//--- DashIsoTime(TimeCurrent()) - no separate timezone convention exists anywhere in this file to
//--- reuse or conflict with, confirmed by this task's own audit) midnight-to-now, recomputed FRESH
//--- from a bounded CopyRates window every cycle (never incrementally accumulated across ticks) -
//--- this sidesteps any EA-restart/session-reset staleness risk by construction, since there is no
//--- persistent running-sum state to go stale. Same vote-gate accounting note as the three prior
//--- Mind additions applies here too: Inp_MindsVoteMinCount (8) and the Early Re-Entry "9 active
//--- voters" literal are BOTH deliberately left unchanged - adding this 18th Mind mechanically
//--- shifts their relative strictness again (8/16->8/17, 9/16->9/17) and the KMIE_LITE_MIND_COUNT
//--- confidence denominator; documented, not silently absorbed. Fair Value uses the DEFAULT/normal
//--- Mind weight, same as every other Mind in this file.
input group "Fair Value Mind (2026-08-31)"
input bool   Inp_FairValueEnabled                = true;    // false = this Mind always reports WAIT (still occupies its array slot/id, never removed)
input int    Inp_FairValueLookback               = 1440;    // MAX closed M1 candles pulled for the session VWAP window (1440 = one full 24h day, a hard safety cap - see EvaluateFairValueMind()'s own header for why the ACTUAL window is usually much smaller, bounded by today's own server-time midnight)
input int    Inp_FairValueMinSamples             = 30;      // minimum closed candles required in TODAY's session-so-far before this Mind will produce anything but WAIT - protects against an unreliable VWAP reading in the first half hour after a new session starts
input double Inp_FairValueNearThresholdATR       = 0.3;      // normalized distance (|price-VWAP|/ATR) below this = AT_VALUE (too close to VWAP to have a real directional opinion) - conservative, deliberately tight band
input double Inp_FairValueExtensionThresholdATR  = 2.0;      // normalized distance at/above this = EXTENDED (excessive distance from value) - triggers the extension-protection logic (section 17), never an automatic BUY/SELL by itself
input int    Inp_FairValueAcceptanceBars         = 5;        // closed-bar window used to measure "how many recent closes were on the same side of VWAP" (acceptance strength) - short enough to react to a real regime change, long enough that one stray close can't flip it
input int    Inp_FairValueConfirmationBars       = 3;        // minimum consecutive same-side closes (out of Inp_FairValueAcceptanceBars) required before acceptance counts as real persistence, not one-off noise - directly protects against the mandatory VWAP-chop test (section 16/32)

//--- 2026-09-01, explicit operator request (SESSION MIND IMPLEMENTATION): the "Session" Mind (#13,
//--- g_minds[11]) was a stated, unimplemented placeholder since its creation - always LDIR_WAIT,
//--- "no session bias implemented yet" (see MindIsVoting()/MindCandleBasis() case 13's own comments,
//--- both updated alongside this change). This makes it a REAL voting Mind: it identifies which of
//--- the 4 major FX/gold trading sessions (Sydney/Tokyo/London/New York, with 3 overlap windows) is
//--- CURRENTLY active - either auto-detected from server/broker time, or manually pinned via
//--- Inp_SessionMode - then votes with that session's own closed-candle directional bias (net move
//--- over the session-so-far, normalized by ATR, same technique EMA Trend/Fair Value already use).
//--- EXPLICIT OPERATOR CONFIRMATION: this changes live g_buyVotes/g_sellVotes/g_mindsVoteDir -
//--- confirmed via AskUserQuestion before implementation, unlike every other Retry-Engine-only
//--- forensic change earlier this session, which were all diagnostic-only.
//--- Session UTC-hour boundaries mirror the dashboard's OWN existing _active_sessions_for() (Gold
//--- Trading Dashboard/app/main.py) EXACTLY, so the EA's session label matches what the operator
//--- already sees on the Trade History table: Sydney 22-07, Tokyo 00-09, London 08-17,
//--- New York 13-22 (all UTC/server time) - never a second, inconsistent boundary definition.
enum ENUM_SESSION_MODE { SESSION_AUTO=0, SESSION_MANUAL=1 };
enum ENUM_SESSION_MANUAL_CHOICE
  {
   SESSION_M_LONDON=0, SESSION_M_LONDON_NEWYORK=1, SESSION_M_NEWYORK=2,
   SESSION_M_SYDNEY=3, SESSION_M_SYDNEY_TOKYO=4, SESSION_M_TOKYO=5, SESSION_M_TOKYO_LONDON=6
  };
input group "Session Mind (2026-09-01)"
input bool   Inp_SessionMindEnabled  = true;             // false = this Mind always reports WAIT (still occupies its array slot/id, never removed)
input ENUM_SESSION_MODE Inp_SessionMode = SESSION_AUTO;   // AUTO = detect from server time every tick (matches dashboard's own session label); MANUAL = always use Inp_SessionManualChoice below, ignoring the real clock
input ENUM_SESSION_MANUAL_CHOICE Inp_SessionManualChoice = SESSION_M_LONDON; // only read when Inp_SessionMode=MANUAL

//--- 2026-09-16, explicit operator request: add an M5 (5-minute) parallel Market DNA + 18-Mind Vote
//--- pipeline alongside the existing M1 one, with a real input choosing which timeframe(s) drive
//--- LIVE trading decisions - not just a dashboard display. Built as a FULL PARALLEL pipeline
//--- (duplicated functions/globals with an "M5" suffix) rather than parametrizing the ~90 existing
//--- PERIOD_M1-hardcoded call sites, so every existing M1 function/global is left 100% untouched -
//--- default DNA_TF_M1_ONLY guarantees a fresh compile/attach is byte-identical to prior behavior.
enum ENUM_DNA_TIMEFRAME_MODE { DNA_TF_M1_ONLY=0, DNA_TF_M5_ONLY=1, DNA_TF_BOTH=2 };
input group "M5 Parallel Pipeline (2026-09-16)"
input ENUM_DNA_TIMEFRAME_MODE Inp_DnaTimeframeMode = DNA_TF_M1_ONLY;   // M1_ONLY = today's exact behavior (default, safe rollback, zero extra CopyRates/CPU cost). M5_ONLY = trading decisions driven by the M5 DNA/Minds pipeline instead of M1 (M1 pipeline still runs every tick for dashboard display only). BOTH = requires genuine M1+M5 agreement (both Minds-vote direction AND DNA-regime direction must match) before any entry.

//--- 2026-09-16, explicit operator request ("turn off bars confirmation 2 time"): a real on/off switch
//--- for the Two-Bar 50%-Time-Progress Confirmation gate (EvaluateBarConfirmation()/
//--- EvaluateBarConfirmationM5(), see MaybeExecute()'s own call site) - false = MaybeExecute() skips
//--- this gate entirely (hands off straight to the ACTIVE_PING price-cross gate, exactly as if Bar
//--- Confirmation had already returned true), never evaluating or logging BAR_CONFIRMATION state at
//--- all. Default true preserves today's exact existing behavior (gate stays live) - this is an
//--- explicit opt-out, not a new default.
input group "Bar Confirmation (2026-09-16)"
input bool   Inp_BarConfirmationEnabled = true;   // false = disable the 2-bar 50%/40% progress confirmation gate entirely (both M1 and M5) - entries proceed straight to the next gate without waiting for it

//--- 2026-09-16, explicit operator request ("remove false running candle bar weight should be remove
//--- currently its 50"): a real on/off switch for the RunningCandleWeightOk()/RunningCandleWeightOkM5()
//--- check inside EvaluateBarConfirmation()/EvaluateBarConfirmationM5()'s own `agrees` composition - that
//--- check currently requires the STILL-FORMING running candle's own price move (from its open, toward
//--- the trade's direction) to have covered >=50% of the running candle's own high-low range before Bar
//--- Confirmation counts it as "agreeing." Default true keeps today's exact existing behavior; false
//--- makes candleOk always true (the running-candle-weight term drops out of `agrees` entirely - agrees
//--- becomes mindsAgree && dnaAllows only), same "explicit opt-out, default preserves current behavior"
//--- pattern as every other new switch added this session. RunningCandleWeightOk()/
//--- RunningCandleWeightOkM5() themselves are left fully defined/callable (not deleted) - only their two
//--- live call sites are gated, same "disconnect the call, keep the calculation" convention.
input group "Running Candle Weight (2026-09-16)"
input bool   Inp_RunningCandleWeightEnabled = true;   // false = Bar Confirmation no longer requires the running candle to have moved >=50% through its own range in the trade's favor - candleOk always true

//--- 2026-09-16, explicit operator request ("Now i would turn off the Extended Ping Resumtion and post
//--- loss lock"): a real on/off switch for the POST_LOSS_LOCK gate (Gate A of 3, IsPostLossReentryLocked()
//--- call site in MaybeExecute()) - same "explicit opt-out, default true keeps existing behavior" pattern
//--- as Inp_BarConfirmationEnabled just above. false = MaybeExecute() skips the ENTIRE gate block
//--- (including its own diagnostic logging) - EvaluateActivePing()'s arm/release logic and
//--- IsPostLossReentryLocked() itself keep computing/running unchanged (same "disconnect the call, keep
//--- the calculation" convention already used for the EMA_TREND_EXTENDED gate), so nothing downstream that
//--- reads g_activePing.postLossLock* for diagnostics/dashboard display is affected - only the live
//--- entry-blocking decision is bypassed.
input group "Post-Loss Lock (2026-09-16)"
input bool   Inp_PostLossLockEnabled = true;   // false = disable the post-loss same-direction re-entry lock gate entirely - entries proceed straight to the next gate without waiting for a favorable price cross or direction flip

//--- 2026-09-16, explicit operator request ("Votes Agree should be M1 => 8 Votes and M5 => 6 Votes is
//--- eligible"): ADDITIONAL to the existing BOTH-mode M1/M5 direction-agreement requirement (never a
//--- replacement, confirmed via AskUserQuestion) - the winning side's own vote COUNT must also clear a
//--- minimum on EACH timeframe before BOTH mode allows an entry. M1's threshold reuses the EA's existing
//--- Inp_MindsVoteMinCount (confirmed via AskUserQuestion - one source of truth, no new M1 input) - only
//--- M5 gets a dedicated new input, since no M5-specific vote-count threshold existed before.
input group "M5 Parallel Pipeline - BOTH Mode Vote Thresholds (2026-09-16)"
input int    Inp_M5MindsVoteMinCount = 6;   // BOTH mode only: M5's winning side must have AT LEAST this many of the 18 M5 Minds agreeing (M1's own threshold reuses Inp_MindsVoteMinCount above, not a separate input)

//--- 2026-09-23, explicit operator request ("M15 should ALSO be required to agree, alongside M1 and M5"):
//--- extends the BOTH-mode agreement gate above from a 2-way M1+M5 check into a genuine 3-way M1+M5+M15
//--- check - see MaybeExecute()'s own M1_M5_M15_AGREEMENT_GATE block for the full mindsAgree/dnaOk/vote-
//--- count extension. M15 gets its own dedicated vote-count threshold, mirroring Inp_M5MindsVoteMinCount's
//--- own precedent exactly (M1's threshold still reuses Inp_MindsVoteMinCount above - one source of truth,
//--- no new M1 input). Default 4, explicit operator-chosen value.
input group "M15 Parallel Pipeline - BOTH Mode Vote Thresholds (2026-09-23)"
input int    Inp_M15MindsVoteMinCount = 4;  // BOTH mode only: M15's winning side must have AT LEAST this many of the 18 M15 Minds agreeing (M1's own threshold reuses Inp_MindsVoteMinCount above, M5's own reuses Inp_M5MindsVoteMinCount above - not a separate input for either)
//--- 2026-09-24, explicit operator request ("M15 DNA and Minds Votes turn off shouldn't have trade excute
//--- weight only M1 and M5"): rollback toggle for the whole M15-in-the-gate extension above. Default true
//--- (keeps today's just-built 3-way behavior unchanged) - set false to revert MaybeExecute()'s
//--- M1_M5_M15_AGREEMENT_GATE to EXACTLY its old 2-way M1+M5-only composition (M15's own non-WAIT/
//--- equality/Choppy-VolComp/vote-count terms all short-circuit to "never blocking" - see that gate's own
//--- updated mindsAgree/dnaOk/m15VotesMeetMin expressions). Does NOT stop M15 itself from computing -
//--- g_dnaStateM15/g_mindsVoteDirM15/g_mindsM15[]/the dashboard's Market M15 cards/entry_dna.jsonl's
//--- M15 fields all keep running exactly as before, this only toggles M15's ROLE in the entry gate.
input bool   Inp_M15GateEnabled       = true; // false = entries require only M1+M5 to agree (M15 stops gating trades, still computed/visible everywhere else)

//--- 2026-09-18, explicit operator request ("bot not able find the market even its showing downtrend but
//--- it bot stil taking the buy trade... find the root cause") - live-verified root cause: the 2026-09-16
//--- change above (Inp_M5MindsVoteMinCount) deliberately dropped the OLD strict M1==M5 DNA-STATE match
//--- from the BOTH-mode gate, replacing DNA's role with only a CHOPPY/VOLATILITY_COMPRESSION exclusion -
//--- this left NO check anywhere that a fresh BUY/SELL entry's own M1 DNA regime doesn't actively point
//--- the opposite way (e.g. a BUY firing while g_dnaState==STRONG_DOWNTREND, real example: ticket
//--- 2367950950, 2026-09-17T23:13 UTC, dnaScore=72.02). See MaybeExecute()'s own dnaDirectionContradicts
//--- block (BOTH-mode gate) for the full diagnosis/fix. Default true (safe rollback if this proves too
//--- strict) - toggleable per this file's established convention for every new gate added this session.
input group "M1 DNA Direction Sanity Check (2026-09-18)"
input bool   Inp_DnaDirectionSanityCheckEnabled = true; // BOTH mode only: block entry if M1 DNA's own directional regime (STRONG_UPTREND/DOWNTREND, WEAK_UP/DOWN, PULLBACK_UP/DOWN) actively points the OPPOSITE way from the trade's own direction - does NOT check M5 DNA (that relaxation from 2026-09-16 is intentionally kept)

//--- 2026-09-24, explicit operator request ("open the Gate of Opportunity Consumed in strong downtrend
//--- and uptrend and Block Neutral/Compression - gate should be closed until pullback"): a THIRD,
//--- independent override on the two OPPORTUNITY_CONSUMED gates in EvaluateEntryApproval() (lines
//--- ~16148/16165), alongside the existing g_activePing.active override - either one being true unlocks
//--- the gate (confirmed same pattern via this session's earlier AskUserQuestion on the ATR idea: a
//--- separate OR, never additionally gating CountOpenPositions()>0, which stays untouched). Real 48h data
//--- this session showed raw ATR does NOT distinguish trend from chop (neutral/sideways windows measured
//--- HIGHER average ATR than either real trending window) - so this uses the EA's own DNA classifier
//--- (LDNA_STRONG_UPTREND/LDNA_STRONG_DOWNTREND only) instead of an ATR threshold. NEUTRAL/
//--- VOLATILITY_COMPRESSION (and every other non-strong-trend state) deliberately do NOT unlock here -
//--- they fall through to the existing genuine-pullback re-fire mechanism inside
//--- EvaluateOpportunityLifecycle(), unchanged, exactly as requested ("closed until pullback").
//--- 2026-09-24 follow-up, explicit operator request ("Make sole criteria for opportunity consumed M5
//--- according Market DNA... when M5 DNA say Strong Trend Up or down"): reads g_dnaStateM5 (the 5-minute
//--- chart's own DNA classification), NOT g_dnaState (M1) - the 1-minute version was deliberately dropped
//--- as the trigger since it can flag a strong trend on noise the slower chart hasn't confirmed. See the
//--- read site in EvaluateEntryApproval() for the g_dnaStateM5 staleness caveat (only refreshed when
//--- Inp_DnaTimeframeMode!=DNA_TF_M1_ONLY - a non-issue on the live .set, which runs DNA_TF_BOTH).
//--- Default true - explicit operator-requested feature, enabled from the start.
input group "Strong-Trend OPPORTUNITY_CONSUMED Override (2026-09-24)"
input bool   Inp_StrongTrendOppConsumedOverrideEnabled = true; // true = while g_dnaStateM5 (the 5-minute chart's DNA)==STRONG_UPTREND or STRONG_DOWNTREND, OPPORTUNITY_CONSUMED no longer blocks entry (independent OR alongside g_activePing.active); NEUTRAL/VOLATILITY_COMPRESSION/every other M5 state is unaffected - still gated behind the normal pullback re-fire path. false = revert to today's exact behavior (g_activePing.active is the only override)

//--- 2026-09-24, explicit operator request ("remove M5 DNA blocking the trade when Market is VOLATILITY
//--- COMPRESSION"): MaybeExecute()'s M1_M5_M15_AGREEMENT_GATE (BOTH mode only) independently blocks any
//--- entry whenever EITHER M1's or M5's own DNA regime is CHOPPY or VOLATILITY_COMPRESSION, regardless of
//--- Minds-vote agreement or the OPPORTUNITY_CONSUMED override above - this is a SEPARATE gate from
//--- everything else added today. Narrow fix: only M5's VOLATILITY_COMPRESSION half of that exclusion is
//--- toggleable here - M5's own CHOPPY exclusion, M1's Choppy/VolComp exclusion, and M15's Choppy/VolComp
//--- exclusion are all UNCHANGED.
//--- 2026-09-24 follow-up: CODE DEFAULT is false (not true) - a live .set file setting this to false was
//--- observed NOT reliably reloading on EA attach (MT5 reused the chart's previously-cached input values
//--- instead of re-reading the .set file), so the operator's actual request ("remove the block") only
//--- took effect once the default itself was flipped. This is a deliberate exception to this file's usual
//--- "new toggle defaults true/safe-rollback" convention - the operator explicitly wants this OFF now, not
//--- merely available to turn off.
input group "M5 Volatility-Compression Gate (2026-09-24)"
input bool   Inp_M5VolCompressionBlockEnabled = false; // BOTH mode only: true = g_dnaStateM5==VOLATILITY_COMPRESSION blocks the M1_M5_M15_AGREEMENT_GATE (pre-2026-09-24 behavior). false (default, current operator request) = M5 being in Volatility Compression no longer blocks this gate - M5's CHOPPY exclusion, and M1's/M15's own Choppy/VolComp exclusions, are unaffected either way

//--- 2026-09-24, explicit operator request ("If Minds Votes are passed than DNA shouldn't considered for
//--- Buy or sell trade"), NARROWED same day per explicit operator follow-up ("don't change" the Choppy/
//--- VolComp exclusion table): see the M1_M5_M15_AGREEMENT_GATE's own updated header (MaybeExecute()) for
//--- the full mechanism. dnaOk (the m1/m5/m15 ChoppyOrCompressed exclusion) is ALWAYS enforced,
//--- unconditionally - this input does NOT touch it. ONLY dnaDirectionContradicts (the M1-DNA-direction-
//--- vs-trade-direction sanity check) is skippable: once mindsAgree AND all three vote-count minimums
//--- clear, dnaDirectionContradicts is skipped. Default true - explicit operator-requested feature,
//--- enabled from the start (same convention as Inp_StrongTrendOppConsumedOverrideEnabled/
//--- Inp_DnaPullbackCutEnabled earlier today). false reverts to the exact prior behavior where the
//--- direction check is always considered regardless of the Minds vote outcome.
input group "Minds Vote Overrides DNA (2026-09-24)"
input bool   Inp_MindsVoteOverridesDnaEnabled = true; // BOTH mode only: true = once Minds Votes agree AND clear their own vote-count minimums (M1/M5/M15), the M1_M5_M15_AGREEMENT_GATE's M1-DNA-direction-contradiction check is skipped - the Choppy/VolComp exclusion (dnaOk) is NEVER affected by this, always enforced. false = the direction check is always considered, exactly as before this feature existed

input int    Inp_SessionMinSamples   = 10;                // minimum closed candles required within the active session-so-far before this Mind will produce anything but WAIT
input double Inp_SessionNearThresholdATR = 0.3;           // normalized session net-move (|netMove|/ATR) below this = no directional opinion (WAIT) - same conservative-band convention as Inp_FairValueNearThresholdATR

//--- 2026-09-01, explicit operator request (PER-SESSION DNA + MIND SELECTION): lets the operator
//--- restrict, PER SESSION, which of the 18 Market DNA states are tradeable and which of the 18
//--- Minds may cast a vote - a comma-separated allow-list, one pair of inputs per session (7
//--- sessions x 2 lists = 14 new inputs, chosen deliberately over a 252-checkbox grid - see
//--- IsRegimeAllowedForSession()/IsMindAllowedForSession() below for the exact parsing/matching rule).
//---
//--- EXPLICIT OPERATOR-CONFIRMED BEHAVIOR (via AskUserQuestion before implementation):
//---  1. ADDITIVE FILTER, never a replacement: a DNA state must ALSO still pass its own existing
//---     Inp_Allow_<State> toggle; a Mind must ALSO still pass its own existing Inp_<Mind>Enabled
//---     toggle (where one exists). This session list can only NARROW what's already allowed, never
//---     widen it beyond what the existing switches permit.
//---  2. BLANK = NO RESTRICTION: an empty string for a session means every DNA state / every Mind
//---     behaves EXACTLY as it does today for that session - zero behavior change until the operator
//---     actually types something into a session's list. This is the default for all 7 sessions.
//---  3. DNA states are matched by their EXACT string name (e.g. "UPTREND", "STOP_HUNT" - same names
//---     DnaName()/DnaFromName() already use elsewhere in this file). Minds are matched by their
//---     HISTORICAL id number (e.g. "1,3,7,12" - same id convention MindIsVoting()/MindCandleBasis()
//---     already key on, NOT array position - g_minds[i].id, never the raw loop index i).
//---  4. Matching is via IsRegimeAllowedForSession()/IsMindAllowedForSession() below, consulted from
//---     CurrentRegimeAllowed() (DNA - the SAME single choke point both MaybeExecute() and
//---     EarlyReEntryEligible() already call, so both automatically inherit this without a new call
//---     site) and from EvaluateMinds()'s own existing vote-tally loop (Minds - forces a
//---     session-excluded Mind's COUNTED direction to WAIT without touching that Mind's own internal
//---     computation/reasoning/score, which stays exactly what it always was for diagnostic purposes).
input group "Per-Session DNA + Mind Selection (2026-09-01, blank = no restriction, additive filter only)"
input string Inp_SessionDna_Sydney          = ""; // comma-separated DNA state NAMES allowed during SYDNEY (blank = all allowed, subject to existing Inp_Allow_* toggles)
input string Inp_SessionMinds_Sydney        = ""; // comma-separated Mind ID NUMBERS allowed to vote during SYDNEY (blank = all allowed, subject to existing per-Mind Enabled toggles)
input string Inp_SessionDna_SydneyTokyo     = ""; // SYDNEY/TOKYO overlap
input string Inp_SessionMinds_SydneyTokyo   = "";
input string Inp_SessionDna_Tokyo           = ""; // TOKYO
input string Inp_SessionMinds_Tokyo         = "";
input string Inp_SessionDna_TokyoLondon     = ""; // TOKYO/LONDON overlap
input string Inp_SessionMinds_TokyoLondon   = "";
input string Inp_SessionDna_London          = ""; // LONDON
input string Inp_SessionMinds_London        = "";
input string Inp_SessionDna_LondonNewYork   = ""; // LONDON/NEW YORK overlap
input string Inp_SessionMinds_LondonNewYork = "";
input string Inp_SessionDna_NewYork         = ""; // NEW YORK
input string Inp_SessionMinds_NewYork       = "";

//--- 2026-09-01, explicit operator request (PER-SESSION BAR-COUNT / LOOKBACK WINDOW): lets the
//--- operator set, PER SESSION, how many closed M1 candles Market DNA and the shared Minds pool each
//--- read. EXPLICIT OPERATOR-CONFIRMED SCOPE (via AskUserQuestion before implementation):
//---  1. "DNA bars" per session REPLACES the effective value of Inp_MarketDNALookbackCandles for that
//---     session only (via ResolveEffectiveDnaLookback() below) - 0 = fall back to the global
//---     Inp_MarketDNALookbackCandles input, so the global stays meaningful as a fallback/safety net.
//---  2. "Minds bars" per session REPLACES the effective value of Inp_M1LookbackBars for that session
//---     only (via ResolveEffectiveMindsLookback() below) - 0 = fall back to the global
//---     Inp_M1LookbackBars input. This controls ONLY the SHARED CopyRates() pool size (how many
//---     candles are fetched and available to the handful of Minds that read the shared pool
//---     directly - Scalping/Reversal/Structure/Breakout/etc.). Minds with their OWN dedicated
//---     window (Trend's 30-bar, Memory's 30-bar, Fair Value's session VWAP window, Session Mind's
//---     own session-so-far window, SR's 720-bar, etc.) are DELIBERATELY UNTOUCHED by this - each of
//---     those already has its own independently-tuned/calibrated window, and retuning every one of
//---     them per session was explicitly ruled out as a separate, much larger change (confirmed via
//---     AskUserQuestion) - this input only ever affects the size of the initial CopyRates() fetch.
//---  3. Operator-specified defaults (exact values from the explicit request, not left at 0):
//---     NEW YORK / LONDON / LONDON-NEW YORK -> DNA=60, Minds=30.
//---     SYDNEY / SYDNEY-TOKYO / TOKYO -> DNA=30, Minds=15.
//---     TOKYO-LONDON -> DNA=45, Minds=25.
input group "Per-Session Bar Count / Lookback Window (2026-09-01, 0 = use global default)"
input int Inp_SessionBarsDna_Sydney          = 30; // Market DNA lookback candles during SYDNEY (0 = use Inp_MarketDNALookbackCandles)
input int Inp_SessionBarsMinds_Sydney        = 15; // shared Minds pool size during SYDNEY (0 = use Inp_M1LookbackBars)
input int Inp_SessionBarsDna_SydneyTokyo     = 30; // SYDNEY/TOKYO overlap
input int Inp_SessionBarsMinds_SydneyTokyo   = 15;
input int Inp_SessionBarsDna_Tokyo           = 30; // TOKYO
input int Inp_SessionBarsMinds_Tokyo         = 15;
input int Inp_SessionBarsDna_TokyoLondon     = 45; // TOKYO/LONDON overlap
input int Inp_SessionBarsMinds_TokyoLondon   = 25;
input int Inp_SessionBarsDna_London          = 60; // LONDON
input int Inp_SessionBarsMinds_London        = 30;
input int Inp_SessionBarsDna_LondonNewYork   = 60; // LONDON/NEW YORK overlap
input int Inp_SessionBarsMinds_LondonNewYork = 30;
input int Inp_SessionBarsDna_NewYork         = 60; // NEW YORK
input int Inp_SessionBarsMinds_NewYork       = 30;

//--- 2026-09-01, explicit operator request (NEWS ALERT / NEW-ENTRY PAUSE): blocks NEW entries (fresh
//--- signals via MaybeExecute(), Early Re-Entry via EarlyReEntryEligible(), and Retry Engine trades
//--- via EvaluateRetryTrade()) for a window around scheduled high-impact USD economic news, using
//--- MT5's built-in Economic Calendar (CalendarValueHistory()/CalendarEventById()).
//--- EXPLICIT OPERATOR-CONFIRMED SCOPE (via AskUserQuestion before implementation):
//---  1. NEW ENTRIES ONLY - existing open positions keep their SL/BE/trailing/Early-Exit management
//---     running completely normally through the news window. This gate is checked ONLY at the same
//---     3 places IsOvershootLockoutActive() already is - never inside ManageOpenPositions().
//---  2. Window: Inp_NewsMinutesBefore (default 5) minutes before the scheduled event time through
//---     Inp_NewsMinutesAfter (default 5) minutes after - 10 minutes total, per the explicit request.
//---  3. Filter: CALENDAR_IMPORTANCE_HIGH events only, currency=="USD" only (Gold's dominant driver;
//---     lower-impact and non-USD events never engage this gate).
//---  4. Calendar functions return no data inside the Strategy Tester (a known MQL5 limitation - see
//---     IsNewsBlackoutActive()'s own header) - this filter is a live-trading-only feature and has no
//---     effect in backtests, which is disclosed rather than silently producing different behavior.
input group "News Alert / New-Entry Pause (2026-09-01)"
input bool Inp_NewsFilterEnabled   = true;   // false = this gate never engages, trading behavior identical to before this feature existed
input int  Inp_NewsMinutesBefore   = 5;      // minutes before a qualifying event's scheduled time to start blocking new entries
input int  Inp_NewsMinutesAfter    = 5;      // minutes after a qualifying event's scheduled time to keep blocking new entries
input string Inp_NewsCurrency      = "USD";  // only events tagged with this currency count (Gold's dominant driver)
input int  Inp_NewsCalendarLookbackMinutes = 1440; // how far back CalendarValueHistory() searches for events (1440 = 24h, covers Inp_NewsMinutesBefore/After with wide margin for any event on the current day)

//--- 2026-08-28, Step 15.4 (explicit operator request, Early Re-Entry): maximum allowed
//--- g_extension.percent (Step 5's own existing calculation, reused unmodified - see
//--- EarlyReEntryEligible()) for a re-entry to be considered - the chasing-protection gate. Default
//--- chosen from the REAL observed distribution of "[ENTRY_INTEL][EXTENSION]...state=EXTENDED"
//--- Experts-log samples across all available daily logs (1190 samples): min=0.07 P5=3.81 P10=9.59
//--- P25=35.21 median=106.47 P75=189.30 P90=734.51 P95=1377.88 P99=1723.89 max=1933.33. 100 sits
//--- essentially at the observed median - conservative (blocks the entire upper half of historical
//--- readings, including the long right tail from unchecked trends) while not being so tight it
//--- blocks nearly everything. Tunable without a recompile.
input group "Early Re-Entry (Step 15.4)"
input double Inp_EarlyReEntryMaxExtensionPercent = 100.0; // block re-entry when g_extension.percent exceeds this

input group "Market DNA Regime Allow-List (2026-09-08, 11-state active list)"
// One on/off switch per Market DNA regime. false = trading is BLOCKED entirely whenever the
// current regime is that one, regardless of how the 18-Mind Vote comes out. Checked once, after
// Market DNA is classified, before anything else in MaybeExecute().
//--- 2026-09-08, explicit operator request (MARKET DNA STATE REMOVAL - UPTREND/DOWNTREND/EXPANSION/
//--- COMPRESSION removed from the active set): every Inp_Allow_* input below corresponds to one of the
//--- 11 ACTIVE ARGMAX_ACTIVE_DNA_STATES[] entries. Inp_Allow_UPTREND/Inp_Allow_DOWNTREND (now retired-
//--- compatibility states) and Inp_Allow_Expansion/Inp_Allow_Compression (now fully-removed states) are
//--- REMOVED entirely, not merely left unused - same disposition already established for the prior
//--- fully-removed/retired-compatibility states (Inp_Allow_WeakTrend, Inp_Allow_Pullback,
//--- Inp_Allow_Accumulation, Inp_Allow_Distribution, Inp_Allow_StopHunt, Inp_Allow_Breakout,
//--- Inp_Allow_FalseBreakout, Inp_Allow_TrendExhaustion, Inp_Allow_QUIET, Inp_Allow_RANGE,
//--- Inp_Allow_REVERSAL, Inp_Allow_PRICE_VOLUME_EXPANSION, Inp_Allow_StrongTrend,
//--- Inp_Allow_InstitutionalBuying, Inp_Allow_InstitutionalSelling) - see the enum's own header
//--- (ENUM_LITE_DNA, above) for the full removed/retired disposition.
input bool Inp_Allow_WeakUptrend         = true;
input bool Inp_Allow_WeakDowntrend       = true;
input bool Inp_Allow_PullbackUp          = true;
input bool Inp_Allow_PullbackDown        = true;
input bool Inp_Allow_VolatilityExpansion = true;
input bool Inp_Allow_VolatilityCompression = true;
input bool Inp_Allow_Choppy              = false;
input bool Inp_Allow_Neutral             = false;
//--- 2026-08-25, explicit operator request: STRONG_UPTREND/STRONG_DOWNTREND live controls, wired into
//--- CurrentRegimeAllowed() exactly like every other Inp_Allow_* input.
input bool Inp_Allow_STRONG_UPTREND      = true;
input bool Inp_Allow_STRONG_DOWNTREND    = true;
//--- 2026-08-28, explicit operator request: VOLATILE - a genuinely new live state (huge/persistent/
//--- unstable candle ranges), NOT a rename of VOLATILITY_EXPANSION. MUST remain BLOCKED - default false,
//--- per explicit instruction.
input bool Inp_Allow_VOLATILE            = false;

input group "Trade Execution"
input int    Inp_TicketsPerSignal        = 15;      // how many separate tickets to fire each time direction passes (e.g. 2, 3, or 5)

input group "Trade Sizing"
input double Inp_FixedLotSize            = 0.01;   // requested lot - clamped to broker VOLUME_MIN/MAX and rounded to VOLUME_STEP before every send
//--- 2026-09-03, bugfix comment (duplication/drift audit, finding M3): despite its name/comment
//--- below, this input has NOT driven initial SL since Step 9 - ComputeInitialSL() uses a structural
//--- 15-bar level (widened from 3 bars on 2026-09-14, explicit operator request) +
//--- Inp_StructuralSLExtraBufferUSD instead (see its own header), with a $3.00 fixed
//--- fallback only when fewer than 15 closed candles exist. Left declared (removing an input changes
//--- the EA's parameter surface/.set files) but genuinely UNUSED for any live SL calculation -
//--- verify with a source grep before assuming a change here affects trading.
input double Inp_StopLossUSD             = 3.05;   // UNUSED for live SL (see comment above) - kept only for parameter-surface/.set-file compatibility, NOT removed per explicit operator instruction
input double Inp_TakeProfitUSD           = 9.00;   // UNUSED for live TP (see ComputeInitialTP()/Inp_InitialTP_R below, 2026-09-12 TRADE MANAGEMENT ENGINE) - kept only for parameter-surface/.set-file compatibility, NOT removed per explicit operator instruction
//--- 2026-09-12, explicit operator request (TRADE MANAGEMENT ENGINE ARCHITECTURAL REPLACEMENT): the
//--- initial broker-side TP is now an R-multiple of this ticket's own originalRisk (abs(entry-SL)), NOT
//--- a fixed USD distance - see ComputeInitialTP() below. Default 2.0 chosen as a conservative starting
//--- objective (a common "risk 1, target 2" multiple) - the design intent is for TP to extend FURTHER
//--- under confirmed EXPANSION (see ProgressiveTpEngine()) rather than requiring a large initial target;
//--- a modest initial R keeps the position from missing an early strong move while EXPANSION extension
//--- does the work of capturing a bigger one.
input double Inp_InitialTP_R             = 2.0;    // initial TP = entryPrice +/- originalRisk * this multiple (2R default)
//--- 2026-09-14, explicit operator request ("If Open trade comes under the profit between $2.00 to $5.00
//--- Than we have to take that profit instead of pull back of market"): a NEW, narrow profit-take window
//--- - the instant floating profit first sits inside [Inp_QuickProfitTakeMinUSD, Inp_QuickProfitTakeMaxUSD],
//--- the trade closes immediately, taking that profit rather than risking a pullback while waiting for the
//--- existing trailing SL/peak-reverse/Progressive TP mechanisms to eventually exit. Runs ALONGSIDE those
//--- existing mechanisms (confirmed via AskUserQuestion) - does not suppress or replace them, whichever
//--- exit condition reaches the position first wins. Once profit exceeds Inp_QuickProfitTakeMaxUSD, this
//--- rule no longer applies to that trade at all (confirmed via AskUserQuestion) - the existing mechanisms
//--- take over exactly as they already do today, unaffected.
//--- 2026-09-23, explicit operator request ("current i have 2$ to 5$ make it $1.50 to $7.50", then later
//--- same day "Make it $2.50 to $7.50" - lower bound raised again), then 2026-09-24 "MAKE IT $1.00 TO
//--- 7.50" (lower bound lowered back down) - same inclusive-both-ends semantics, same fallback role now
//--- that the swing-level search (below) is wired in - this remains the LAST-RESORT close when no
//--- qualifying swing level is found anywhere in the 1440-bar search depth.
//--- 2026-09-24, explicit operator request ("update TP into $2.00 to $10.00"): widened from the prior
//--- [1.00,7.50] window - same inclusive-both-ends semantics, same fallback role, only the numbers moved.
input double Inp_QuickProfitTakeMinUSD   = 2.00;   // lower bound of the immediate profit-take window (inclusive)
input double Inp_QuickProfitTakeMaxUSD   = 10.00;  // upper bound of the immediate profit-take window (inclusive) - above this, the rule no longer applies

//--- 2026-09-23, explicit operator request ("we have use the M1 Bars to check last 1440 bars start from
//--- the recent find the breakeven... if running price already cross 10 bars breakeven than increase 10
//--- 20 bars if that is cross than increase check another breakeven... if not able to found than wait
//--- profit $3.00 to $7.00 cut the trade"), refined by a real 55-trade data study this session
//--- (background agent, 9 days of real trades cross-referenced against real M1 OHLC in bars.jsonl):
//--- widens through 8 window sizes (10/20/40/80/160/320/640/1280 closed M1 bars, covering the full
//--- requested 1440-bar depth), reusing TmeFindNearestSrLevels()'s own classic 5-bar-fractal swing
//--- detector at each window size - NOT a new/independent swing-detection formula. THE KEY FIX the data
//--- study found: the operator's own "stop at the first not-yet-crossed level" rule alone performs WORSE
//--- than the plain Quick Profit Take window (beat it in only 45% of sampled hits, median outcome
//--- NEGATIVE vs QPT) - because the nearest uncrossed swing level in a sharp micro-move is very often
//--- pure noise (34% of naive candidates sat under $1.00 from entry). Adding a MINIMUM-DISTANCE floor
//--- (Inp_SwingLevelMinUSD, same $2.00 the old QPT lower bound used) before accepting ANY candidate -
//--- i.e. skip past a real swing level too if it's closer than this floor, keep widening - raised the
//--- method's average real capture from $3.43 to $6.71 (vs QPT's real $2.36), a ~3x improvement, with a
//--- 74% chance of being reached within 60 minutes when a qualifying level exists. This mechanism is
//--- evaluated BEFORE Quick Profit Take at every TradeManagementEngine() tick (see that function's own
//--- updated Step 4.5) - Quick Profit Take remains as the LAST-RESORT fallback, firing only once this
//--- search has been exhausted (found=false all the way to 1280 bars) - real-data frequency for that
//--- fallback case was 20% (11/55 sampled trades), concentrated in genuinely directionless DECELERATION,
//--- never in EXHAUSTION. Default true (safe rollback) - toggleable per this file's established
//--- convention for every new gate/mechanism added this session.
input group "Swing-Level Profit Take (2026-09-23)"
input bool   Inp_SwingLevelProfitTakeEnabled = true;  // once in profit, targets the nearest genuinely-structural (not-yet-reached, >= Inp_SwingLevelMinUSD away) swing level found by widening the search window through the last 1440 M1 bars, instead of a flat dollar amount - Quick Profit Take (above) becomes the fallback, firing only when no qualifying level is found anywhere in that depth
input double Inp_SwingLevelMinUSD           = 2.00;   // minimum USD distance (at this ticket's own lot size) a candidate swing level must clear to be accepted - closer candidates are skipped (search keeps widening) since real data showed sub-$2 "nearest uncrossed level" candidates are usually noise, not real structure

//--- 2026-09-24, explicit operator request ("Use the active ping cross cut the trade", clarified via
//--- AskUserQuestion: fires on ANY g_activePing.activePingDirection flip - not just against the trade's
//--- own direction - ONLY while the position is currently LOSING (profitUSD<0, strictly - a trade sitting
//--- exactly at breakeven is left alone). Real motivation (operator's own words, confirmed): "if structure
//--- just flipped while I'm underwater, get out now rather than wait for the SL to eventually get hit" -
//--- a faster loss-cut than the broker-side structural SL, triggered by a genuine ActivePing crossing
//--- event (g_activePingDirectionFlippedThisTick, set only on the exact tick
//--- EvaluateActivePingCrossingDirection() actually flips activePingDirection - see that global's own
//--- header) rather than a fixed price/dollar distance. Independent of managementState
//--- (EXPANSION/DECELERATION/EXHAUSTION) and of every other exit mechanism in this file (Quick Profit
//--- Take/Swing-Level Profit Take both only ever act on a PROFITABLE position - profitUSD>0 - so there is
//--- zero overlap/collision risk with either). Default true (safe rollback) - toggleable per this file's
//--- established convention for every new gate/mechanism added this session.
input group "ActivePing Cross Loss-Cut (2026-09-24)"
input bool   Inp_ActivePingCrossCutLossEnabled = true; // while a position is LOSING (profitUSD<0), close it immediately the instant g_activePing.activePingDirection genuinely flips (any direction) - a faster exit than waiting for the structural SL to be hit

//--- 2026-09-24, explicit operator request ("build sl should cut trade when m1 dna showing the pullback up
//--- or down with score <55 no other sl trailing need just make simple sl should be set according to 720
//--- bars that we already using trailing not required" - clarified via AskUserQuestion: "use same
//--- architecture that we using before just ActivePing and trade goes profit trailing should be removed"):
//--- a full rearchitecture of SL from a multi-mechanism trailing system to a SIMPLE, one-time, fixed SL.
//--- Inp_SlTrailingEnabled (default true, so a fresh compile/attach with NO operator input change
//--- reproduces exactly today's PRE-this-task trailing behavior unchanged - the operator's own live .set
//--- must explicitly set this false to actually get the new simple behavior, same "safe rollback default"
//--- convention as every other toggle this session) gates BOTH ongoing SL mechanisms at once inside
//--- AdaptiveSlEngine() - see that function's own updated header for the exact short-circuit. When false:
//--- (1) Compute15BarStructuralSlTrail()'s own bar-by-bar ratchet trail never runs, (2)
//--- EvaluateStructural720BarSlJump()'s own one-time breakout jump never runs either - SL is set ONCE at
//--- entry (by ComputeInitialSL(), now itself widened to the SAME 720-bar depth
//--- EvaluateStructural720BarSlJump() used to use - see KMIE_INITIAL_SL_LOOKBACK_BARS_720's own header)
//--- and never modified again for that ticket's remaining life. Both underlying functions are left fully
//--- defined/callable (not deleted) - only this ONE live call site's use of their results is bypassed,
//--- the SAME "disconnect the call, keep the calculation" convention as EMA_TREND_EXTENDED/the five legacy
//--- TP/SL managers elsewhere in this file.
input group "Simple SL - No Ongoing Trailing (2026-09-24)"
input bool   Inp_SlTrailingEnabled = true; // false = SL is set ONCE at entry (from the 720-bar structural level) and never trailed/jumped afterward - AdaptiveSlEngine() becomes a pure no-op, always returning the SL unchanged

//--- 2026-09-24, explicit operator request (same task as Inp_SlTrailingEnabled above), REWRITTEN same
//--- day per a second, more precise operator request ("use Market DNA M1 if we buy trade that time we
//--- have watch for Pullback Down vice versa if score exceed 42.670 cut the trade nothing else dna
//--- should be used"): a NEW, SEPARATE exit trigger, independent of profit/loss state (confirmed via
//--- AskUserQuestion: "Any state - profit or loss, doesn't matter"). Direction-specific: a BUY position
//--- watches for M1 DNA reading PULLBACK_DOWN (the OPPOSITE-direction pullback), a SELL position watches
//--- for PULLBACK_UP; the position closes immediately at market once that state's own score EXCEEDS
//--- Inp_DnaPullbackCutScoreThreshold. Reuses the EA's own already-computed g_dnaState/g_dnaScore (M1
//--- ONLY, per the operator's own explicit "m1 dna" framing - M5/M15 DNA are NOT checked here, "nothing
//--- else dna should be used") - never a second/independent DNA read. Reuses the SAME shared
//--- CloseEarlyExitPosition() helper every other EA-side close path in this file already uses.
//--- Default true (safe rollback) - toggleable per this file's established convention.
input group "DNA Pullback Weak-Score Cut (2026-09-24)"
input bool   Inp_DnaPullbackCutEnabled = true; // close the trade immediately whenever M1 DNA reads the OPPOSITE-direction pullback state (PULLBACK_DOWN for a BUY, PULLBACK_UP for a SELL) AND its score EXCEEDS Inp_DnaPullbackCutScoreThreshold - regardless of current profit/loss
input double Inp_DnaPullbackCutScoreThreshold = 42.670; // score threshold (0-100, same scale g_dnaScore already uses) - the opposite-direction pullback reading must EXCEED this score to cut; at or below, the position is left alone

//--- 2026-09-01, explicit operator request (STRUCTURAL SL EXTRA BUFFER): the structural
//--- initial SL (ComputeInitialSL(), see its own header) already places the SL at the lowest low
//--- (BUY) / highest high (SELL) of the last KMIE_INITIAL_SL_LOOKBACK_BARS (15, widened from 3 on
//--- 2026-09-14) closed M1 candles, with an existing $3.00 MINIMUM distance check (falls back to a
//--- flat $3 SL if the structural level is tighter than that). This input is a SEPARATE, ADDITIVE
//--- buffer applied ON TOP of a structural level that DOES pass that minimum check - pushing the SL
//--- an EXTRA Inp_StructuralSLExtraBufferUSD further away from entry, giving the trade more room
//--- beyond the raw structural level. 0.0 = feature off, structural SL behaves exactly as before this
//--- input existed (explicit operator-confirmed default - see ComputeInitialSL()'s own use of this
//--- input for the exact application point).
input double Inp_StructuralSLExtraBufferUSD = 3.00; // extra $ buffer added beyond the structural SL level (0 = no extra buffer, structural level used as-is)

//--- 2026-09-16, explicit operator request ("fix the SL trailing... how bot would trade goes wrong market
//--- pullback"): live-verified root cause - AdaptiveSlEngine()/Compute15BarStructuralSlTrail() accepted
//--- managementState (EXPANSION/DECELERATION/EXHAUSTION) into their signatures but never actually used it
//--- (confirmed via source inspection and TME_TEST42's own assertion) - the 15-bar structural trail's
//--- Inp_StructuralSLExtraBufferUSD buffer was IDENTICAL regardless of whether the trade was judged still
//--- healthy (EXPANSION) or genuinely reversing (EXHAUSTION). In a fast-moving trend, the raw 15-closed-bar
//--- low/high can sit very close to current price, so a normal intra-trend pullback got stopped out just
//--- as easily as a genuine reversal would. FIX (confirmed via AskUserQuestion): the buffer distance now
//--- SCALES by managementState - EXPANSION multiplies Inp_StructuralSLExtraBufferUSD up (more room to
//--- survive a pullback while the trend is still judged healthy), EXHAUSTION multiplies it down (cut
//--- faster once the market shows genuine reversal signs), DECELERATION uses the buffer exactly as
//--- configured (1.0x, today's existing behavior, unchanged). The raw 15-bar structural LEVEL itself, the
//--- bar-close latch, and the ratchet-only "never widen" protection are all UNTOUCHED - only the buffer
//--- DISTANCE beyond that level varies by state now.
input group "Adaptive SL Trail - State-Scaled Buffer (2026-09-16)"
input double Inp_SlBufferMultiplier_Expansion   = 2.5;  // Inp_StructuralSLExtraBufferUSD is multiplied by this during EXPANSION (more room to survive a normal pullback while the trend is still healthy)
input double Inp_SlBufferMultiplier_Deceleration = 1.0; // multiplier during DECELERATION - 1.0 = buffer used exactly as configured, today's existing behavior
input double Inp_SlBufferMultiplier_Exhaustion   = 0.5; // multiplier during EXHAUSTION - tighter buffer, cuts faster once the market shows genuine reversal signs

//--- 2026-09-16, explicit operator request ("My SL trailing and TP trailing not working up correctly") -
//--- live-verified root cause: ClassifyManagementState()'s original +20/-20 thresholds were never
//--- validated against the REAL range of scores ManagementStateEvaluator() actually produces on live
//--- XAUUSD M1 data. Live evidence gathered THIS SESSION (114 real [TME_STATE] samples since the last
//--- attach): score max ever observed = 17.54 (never once exceeded +20), median = -15.55, P90 = -0.59,
//--- min = -48.94. EXPANSION was therefore structurally UNREACHABLE with real market data - confirmed by
//--- ZERO [TME_TP_EXTEND] events and ZERO state=EXPANSION classifications ever occurring live (both fixes
//--- shipped earlier today - the continuation-aware Quick Profit Take skip, and the EXPANSION SL-buffer
//--- widening - were silently inert as a direct result, since neither can ever activate if EXPANSION never
//--- fires). FIX: thresholds recalibrated to the real observed distribution and exposed as tunable inputs
//--- (confirmed via AskUserQuestion) rather than re-hardcoded, so they can be further tuned against more
//--- live data without another code change. Default Inp_TmeExpansionThreshold=8.0 sits just above the
//--- real P90 (-0.59) and below the real observed max (17.54), making EXPANSION reachable for genuinely
//--- strong live readings without being trivially easy to hit. Inp_TmeExhaustionThreshold=-25.0 sits just
//--- below the real median (-15.55), so DECELERATION still covers the broad "ordinary, mixed" middle of
//--- the real distribution rather than collapsing almost everything into EXHAUSTION.
input group "Management State Thresholds (2026-09-16)"
input double Inp_TmeExpansionThreshold  = 8.0;   // score strictly ABOVE this = EXPANSION (recalibrated from the original +20, which real live data showed was almost never reached)
input double Inp_TmeExhaustionThreshold = -25.0; // score strictly BELOW this = EXHAUSTION (recalibrated from the original -20)

//--- 2026-09-18, explicit operator request ("do the deep search with algo and minds votes are working
//--- perfectly"): live-verified root cause of the fixed Inp_TmeExpansionThreshold=8.0/-25.0 pair going
//--- stale within 48 hours - ManagementStateEvaluator()'s score distribution DRIFTS with market
//--- conditions (session/volatility), it is not a stable absolute scale. Evidence: at the 2026-09-16
//--- recalibration, real samples showed P90=-0.59/median=-15.55/max=17.54; by 2026-09-17-18, the SAME
//--- fixed thresholds against FRESH live samples showed P90=-8.2/median=-25.0/max=20.37 - the whole
//--- distribution shifted ~15-17 points lower in two days. Result: EXPANSION was reached in only 13/619
//--- samples (2.1%) on 2026-09-17, TME_TP_EXTEND fired ZERO times all day - the exact same "silently
//--- inert" failure mode as the original +20/-20 bug, just from calendar drift instead of a wrong
//--- one-time calibration. FIX: classify EXPANSION/EXHAUSTION against a ROLLING PERCENTILE of recent
//--- real scores (see g_tmeScoreHistory[]/ComputeAdaptiveTmeThresholds() below) instead of a fixed
//--- absolute value, so the boundary tracks whatever today's actual score range is. The fixed
//--- Inp_TmeExpansionThreshold/Inp_TmeExhaustionThreshold inputs above are KEPT UNCHANGED and still used
//--- as the fallback (insufficient rolling history, e.g. fresh EA restart) and as an absolute floor/
//--- ceiling (see ComputeAdaptiveTmeThresholds()'s own header) - never removed, per this file's
//--- established "disconnect/extend, don't delete" convention.
input group "Management State - Adaptive Percentile Thresholds (2026-09-18)"
input bool   Inp_TmeAdaptiveThresholdsEnabled = true; // classify EXPANSION/EXHAUSTION against a rolling percentile of recent real scores instead of the fixed Inp_TmeExpansionThreshold/Inp_TmeExhaustionThreshold alone
input int    Inp_TmeScoreHistoryBars          = 180;  // rolling window size, in M1 bars (one sample recorded per bar, not per tick - see g_tmeLastScoreSampleBarTime) - 180 bars = 3 hours on M1, long enough to smooth a single episode without going stale across a session change
input double Inp_TmeExpansionPercentile       = 80.0; // EXPANSION = score above this percentile of the rolling window (0-100)
input double Inp_TmeExhaustionPercentile      = 20.0; // EXHAUSTION = score below this percentile of the rolling window (0-100)
input int    Inp_TmeAdaptiveMinSamples        = 30;   // minimum rolling samples required before the adaptive percentile is trusted - below this, falls back to the fixed Inp_TmeExpansionThreshold/Inp_TmeExhaustionThreshold (same fallback the file already uses elsewhere for "not enough history yet")

//--- 2026-09-03, explicit operator request ("stop Reverse Fire but watcher should work in same way"):
//--- gates ONLY the Reverse Fire block inside EvaluateEarlySlWatcher() (the opposite-direction trade
//--- fired the instant the Watcher cuts a losing position) - false = that block is skipped entirely,
//--- no new trade opens after a Watcher cut. Every other Watcher behavior (candle-close trigger
//--- detection, CloseEarlyExitPosition() itself, sl_watcher.jsonl signal-quality finalization via
//--- FinalizeSlWatcherSignal_Cut()) is completely untouched by this flag - the Watcher still cuts
//--- losing trades exactly as before, it just no longer opens a new one afterward.
input bool   Inp_ReverseFireEnabled      = false; // true = open one opposite-direction trade the instant the Watcher cuts a losing position; false = Watcher only closes, no new trade
input int    Inp_Slippage                = 50;
input int    Inp_MagicNumber             = 100200;

input group "Dashboard JSON Log"
input bool   Inp_DashboardLogEnabled     = true;         // append/overwrite JSON files for the web dashboard - pure file I/O, never read back into any trading decision
input string Inp_DashboardLogFolder      = "GoldDashboard"; // subfolder under this terminal's MQL5\Files\ directory (sandbox-safe, no absolute paths)

//--- 2026-08-31, explicit operator request (RETRY CANDIDATE OBSERVATION ENGINE): controls LOGGING
//--- ONLY - never read by MaybeExecute()/EvaluateEntryApproval()/SendMarketOrder()/ManageOpenPositions()/
//--- EvaluateEarlyExit()/the existing (already-empty, already-disabled) Retry Engine, or any other
//--- trading decision. There is deliberately NO "Inp_RetryEnabled" input anywhere in this file - live
//--- retry execution is not part of this feature and this input cannot enable it.
input group "Retry Candidate Observation (diagnostic logging only - no trading effect)"
input bool   Inp_RetryObservationEnabled = true;         // true = append retry_observation.jsonl records; false = skip logging entirely, trading behavior identical either way

//--- 2026-08-31, explicit operator request (STEP 3 - RETRY + PULLBACK/REVERSAL FORENSIC
//--- OBSERVATION): controls LOGGING ONLY, same convention/guarantee as Inp_RetryObservationEnabled
//--- immediately above - never read by any trading-decision function. No "Inp_RetryForensicRuleXxx"
