//====================================================================
// ACTIVE_PING (2026-09-03, explicit operator request - replaces the OPPORTUNITY_CONSUMED re-entry
// gate, NOT the Active Leg/Pullback/Resumption/Continuation opportunity-existence system, which stays
// completely untouched). Per explicit instruction: "Make the EA EMA20/EMA50 implementation the
// canonical trading source of truth... ACTIVE_PING must directly consume the existing EA EMA20/EMA50
// calculation and existing EMA Trend Mind slope logic... Do not create a second EMA formula. Do not
// alter EMA Trend Mind mathematics."
//
// This function is a SEPARATE, independent read of the SAME EmaAt() helper EvaluateEmaTrendMind()
// uses, with the SAME periods/slopeLookback/gap-ATR formula copied verbatim - deliberately NOT
// refactored into a shared sub-function called by both, so EvaluateEmaTrendMind()'s own existing
// behavior is provably unchanged (zero risk of a refactor altering live Mind-vote math). This mirrors
// the established precedent in this file for "read-only reuse without touching the original" (e.g.
// ComputePriceRangeDnaLive() alongside ComputePriceRangeDna()).
//
// EMA20_EMA50_CORRIDOR_ACTIVE: the reference closed candle's own close sits between EMA20 and EMA50 -
// this is the EXACT condition the dashboard's renderEmaBand() highlight visualizes (see that
// function's own header in index.html - it draws a filled band between the ema20[i]/ema50[i] point
// series for every bar, unconditionally). The dashboard's own EMA calculation is NOT changed and is
// NOT read here (per explicit instruction to leave the visualization layer alone) - this is the EA's
// own independent, closed-candle-safe computation of the same underlying concept (price between the
// two EMAs), using the EA's own EmaAt().
//
// EMA_SLOPE_ACTIVE: reuses the EMA Trend Mind's OWN exact BUY/SELL decision (gap>0/<0 AND
// normalizedGap>=Inp_EMAMinGapATR AND slope agreeing) - active whenever that verdict is non-WAIT.
//
// ACTIVE_PING = corridorActive OR slopeActive. Evaluated ONCE per NEW CLOSED M1 bar (see
// g_activePingLastBarTime's own header) - never per-tick, and never off the still-forming bar (the
// same CopyRates(...,1,...) closed-candles-only convention as EvaluateEmaTrendMind() itself).

//--- Pure decision function - the single source of truth for corridorActive/slopeDirection/
//--- slopeActive/active, given already-computed scalar inputs. Callable both from
//--- EvaluateActivePing() (live) and RunActivePingTests() (deterministic, literal test inputs) - same
//--- "pure classifier + live wrapper" pattern already established by ClassifyPriceVolumeExpansion()/
//--- EvaluatePriceVolumeExpansionStructure() elsewhere in this file. minGapATR/slopeLookback are
//--- passed in explicitly (not read from Inp_* globals) so tests can exercise exact threshold values
//--- deterministically regardless of the live input configuration.
void ClassifyActivePing(const double refClose, const double ema20, const double ema50,
                         const bool haveAtr, const double gap, const double normalizedGap, const double emaSlope,
                         const double minGapATR,
                         bool &outCorridorActive, ENUM_LITE_DIR &outSlopeDirection, bool &outSlopeActive, bool &outActive)
  {
   outCorridorActive = (refClose>=MathMin(ema20,ema50) && refClose<=MathMax(ema20,ema50));

   if(!haveAtr)
     {
      outSlopeDirection = LDIR_WAIT;
      outSlopeActive = false;
      outActive = outCorridorActive;
      return;
     }

   // SAME exact condition as EvaluateEmaTrendMind()'s own BUY/SELL branches - copied verbatim.
   if(gap > 0.0 && normalizedGap >= minGapATR && emaSlope > 0.0)       outSlopeDirection = LDIR_BUY;
   else if(gap < 0.0 && normalizedGap >= minGapATR && emaSlope < 0.0)  outSlopeDirection = LDIR_SELL;
   else                                                                 outSlopeDirection = LDIR_WAIT;
   outSlopeActive = (outSlopeDirection != LDIR_WAIT);
   outActive = outCorridorActive || outSlopeActive;
  }

//--- 2026-09-09, explicit operator request (EMA20/EMA50 NEUTRAL-MARKET BLOCKER - Part 2 of the 3 new
//--- entry-protection gates): pure classifier, no globals - same "pure classifier, no globals"
//--- convention as ClassifyActivePing() just above. A market is "neutral" (genuinely flat/choppy EMA
//--- structure, independent of the existing EMA Trend Mind/EMA Slope Blocker directional veto) when the
//--- EMA20/50 separation is narrow (normalizedGap<=neutralGapATR) AND there has been recent whipsaw
//--- (at least one gap-sign crossover in the trailing window) - BOTH conditions required, gap alone is
//--- not sufficient (a persistently narrow-but-one-sided gap is not whipsaw).
//--- 2026-09-11, explicit operator request (ACTIVE_PING/EMA35 ARCHITECTURE REWIRE - Part B): NOW DEAD/
//--- DISCONNECTED - this function is left DEFINED but no longer called by EvaluateActivePing() (which now
//--- sets r.emaNeutral = (r.ema35MarketSide==EMA35_NEUTRAL) directly - see that function's own updated
//--- body). Inp_EMANeutralGapATR/g_emaGapSignHistory[]/g_emaGapSignHistoryCount/emaCrossoverCount20 are
//--- ALSO now genuinely unreferenced by any live entry gate as a direct consequence. Left in place
//--- (not deleted) matching this file's own established convention for a fully-superseded mechanism
//--- (e.g. the old 11-tier trailing SL arrays from a prior task) - deletion is harder to reverse than
//--- leaving a disconnected, documented mechanism in place, and this task's explicit scope is the
//--- ACTIVE_PING/EMA35 architecture, not a dead-code cleanup pass.
bool ClassifyEmaNeutral(const double normalizedGap, const int crossoverCount, const double neutralGapATR)
  {
   return (normalizedGap<=neutralGapATR && crossoverCount>=1);
  }

//--- 2026-09-11, explicit operator request (ACTIVE_PING/EMA35 ARCHITECTURE REWIRE - Part A): pure
//--- classifier, no globals - same "pure classifier, no globals" convention as ClassifyActivePing()/
//--- ClassifyEmaNeutral() above. Classifies price's relationship to the NEW independent EMA35 axis.
//--- price==EMA35 exactly is unsuitable for M1 (near-never true), so an ATR-normalized distance band
//--- (Inp_EMA35NeutralBandATR, default 0.10 - deliberately a DIFFERENT scale from Inp_EMANeutralGapATR's
//--- 0.375, a different concept) is used instead of a bare equality/corridor check.
ENUM_EMA35_MARKET_SIDE ClassifyEma35MarketSide(const double refClose, const double ema35, const double atr, const double neutralBandATR)
  {
   if(atr<=0.0) return EMA35_NEUTRAL; // fail-safe, never fabricate a side without a valid ATR
   double normalizedDistance = MathAbs(refClose-ema35)/atr;
   if(normalizedDistance<=neutralBandATR) return EMA35_NEUTRAL;
   return (refClose>ema35) ? EMA35_BUY : EMA35_SELL;
  }

//--- 2026-09-09, explicit operator request (EMA CONTINUATION/EXTENSION CLASSIFICATION): pure classifier,
//--- no globals - same "pure classifier, no globals" convention as ClassifyActivePing()/
//--- ClassifyEmaNeutral() just above. Distinguishes a healthy directional continuation (safe to
//--- enter/confirm) from an overextended trend (direction still valid, but price too far from EMA35 -
//--- wait for pullback, NOT a block, NOT a reversal).
//--- 2026-09-11, explicit operator request (ACTIVE_PING/EMA35 ARCHITECTURE REWIRE - Part B): REWRITTEN to
//--- take EMA35 inputs instead of EMA20/EMA50 inputs (per spec section 17 - "migrate to EMA35... reusing
//--- the existing 2.0 ATR threshold value, just recomputed as abs(price-EMA35)/ATR"). The FUNCTION NAME,
//--- its RETURN TYPE (ENUM_EMA_ENTRY_STATE, the existing 3-value enum - NOT a new 4th parallel enum, since
//--- the neutral-vs-continuation-vs-extended concept is identical, just re-based on EMA35), and the
//--- Inp_EMAExtensionMaxATR threshold (REUSED, not replaced - same 2.0 default) are all UNCHANGED from the
//--- prior EMA20/50-based version above - only the formula inside changed. Simpler than the old version
//--- since ema35MarketSide (from ClassifyEma35MarketSide() above) already IS the directional-validity
//--- verdict - no separate EMA-ordering-vs-slope-agreement check is needed the way the old EMA20/EMA50
//--- version needed (ema20>ema50 && slopeDirection==BUY && ...).
ENUM_EMA_ENTRY_STATE ClassifyEmaEntryState(const ENUM_EMA35_MARKET_SIDE ema35MarketSide, const double refClose,
                                            const double ema35, const double atr, const double extensionMaxATR)
  {
   if(ema35MarketSide==EMA35_NEUTRAL) return EMA_ENTRY_NEUTRAL;
   if(atr<=0.0) return EMA_ENTRY_NEUTRAL; // cannot compute extension without a valid ATR - fail safe, never fabricate
   double extensionATR = (ema35MarketSide==EMA35_BUY) ? (refClose-ema35)/atr : (ema35-refClose)/atr;
   return (extensionATR>extensionMaxATR) ? EMA_ENTRY_TREND_EXTENDED : EMA_ENTRY_TREND_CONTINUATION;
  }

ActivePingState EvaluateActivePing()
  {
   ActivePingState r;
   r.valid=false; r.barTime=0; r.ema20=0.0; r.ema50=0.0; r.refClose=0.0; r.corridorActive=false;
   r.gap=0.0; r.normalizedGap=0.0; r.atr=0.0; r.emaSlope=0.0; r.slopeDirection=LDIR_WAIT;
   r.slopeActive=false; r.trendingSideActive=false; r.active=false; r.reasoning="";
   //--- 2026-09-09: six new fields - default to "carry forward prior state" for the lock fields (set
   //--- properly below once the rest of this function's existing EMA/ATR computation is available) and
   //--- to "no crossover/not neutral" for the EMA fields until computed below.
   r.postLossLockDirection = g_activePing.postLossLockDirection;
   r.postLossLockReferencePrice = g_activePing.postLossLockReferencePrice;
   r.postLossLockArmed = g_activePing.postLossLockArmed;
   r.postLossLockReleased = g_activePing.postLossLockReleased;
   r.emaCrossoverCount20 = 0;
   r.emaNeutral = false;
   r.emaEntryState = EMA_ENTRY_NEUTRAL;
   r.extensionATR = 0.0;
   //--- 2026-09-11, explicit operator request (ACTIVE_PING/EMA35 ARCHITECTURE REWIRE - Part A/C): default
   //--- init for the new fields - never fabricated, fail-safe defaults until genuinely computed below.
   r.ema35 = 0.0;
   r.ema35Slope = 0.0;
   r.ema35MarketSide = EMA35_NEUTRAL;
   r.ema35NormalizedDistance = 0.0;
   //--- 2026-09-14, explicit operator request (ACTIVE_PING CROSSING-BASED DIRECTION): activePingDirection
   //--- is no longer this function's field to default/derive - it is owned by the separate per-tick
   //--- EvaluateActivePingCrossingDirection() state machine (see g_activePingCrossing's own header).
   //--- Since this function's return value gets wholesale-assigned to g_activePing by its caller
   //--- (g_activePing = EvaluateActivePing();), defaulting this field to LDIR_WAIT here would silently
   //--- ERASE the crossing machine's own persisted direction every time a new bar closes - carry forward
   //--- whatever g_activePing.activePingDirection currently holds instead of resetting it.
   r.activePingDirection = g_activePing.activePingDirection;
   r.activePingRefreshBarCount = 0;

   if(Inp_EMAFastPeriod < 1 || Inp_EMASlowPeriod < 1 || Inp_EMAFastPeriod >= Inp_EMASlowPeriod)
     {
      r.reasoning = StringFormat("invalid EMA periods (fast=%d slow=%d)", Inp_EMAFastPeriod, Inp_EMASlowPeriod);
      return r;
     }

   const int atrPeriod = 14; // SAME fixed default as EvaluateEmaTrendMind()
   const int slopeLookback = MathMax(0, Inp_EMASlopeLookback);
   const int needed = Inp_EMASlowPeriod + slopeLookback + atrPeriod + 5; // SAME warm-up budget formula

   MqlRates ratesEma[]; ArraySetAsSeries(ratesEma, true);
   int nEma = CopyRates(g_symbol, PERIOD_M1, 1, needed, ratesEma); // index 1 = first CLOSED candle, never the running one
   if(nEma < needed)
     {
      r.reasoning = StringFormat("insufficient closed-candle history (have=%d need=%d)", nEma, needed);
      return r;
     }

   r.barTime = ratesEma[0].time;
   r.refClose = ratesEma[0].close;

   double alphaFastCache = 2.0 / (Inp_EMAFastPeriod + 1.0);
   double emaFastNow  = EmaAt(ratesEma, nEma, Inp_EMAFastPeriod, 0, alphaFastCache);
   double emaFastPrev = EmaAt(ratesEma, nEma, Inp_EMAFastPeriod, slopeLookback, alphaFastCache);
   double alphaSlowCache = 2.0 / (Inp_EMASlowPeriod + 1.0);
   double emaSlowNow  = EmaAt(ratesEma, nEma, Inp_EMASlowPeriod, 0, alphaSlowCache);

   if(!MathIsValidNumber(emaFastNow) || !MathIsValidNumber(emaFastPrev) || !MathIsValidNumber(emaSlowNow))
     {
      r.reasoning = "invalid EMA values";
      return r;
     }

   r.ema20 = emaFastNow;
   r.ema50 = emaSlowNow;

   double atr = 0.0;
   int atrSamples = 0;
   for(int i = 0; i < atrPeriod && (i+1) < nEma; i++)
     {
      double highLow  = ratesEma[i].high - ratesEma[i].low;
      double highPrev = MathAbs(ratesEma[i].high - ratesEma[i+1].close);
      double lowPrev  = MathAbs(ratesEma[i].low  - ratesEma[i+1].close);
      double tr = MathMax(highLow, MathMax(highPrev, lowPrev));
      atr += tr; atrSamples++;
     }
   if(atrSamples > 0) atr /= atrSamples;

   bool haveAtr = (atrSamples >= atrPeriod && MathIsValidNumber(atr) && atr > 0.0);
   if(haveAtr)
     {
      r.gap = emaFastNow - emaSlowNow;
      r.normalizedGap = MathAbs(r.gap) / atr;
      r.emaSlope = emaFastNow - emaFastPrev;
      r.atr = atr;
     }

   ClassifyActivePing(r.refClose, r.ema20, r.ema50, haveAtr, r.gap, r.normalizedGap, r.emaSlope, Inp_EMAMinGapATR,
                       r.corridorActive, r.slopeDirection, r.slopeActive, r.active);

   //--- 2026-09-11, explicit operator request (ACTIVE_PING/EMA35 ARCHITECTURE REWIRE - Part A): NEW,
   //--- independent EMA35 axis. Replicates EvaluateEma35TrackingSl()'s own exact formula (period=35,
   //--- alpha=2/(35+1), EmaAt(), closed-bars-only) - see that function's own header for the convention
   //--- being mirrored (deliberately NOT shared/called - same "provably unchanged original" precedent as
   //--- ClassifyActivePing() vs EvaluateEmaTrendMind() above). Reuses the SAME already-fetched closed-bar
   //--- ratesEma[] array (fetched above for EMA20/50/ATR, needed=Inp_EMASlowPeriod(50)+slopeLookback(2)+
   //--- atrPeriod(14)+5=71 bars by default) rather than a second/duplicate CopyRates call - 71 bars is
   //--- comfortably >= the 35+slopeLookback+5=42 bars EMA35 (with its own slope reading) requires, so no
   //--- live/duplicate fetch is structurally necessary. If a future retune of Inp_EMASlowPeriod ever made
   //--- ratesEma[] too small for EMA35's own needs, the MathIsValidNumber() guard below fails safe (ema35
   //--- stays 0.0, r.valid still becomes true off the EMA20/50 path) rather than silently fabricating a
   //--- value from insufficient history.
   const int ema35Period = 35; // SAME literal as EvaluateEma35TrackingSl()
   double alphaEma35 = 2.0 / (ema35Period + 1.0);
   double ema35Now  = EmaAt(ratesEma, nEma, ema35Period, 0, alphaEma35);
   double ema35Prev = EmaAt(ratesEma, nEma, ema35Period, slopeLookback, alphaEma35); // SAME Inp_EMASlopeLookback used by the EMA20 slope above
   if(MathIsValidNumber(ema35Now) && MathIsValidNumber(ema35Prev))
     {
      r.ema35 = ema35Now;
      r.ema35Slope = ema35Now - ema35Prev; // CONFIRMATION/CONTEXT ONLY - never wired as an independent gate (see field's own header)
      if(haveAtr)
        {
         r.ema35NormalizedDistance = MathAbs(r.refClose-r.ema35)/atr;
         r.ema35MarketSide = ClassifyEma35MarketSide(r.refClose, r.ema35, atr, Inp_EMA35NeutralBandATR);
        }
     }

   //--- 2026-09-11, explicit operator request (ACTIVE_PING/EMA35 ARCHITECTURE REWIRE - Part C): ACTIVE_PING's
   //--- own 25-CLOSED-bar structural refresh window (spec section 5 - "bar[1] through bar[25], bar[1]=most
   //--- recently closed M1 bar... the currently forming candle MUST NOT be used"). EvaluateActivePing()
   //--- ALREADY recomputes exactly once per new closed M1 bar (g_activePingLastBarTime's latch in OnTick(),
   //--- unchanged) and ALREADY exclusively uses closed bars - this is a SEPARATE, explicit 25-bar fetch
   //--- (distinct from ratesEma[]'s own 71-bar EMA20/50/ATR warm-up window) used specifically to establish
   //--- activePingDirection's own deterministic refresh-cadence/window-size plumbing.
   //---
   //--- 2026-09-14, explicit operator request (ACTIVE_PING CROSSING-BASED DIRECTION): activePingDirection
   //--- is NO LONGER derived here (previously mirrored ema35MarketSide directly every closed bar, per the
   //--- 2026-09-11 architectural decision this comment block used to document). It is now owned entirely by
   //--- EvaluateActivePingCrossingDirection() (see that function's own header), a SEPARATE per-TICK state
   //--- machine that only flips direction when live price genuinely crosses the last-25-closed-bar high/low
   //--- - called from OnTick() immediately after this function. r.activePingDirection is intentionally left
   //--- UNTOUCHED here (whatever the crossing function last wrote persists across this function's own
   //--- once-per-closed-bar recompute of every OTHER field) - do not reset it to WAIT or re-derive it from
   //--- ema35MarketSide here, that would silently overwrite the crossing state machine's own output.
   {
      MqlRates activePing25Bars[]; ArraySetAsSeries(activePing25Bars, true);
      int got = CopyRates(g_symbol, PERIOD_M1, 1, 25, activePing25Bars); // bar[1]=most recently closed, bar[25]=oldest; shift=1 start, running candle never included
      r.activePingRefreshBarCount = (got>0) ? got : 0;
   }

   //--- 2026-09-08, explicit operator request (ACTIVE_PING ENTRY-TO-EXIT RANGE, REPOINTED per explicit
   //--- operator correction - "I off the retry Engine to don't retry than why you build it under it i
   //--- need this in original trade singal" / confirmed via AskUserQuestion: "Decouple it from the
   //--- Retry Engine entirely"): THIRD condition, computed here (not inside ClassifyActivePing(), which
   //--- stays a pure/global-free classifier per its own established header) since it reads
   //--- g_lastClosedTrade, a live global. Originally reused g_retryEngine's own candidate memory - that
   //--- was wrong because g_retryEngine only ever arms for TRAILING/BREAK_EVEN protected exits
   //--- (RegisterRetryCandidate()'s own deliberate, narrow scope), going stale whenever a recent close
   //--- was any OTHER exit type, unrelated to whether Early Re-Entry (KMIE_LITE_EARLY_REENTRY_MAX_COUNT
   //--- =0, a DIFFERENT already-disabled mechanism) or the Retry Engine itself is enabled/disabled. Now
   //--- reads g_lastClosedTrade instead - a separate tracker updated on EVERY closed ticket regardless
   //--- of exit type (see CleanupTrailingSlots()'s own new population block) - "the original trade
   //--- signal" the operator asked for, not a Retry-Engine-eligibility-filtered subset of it. Only
   //--- meaningful once a position has actually closed this session (valid) AND its entry price was
   //--- successfully resolved from history (entryPrice>0.0 - never treats an unresolved 0.0 as a valid
   //--- range boundary). rangeActive = r.refClose (the SAME reference close corridor/slope already use)
   //--- sits between the closed trade's own entry and exit price, inclusive, regardless of which of the
   //--- two is numerically larger (a SELL's exit is typically below its entry, a BUY's exit above -
   //--- MathMin/MathMax handles both without a direction-specific branch).
   r.rangeActive = false;
   if(g_lastClosedTrade.valid && g_lastClosedTrade.entryPrice>0.0)
     {
      double rangeLo = MathMin(g_lastClosedTrade.entryPrice, g_lastClosedTrade.exitPrice);
      double rangeHi = MathMax(g_lastClosedTrade.entryPrice, g_lastClosedTrade.exitPrice);
      r.rangeActive = (r.refClose>=rangeLo && r.refClose<=rangeHi);
     }
   //--- 2026-09-16, explicit operator request (ACTIVE_PING SIMPLIFIED TO EMA20/50 - "Active Ping should be
   //--- only in 20 to 50 removed 35 and crosses both EMA 20 & 50"): FULL REPLACEMENT of the 2026-09-11
   //--- EMA35-based formula (r.active = (r.ema35MarketSide!=EMA35_NEUTRAL) || r.rangeActive - removed
   //--- entirely, both the EMA35-side term AND the post-loss rangeActive term dropped, per the operator's
   //--- own explicit "should be ONLY" scoping - not additive). ACTIVE_PING is now active whenever the
   //--- reference closed candle's close sits inside the EMA20/EMA50 corridor - r.corridorActive, already
   //--- computed by ClassifyActivePing() just above using the EMA20/50 pair specifically (never touched by
   //--- the 2026-09-11 rewire, its output was just being discarded at this line since that date - now
   //--- reused directly). The SECOND condition - "price/candle crosses both EMA20 and EMA50" - is a
   //--- genuinely per-tick, event-driven check (EvaluateEma2050CrossActive(), called every tick from
   //--- OnTick(), see its own header) that this once-per-closed-bar function cannot itself observe; OnTick()
   //--- ORs g_ema2050CrossedThisTick into g_activePing.active immediately after that function runs each
   //--- tick (see OnTick()'s own call site) - so THIS line establishes the corridor baseline once per new
   //--- closed bar, and OnTick() layers the live crossing flag on top of it every tick without this
   //--- function needing to run more often than its existing once-per-bar cadence.
   //--- r.ema35/r.ema35Slope/r.ema35MarketSide/r.ema35NormalizedDistance/r.rangeActive are still computed
   //--- above (untouched) - g_activePing.emaNeutral/EMA_NEUTRAL_BLOCK and CheckActivePingPriceCross() still
   //--- read them exactly as before; only THIS field's own formula changed.
   //--- 2026-09-18, explicit operator request ("MY OPPORTUNITY CONSUMED IS WORKING ITS TOTALY UPTREND BUT
   //--- BOT NOT EXCUTING THE TRADE WHY") - ported from KMIE_MarketDNA_Lite.mq5 into this baseline file.
   //--- THIRD condition added: trendingSideActive. corridorActive only covers price BETWEEN the two EMAs;
   //--- a sustained trend that has already moved cleanly past both EMAs and kept running satisfied
   //--- neither corridorActive nor a fresh same-tick cross, leaving OPPORTUNITY_CONSUMED stuck blocking
   //--- every re-entry attempt indefinitely during exactly the "totally uptrend" case ACTIVE_PING exists
   //--- to recognize. True when refClose sits fully above BOTH ema20 and ema50, OR fully below BOTH
   //--- (never just one - that would be a mixed/ambiguous read, not a genuine trending side) AND
   //--- normalizedGap (already computed above, |ema20-ema50|/atr) clears Inp_ActivePingTrendingGapATR -
   //--- real separation between the two EMAs, not noise-level. Toggleable
   //--- (Inp_ActivePingTrendingSideEnabled, default true) for a safe rollback.
   r.trendingSideActive = Inp_ActivePingTrendingSideEnabled
      && ((r.refClose>r.ema20 && r.refClose>r.ema50) || (r.refClose<r.ema20 && r.refClose<r.ema50))
      && (r.normalizedGap>=Inp_ActivePingTrendingGapATR);
   r.active = r.corridorActive || r.trendingSideActive;

   //--- 2026-09-09, explicit operator request (POST-LOSS SAME-DIRECTION RE-ENTRY LOCK - arm/disarm
   //--- logic): this whole block runs at the SAME once-per-new-closed-bar cadence as the rest of this
   //--- function (see OnTick()'s own g_activePingLastBarTime latch, ~line 3773-3778, which already
   //--- guarantees EvaluateActivePing() itself is only called once per new closed bar - no second/
   //--- separate latch added here).
   //--- Arm: a NEW losing closed trade (realized P&L<0, direction resolved, and NOT the same ticket
   //--- already armed off before) arms the lock for that trade's own direction.
   if(g_lastClosedTrade.valid && g_lastClosedTrade.haveRealizedProfit && g_lastClosedTrade.realizedProfitUSD<0.0
      && g_lastClosedTrade.direction!=LDIR_WAIT && g_lastClosedTrade.ticket!=g_postLossLockLastArmedTicket)
     {
      r.postLossLockDirection = g_lastClosedTrade.direction;
      r.postLossLockArmed = true;
      r.postLossLockReferencePrice = g_lastClosedTrade.exitPrice;
      r.postLossLockReleased = false;
      g_postLossLockLastArmedTicket = g_lastClosedTrade.ticket;
     }
   //--- else: r.postLossLock* already carries forward the PRIOR g_activePing.postLossLock* values (set
   //--- at the top of this function, before this call overwrote g_activePing).

   //--- Release condition 1 (favorable cross) - diagnostics/cache-consistency only; the REAL live
   //--- decision always happens fresh every tick inside IsPostLossReentryLocked() itself (called from
   //--- MaybeExecute()), which reads the LIVE g_lastClosedTrade.exitPrice/SymbolInfoDouble() directly
   //--- rather than depending on this cached snapshot.
   if(r.postLossLockArmed)
     {
      double lockCurPrice = (r.postLossLockDirection==LDIR_BUY) ? SymbolInfoDouble(g_symbol, SYMBOL_BID) : SymbolInfoDouble(g_symbol, SYMBOL_ASK);
      int lockDirSign = (r.postLossLockDirection==LDIR_BUY) ? 1 : (r.postLossLockDirection==LDIR_SELL) ? -1 : 0;
      if(lockDirSign!=0 && HasPriceCrossedFavorably(lockDirSign, g_lastClosedTrade.exitPrice, lockCurPrice))
        {
         r.postLossLockArmed = false;
         r.postLossLockReleased = true;
        }
     }

   //--- Release condition 2 (direction flip) - if the Minds vote direction this bar is the OPPOSITE of
   //--- the locked direction, the lock releases (a genuine directional flip, not just "price came back").
   if(r.postLossLockArmed)
     {
      bool isOpposite = (r.postLossLockDirection==LDIR_BUY && g_mindsVoteDir==LDIR_SELL) ||
                         (r.postLossLockDirection==LDIR_SELL && g_mindsVoteDir==LDIR_BUY);
      if(isOpposite)
        {
         r.postLossLockArmed = false;
         r.postLossLockReleased = true;
        }
     }

   //--- 2026-09-09, explicit operator request (EMA20/EMA50 NEUTRAL-MARKET BLOCKER - crossover/neutral
   //--- logic): reuses r.gap/r.normalizedGap/r.atr/haveAtr already computed above in THIS SAME function -
   //--- no second/independent EMA or ATR calculation. Current bar's gap sign: +1 if gap>0, -1 if gap<0, 0
   //--- if exactly 0.0. Ring buffer shifted by one (drop oldest, index 19; index 0 = most recent).
   {
      int curGapSign = (r.gap>0.0) ? 1 : (r.gap<0.0) ? -1 : 0;
      for(int shiftIdx=19; shiftIdx>0; shiftIdx--)
         g_emaGapSignHistory[shiftIdx] = g_emaGapSignHistory[shiftIdx-1];
      g_emaGapSignHistory[0] = curGapSign;
      if(g_emaGapSignHistoryCount<20) g_emaGapSignHistoryCount++;

      int crossoverCounter = 0;
      int histLen = MathMin(g_emaGapSignHistoryCount, 20);
      for(int ci=0; ci<histLen-1; ci++)
        {
         if(g_emaGapSignHistory[ci]!=g_emaGapSignHistory[ci+1] && g_emaGapSignHistory[ci]!=0 && g_emaGapSignHistory[ci+1]!=0)
            crossoverCounter++;
        }
      r.emaCrossoverCount20 = crossoverCounter;
      //--- 2026-09-11, explicit operator request (ACTIVE_PING/EMA35 ARCHITECTURE REWIRE - Part B):
      //--- r.emaNeutral is NOW REDEFINED to mirror r.ema35MarketSide==EMA35_NEUTRAL, replacing the old
      //--- ClassifyEmaNeutral(normalizedGap, crossoverCount, Inp_EMANeutralGapATR) call entirely. The
      //--- crossoverCounter/g_emaGapSignHistory[] logic just above is LEFT RUNNING (still populates
      //--- r.emaCrossoverCount20, a kept diagnostic field) but its OUTPUT no longer feeds any live entry
      //--- gate - see ClassifyEmaNeutral()'s own updated header for the "now dead, disconnected, not
      //--- deleted" rationale.
      r.emaNeutral = (r.ema35MarketSide==EMA35_NEUTRAL);
   }

   //--- 2026-09-09, explicit operator request (EMA CONTINUATION/EXTENSION CLASSIFICATION): computed
   //--- immediately after r.emaNeutral above via ClassifyEmaEntryState() - see that function's own
   //--- header. r.extensionATR is the raw signed (price-EMA35)/ATR value, separately computed here (not
   //--- duplicated inside the classifier's return value) for logging/diagnostics only - 0.0 when
   //--- emaEntryState==EMA_ENTRY_NEUTRAL (no valid direction to measure extension against).
   //--- 2026-09-11, explicit operator request (ACTIVE_PING/EMA35 ARCHITECTURE REWIRE - Part B): call site
   //--- updated to pass EMA35-based arguments (r.ema35MarketSide, r.ema35) instead of the old EMA20/50
   //--- arguments (r.emaNeutral, r.ema20, r.ema50, r.slopeDirection) - ClassifyEmaEntryState()'s own
   //--- signature changed accordingly (see that function's updated header). r.emaEntryState/r.extensionATR
   //--- themselves are REUSED AS-IS (same struct fields, same names) - MaybeExecute()'s EMA_EXTENSION gate
   //--- automatically inherits the new EMA35-based semantics with zero changes at that call site.
   r.emaEntryState = haveAtr ? ClassifyEmaEntryState(r.ema35MarketSide, r.refClose, r.ema35, r.atr, Inp_EMAExtensionMaxATR) : EMA_ENTRY_NEUTRAL;
   r.extensionATR = 0.0;
   if(haveAtr && (r.emaEntryState==EMA_ENTRY_TREND_CONTINUATION || r.emaEntryState==EMA_ENTRY_TREND_EXTENDED))
     {
      r.extensionATR = (r.ema35MarketSide==EMA35_BUY) ? (r.refClose-r.ema35)/r.atr : (r.ema35-r.refClose)/r.atr;
     }

   //--- [EMA_ENTRY_STATE] transition log - fires ONLY when the state differs from the last logged state
   //--- (g_lastLoggedEmaEntryState), matching the once-per-new-closed-bar cadence everything else in this
   //--- area already has (EvaluateActivePing() itself is only called once per new closed bar), never
   //--- spamming per-tick.
   if(r.emaEntryState != g_lastLoggedEmaEntryState)
     {
      string stateName = (r.emaEntryState==EMA_ENTRY_NEUTRAL) ? "EMA_NEUTRAL" :
                          (r.emaEntryState==EMA_ENTRY_TREND_CONTINUATION) ? "EMA_TREND_CONTINUATION" : "EMA_TREND_EXTENDED";
      if(r.emaEntryState==EMA_ENTRY_NEUTRAL)
         Print("[EMA_ENTRY_STATE] state=" + stateName);
      else
         Print(StringFormat("[EMA_ENTRY_STATE] state=%s direction=%s normalizedGap=%.3f extensionATR=%.3f",
               stateName, DirName(r.slopeDirection), r.normalizedGap, r.extensionATR));
      DashAppendLine("logs.jsonl", StringFormat(
         "{\"time\":\"%s\",\"tag\":\"EMA_ENTRY_STATE\",\"message\":\"state=%s direction=%s normalizedGap=%.3f extensionATR=%.3f\"}",
         DashIsoTime(TimeCurrent()), stateName, DirName(r.slopeDirection), r.normalizedGap, r.extensionATR));
      g_lastLoggedEmaEntryState = r.emaEntryState;
     }

   r.valid = true;

   if(!haveAtr)
     {
      r.reasoning = StringFormat("ATR invalid or unavailable (samples=%d atr=%.5f) - corridorActive=%s rangeActive=%s still valid, slope unavailable",
            atrSamples, atr, r.corridorActive ? "true" : "false", r.rangeActive ? "true" : "false");
      return r;
     }

   r.reasoning = StringFormat("EMA%d=%.3f EMA%d=%.3f refClose=%.3f corridorActive=%s gap=%.3f ATR=%.3f gap/ATR=%.2f slope=%.5f slopeDir=%s slopeActive=%s rangeActive=%s trendingSideActive=%s active=%s | EMA35=%.3f ema35Slope=%.5f ema35Side=%s ema35NormDist=%.3f activePingDir=%s emaEntryState=%s extensionATR=%.3f",
         Inp_EMAFastPeriod, r.ema20, Inp_EMASlowPeriod, r.ema50, r.refClose, r.corridorActive ? "true" : "false",
         r.gap, r.atr, r.normalizedGap, r.emaSlope, DirName(r.slopeDirection), r.slopeActive ? "true" : "false",
         r.rangeActive ? "true" : "false", r.trendingSideActive ? "true" : "false", r.active ? "true" : "false",
         r.ema35, r.ema35Slope, EnumToString(r.ema35MarketSide), r.ema35NormalizedDistance, DirName(r.activePingDirection),
         EnumToString(r.emaEntryState), r.extensionATR);
   return r;
  }

//--- Diagnostic writer for ACTIVE_PING - throttled to once per NEW CLOSED M1 bar (via
//--- g_activePingLastBarTime, checked by the caller before this is even invoked), writes to a NEW,
//--- dedicated file active_ping.jsonl, never mixed into any existing log. NEVER read by any trading
//--- decision - purely for the operator/Claude to verify EMA20/EMA50/corridor/slope/ACTIVE_PING
//--- deterministically against real XAUUSD data, per explicit instruction ("Add diagnostics that
//--- expose the EA EMA20, EMA50, corridor state, slope state, ACTIVE_PING state, and bar timestamp").
void LogActivePing(const ActivePingState &r)
  {
   if(!Inp_DashboardLogEnabled) return;
   string line = StringFormat(
      "{\"time\":\"%s\",\"symbol\":\"%s\",\"valid\":%s,\"barTime\":\"%s\","
      "\"ema20\":%s,\"ema50\":%s,\"refClose\":%s,\"corridorActive\":%s,"
      "\"gap\":%s,\"normalizedGap\":%s,\"atr\":%s,\"emaSlope\":%s,"
      "\"slopeDirection\":\"%s\",\"slopeActive\":%s,\"rangeActive\":%s,"
      "\"rangeEntryPrice\":%s,\"rangeExitPrice\":%s,\"active\":%s,\"reasoning\":\"%s\"}",
      DashIsoTime(TimeCurrent()), g_symbol, r.valid ? "true" : "false", DashIsoTime(r.barTime),
      r.valid ? DoubleToString(r.ema20,3) : "null", r.valid ? DoubleToString(r.ema50,3) : "null",
      r.valid ? DoubleToString(r.refClose,3) : "null", r.valid ? (r.corridorActive?"true":"false") : "false",
      (r.valid && r.atr>0.0) ? DoubleToString(r.gap,3) : "null", (r.valid && r.atr>0.0) ? DoubleToString(r.normalizedGap,4) : "null",
      (r.valid && r.atr>0.0) ? DoubleToString(r.atr,3) : "null", (r.valid && r.atr>0.0) ? DoubleToString(r.emaSlope,5) : "null",
      DirName(r.slopeDirection), r.slopeActive ? "true" : "false", r.rangeActive ? "true" : "false",
      (g_lastClosedTrade.valid && g_lastClosedTrade.entryPrice>0.0) ? DoubleToString(g_lastClosedTrade.entryPrice,3) : "null",
      (g_lastClosedTrade.valid && g_lastClosedTrade.entryPrice>0.0) ? DoubleToString(g_lastClosedTrade.exitPrice,3) : "null",
      r.active ? "true" : "false",
      DashJsonEscape(r.reasoning));
   DashAppendLine("active_ping.jsonl", line);
  }

//--- 2026-08-30, explicit operator request (ABSORPTION MIND). Guarded division - returns
//--- `fallback` (never NaN/INF) whenever `denom` is zero, negative-zero, or not a valid finite
//--- number, instead of the raw `/` operator's undefined/inf/NaN result. Used everywhere this
//--- Mind divides by a value that could legitimately be zero (a flat window's avgRange, a
//--- doji's zero-range newest candle, etc.) - satisfies section 13/"G. Division by zero"'s
//--- explicit safety requirement.
double SafeDiv(const double numer, const double denom, const double fallback)
  {
   if(!MathIsValidNumber(denom) || MathAbs(denom) <= 0.0) return fallback;
   double result = numer / denom;
   if(!MathIsValidNumber(result)) return fallback;
   return result;
  }

//--- 2026-08-30, explicit operator request (ABSORPTION MIND - CONTROLLED PRODUCTION
//--- IMPLEMENTATION). Writes ONE Mind result into g_minds[16] (id 18).
//---
//--- PURPOSE: "is significant directional effort producing proportional price movement, or is it
//--- being absorbed by opposing activity/liquidity?" - an EFFORT-vs-RESULT measurement, distinct
//--- from every existing Mind (see the duplication-audit note at the end of this header).
//---
//--- INDEPENDENCE (explicit requirement - verified by construction, not just by comment): this
//--- function reads ONLY g_symbol/PERIOD_M1 CopyRates data (fresh, its own dedicated window,
//--- fetched right here) and its own persistence globals (g_prevAbsorptionSide/
//--- g_prevAbsorptionStreak). It does NOT read g_dnaState, g_dnaScore, g_ci (CandleIntelligence,
//--- including g_ci.absorption/g_ci.rejection - the pre-existing, directionless "effort without
//--- progress" scalar this task's own pre-implementation audit found in EvaluateMarketDNA() - left
//--- completely untouched by this Mind, per explicit operator decision to keep the two provably
//--- separate), scores[LDNA_*], g_mindsVoteDir, or any other g_minds[] slot. Every number below is
//--- computed fresh from raw OHLC+tick_volume.
//---
//--- DATA SOURCE: this file has no tick-level data path anywhere (confirmed by this task's own
//--- pre-implementation audit - no CopyTicks/MqlTick/SymbolInfoTick usage exists) and no
//--- Microstructure engine/include. Per the data hierarchy in section 7 of the spec, this Mind
//--- therefore uses the next-best tier: OHLC + MqlRates.tick_volume (MT5's real per-bar tick
//--- count, not a synthetic estimate) over a dedicated CLOSED-candle CopyRates(...,1,...) window -
//--- same closed-candle convention every other Mind in this file already uses.
//---
//--- PIPELINE (7 stages, matching the spec's own structure):
//--- 1. PRESSURE - dominant directional lean over the window, from body-weighted up/down bar
//---    count (bar's OWN close-vs-open, not a borrowed SignOf() from another Mind's raw feature).
//--- 2. EFFORT - the newest closed bar's tick_volume, normalized against the window's own average
//---    tick_volume (0..100 - how much participation, relative to this symbol's own recent
//---    baseline, not an arbitrary absolute count).
//--- 3. RESPONSE - the newest closed bar's own directional displacement (close-open, signed by
//---    the pressure side) normalized against the window's own average TRUE range (0..100 - how
//---    much price actually moved, relative to what a "normal" bar for this window moves).
//--- 4. INEFFICIENCY - 100-response, i.e. how little result was achieved for the effort present;
//---    SafeDiv-guarded (see SafeDiv() below), never divides by a zero/near-zero denominator.
//--- 5. REJECTION - the newest closed bar's own dominant single-sided wick%, computed independently
//---    here (NOT read from g_ci.rejection) from the SAME bar this function already fetched.
//--- 6. PERSISTENCE - consecutive-cycle streak of the SAME dominant side, read from
//---    g_prevAbsorptionSide/g_prevAbsorptionStreak (this cycle's own streak is written back to
//---    g_curAbsorptionStreak for EvaluateMinds()'s caller, OnTick(), to persist at cycle-end -
//---    see those globals' own declaration comment for the full lifecycle).
//--- 7. FINAL SCORE - transparent weighted sum (40% pressure-strength/effort, 30% inefficiency,
//---    20% rejection, 10% persistence - the spec's own initial weights), Clamp0to100()'d, split
//---    into buyerAbsorptionScore/sellerAbsorptionScore/absorptionScore.
//---
//--- DUPLICATION AUDIT: does NOT reduce to SignOf(netMove) (Consensus/#14), SignOf(ups-downs)
//--- (Structure/#7), SignOf(shortSlope) (Momentum/#1), candle-majority (buyingStrength/
//--- sellingStrength, used by no Mind directly), raw wick comparison alone (Reversal/#3 - that Mind
//--- compares AVERAGE wick% across a window with no effort/response/inefficiency component at
//--- all), raw volatility (Volatility/#6 - range vs average range, no directional/effort
//--- component), or breakout-extreme (Breakout/#12 - 2-vs-N bar high/low break, unrelated
//--- mechanism). Absorption's own decisive, unique ingredient is the EFFORT/RESPONSE ratio (stage
//--- 4, inefficiency) - no other Mind in this file computes a participation-normalized-by-its-own-
//--- result quantity.
void EvaluateAbsorptionMind()
  {
   const int slot = 16; // g_minds[] array position for this Mind (id 18)
   g_minds[slot].id = 18;
   g_minds[slot].name = "Absorption";

   if(!Inp_AbsorptionEnabled)
     {
      g_minds[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_curAbsorptionStreak = 0;
      g_minds[slot].reasoning = "Inp_AbsorptionEnabled=false";
      return;
     }
   if(Inp_AbsorptionLookback < 2 || Inp_AbsorptionMinSamples < 1 || Inp_AbsorptionMinSamples > Inp_AbsorptionLookback)
     {
      g_minds[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_curAbsorptionStreak = 0;
      g_minds[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("invalid Absorption inputs (lookback=%d minSamples=%d)",
            Inp_AbsorptionLookback, Inp_AbsorptionMinSamples);
      return;
     }

   // CLOSED candles only - CopyRates(...,1,...) starts at index 1, matching this file's existing
   // closed-candle convention (see every other CopyRates(...,1,...) call in this file). Index 0
   // (the currently-forming candle) is NEVER fetched into this window.
   MqlRates ratesAbs[]; ArraySetAsSeries(ratesAbs, true);
   int nAbs = CopyRates(g_symbol, PERIOD_M1, 1, Inp_AbsorptionLookback, ratesAbs);
   if(nAbs < Inp_AbsorptionMinSamples)
     {
      g_minds[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_curAbsorptionStreak = 0; // insufficient data resets persistence - never carry a streak across a data gap
      g_minds[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("insufficient closed-candle history (have=%d need>=%d)",
            nAbs, Inp_AbsorptionMinSamples);
      return;
     }

   // 2026-08-30, explicit operator request (ABSORPTION MIND, section 13/"I. Stale tick data - do
   // not manufacture an absorption signal"): this file has no genuine tick timestamp to check (no
   // CopyTicks path exists anywhere - see this Mind's own header), so the closest available
   // staleness signal is the newest CLOSED bar's own time versus the terminal's current time - if
   // it's implausibly old (>5 minutes stale on an M1 series - more than 5 missed bars), the feed
   // itself is suspect and this Mind refuses to manufacture a reading from it, rather than treating
   // old data as if it were current.
   if(TimeCurrent() - ratesAbs[0].time > 300)
     {
      g_minds[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_curAbsorptionStreak = 0;
      g_minds[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("stale data - newest closed bar is %d seconds old", (int)(TimeCurrent() - ratesAbs[0].time));
      return;
     }

   // --- STAGE 1: PRESSURE - body-weighted directional lean over the window, computed fresh from
   // THIS window's own bars (never SignOf() on another Mind's already-computed feature).
   double sumRange = 0.0, sumTickVol = 0.0;
   int upBars = 0, downBars = 0;
   for(int i = 0; i < nAbs; i++)
     {
      double bodyMove = ratesAbs[i].close - ratesAbs[i].open;
      double range = ratesAbs[i].high - ratesAbs[i].low;
      sumRange += range;
      sumTickVol += (double)ratesAbs[i].tick_volume;
      if(bodyMove > 0.0) upBars++; else if(bodyMove < 0.0) downBars++;
     }

   if(!MathIsValidNumber(sumRange) || sumRange <= 0.0)
     {
      g_minds[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_curAbsorptionStreak = 0;
      g_minds[slot].reasoning = "zero range over window - no valid observation";
      return;
     }

   ENUM_LITE_DIR pressureSide;
   if(upBars > downBars) pressureSide = LDIR_BUY;
   else if(downBars > upBars) pressureSide = LDIR_SELL;
   else pressureSide = LDIR_WAIT; // BALANCED - equal up/down bar count, no dominant side

   if(pressureSide == LDIR_WAIT)
     {
      g_minds[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_curAbsorptionStreak = 0;
      g_minds[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("pressure=BALANCED (up=%d down=%d, n=%d) - no dominant side", upBars, downBars, nAbs);
      return;
     }

   // --- STAGE 2: EFFORT - newest closed bar's own tick_volume, normalized against the window's
   // own average tick_volume. Guards: zero/invalid average tick_volume -> WAIT (never a fabricated
   // effort reading).
   double avgTickVol = sumTickVol / nAbs;
   double newestTickVol = (double)ratesAbs[0].tick_volume;
   if(!MathIsValidNumber(avgTickVol) || avgTickVol <= 0.0)
     {
      g_minds[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_curAbsorptionStreak = 0;
      g_minds[slot].reasoning = "zero/invalid tick_volume over window - cannot measure effort";
      return;
     }
   // effort = 100 at 2x the window's own average tick_volume (a genuinely active bar relative to
   // this window's own recent baseline), scaled linearly below that, clamped at 100 above it.
   double effort = Clamp0to100((newestTickVol / (avgTickVol * 2.0)) * 100.0);

   if(effort < Inp_AbsorptionEffortThreshold)
     {
      g_minds[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[slot].score = effort * 0.4; // partial score reflects the real (low) effort, matching section 12's "not simply copy the same value" - direction stays WAIT regardless
      g_curAbsorptionStreak = 0;
      g_minds[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("effort=%.1f below Inp_AbsorptionEffortThreshold=%.1f (newestTickVol=%.0f avgTickVol=%.1f) - participation too thin",
            effort, Inp_AbsorptionEffortThreshold, newestTickVol, avgTickVol);
      return;
     }

   // --- STAGE 3: RESPONSE - newest closed bar's own directional displacement, signed by the
   // pressure side (so a bar that moved WITH pressure scores high response; one that moved AGAINST
   // it scores zero, clamped, never negative), normalized against the window's own average range.
   double avgRange = sumRange / nAbs;
   double newestBodyMove = ratesAbs[0].close - ratesAbs[0].open;
   double directionalMove = (pressureSide == LDIR_BUY) ? newestBodyMove : -newestBodyMove;
   double response = Clamp0to100(SafeDiv(directionalMove, avgRange, 0.0) * 100.0);

   // --- STAGE 4: INEFFICIENCY - the core effort-vs-result quantity. High response despite high
   // effort = efficient (low inefficiency, healthy continuation). Low response despite high effort
   // = inefficient (high inefficiency, absorption evidence).
   double inefficiency = Clamp0to100(100.0 - response);

   if(inefficiency < Inp_AbsorptionInefficiencyThreshold)
     {
      g_minds[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[slot].score = Clamp0to100(inefficiency * 0.5);
      g_curAbsorptionStreak = 0;
      g_minds[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("pressure=%s effort=%.1f response=%.1f inefficiency=%.1f below Inp_AbsorptionInefficiencyThreshold=%.1f - effort IS producing proportional price movement (healthy, not absorbed)",
            DirName(pressureSide), effort, response, inefficiency, Inp_AbsorptionInefficiencyThreshold);
      return;
     }

   // --- STAGE 5: REJECTION - newest closed bar's own dominant single-sided wick%, computed
   // independently here (same math style as g_ci.rejection, but from THIS function's own window -
   // never reads g_ci).
   double newestRange = ratesAbs[0].high - ratesAbs[0].low;
   double upperWickPct = SafeDiv(ratesAbs[0].high - MathMax(ratesAbs[0].open, ratesAbs[0].close), newestRange, 0.0) * 100.0;
   double lowerWickPct = SafeDiv(MathMin(ratesAbs[0].open, ratesAbs[0].close) - ratesAbs[0].low, newestRange, 0.0) * 100.0;
   // For BUY pressure, the RELEVANT rejection is the UPPER wick (price pushed up, refused at the
   // top) - buyer absorption. For SELL pressure, the relevant rejection is the LOWER wick - seller
   // absorption. Using the opposite-side wick would measure the wrong thing entirely.
   double rejection = Clamp0to100((pressureSide == LDIR_BUY) ? upperWickPct : lowerWickPct);

   // --- STAGE 6: PERSISTENCE - consecutive-cycle streak of the SAME dominant pressure side.
   // g_curAbsorptionStreak (written here) becomes g_prevAbsorptionStreak at the end of THIS
   // OnTick() cycle (see OnTick()'s own g_prevAbsorptionStreak update) - so this reads the streak
   // as of the PREVIOUS cycle, exactly mirroring g_prevNetMove/g_curNetMove30's own convention.
   if(g_prevAbsorptionSide == pressureSide) g_curAbsorptionStreak = g_prevAbsorptionStreak + 1;
   else g_curAbsorptionStreak = 1; // side changed (or first-ever evaluation, g_prevAbsorptionSide==LDIR_WAIT) - streak restarts at 1, never fabricated
   g_prevAbsorptionSide = pressureSide;
   double persistence = Clamp0to100((g_curAbsorptionStreak / (double)MathMax(1, Inp_AbsorptionPersistenceCycles)) * 100.0);

   // --- STAGE 7: FINAL SCORE - transparent weighted sum, spec's own initial weights (section 9):
   // 40% pressure/participation strength (here: effort, since pressure itself is already binary
   // BUY/SELL by this point - effort IS the participation-strength component), 30% inefficiency,
   // 20% rejection, 10% persistence.
   double absorptionScore = Clamp0to100(effort * 0.40 + inefficiency * 0.30 + rejection * 0.20 + persistence * 0.10);

   // confidence/reliability/stability - kept conceptually separate per section 12, never copies of
   // each other or of absorptionScore itself:
   //   confidence  = how convincing the CORE evidence is (inefficiency+rejection average - the two
   //                 stages that most directly indicate absorption specifically, as opposed to
   //                 effort/persistence which are supporting context)
   //   reliability = how trustworthy the underlying SAMPLE is (sample-size ratio: nAbs vs the
   //                 requested Inp_AbsorptionLookback - a window that had to be truncated is less
   //                 reliable than a full one, independent of what the evidence itself says)
   //   stability   = how persistent the behavior is (persistence score directly - reused as its
   //                 own named field since it already IS a 0..100 stability measure, not
   //                 recalculated a second way)
   double confidence = Clamp0to100((inefficiency + rejection) / 2.0);
   double reliability = Clamp0to100((nAbs / (double)Inp_AbsorptionLookback) * 100.0);
   double stability = persistence;

   double buyerAbsorptionScore = (pressureSide == LDIR_BUY) ? absorptionScore : 0.0;
   double sellerAbsorptionScore = (pressureSide == LDIR_SELL) ? absorptionScore : 0.0;

   if(absorptionScore >= Inp_AbsorptionConfirmationThreshold)
     {
      // BUYER ABSORPTION (pressure=BUY, strong absorption) => buyers making effort but failing to
      // advance price => bearish evidence => SELL vote. SELLER ABSORPTION (pressure=SELL) => BUY
      // vote. This inversion is mandatory per spec section 5/10 - NOT a bug, NOT reversed logic.
      ENUM_LITE_DIR voteDir = (pressureSide == LDIR_BUY) ? LDIR_SELL : LDIR_BUY;
      string sideLabel = (pressureSide == LDIR_BUY) ? "BUYER" : "SELLER";
      string explanation = (pressureSide == LDIR_BUY)
            ? StringFormat("Buyer absorption: strong buying effort (%.1f) is producing weak upward price response (%.1f) with elevated upper rejection (%.1f).", effort, response, rejection)
            : StringFormat("Seller absorption: strong selling effort (%.1f) is producing weak downward price response (%.1f) with elevated lower rejection (%.1f).", effort, response, rejection);
      g_minds[slot].direction = voteDir; g_minds[slot].score = absorptionScore;
      g_minds[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("%s pressure=%s effort=%.1f response=%.1f inefficiency=%.1f rejection=%.1f persistence=%.1f (streak=%d) buyerAbsorption=%.1f sellerAbsorption=%.1f score=%.1f confidence=%.1f reliability=%.1f stability=%.1f state=%s_ABSORBED vote=%s",
            explanation, DirName(pressureSide), effort, response, inefficiency, rejection, persistence, g_curAbsorptionStreak,
            buyerAbsorptionScore, sellerAbsorptionScore, absorptionScore, confidence, reliability, stability, sideLabel, DirName(voteDir));
      return;
     }

   // Absorption evidence present but below the confirmation threshold - WAIT, but report the real
   // (partial) score, matching section 25's explicit example (a 2/3-style partial case still
   // reports a real score while direction stays WAIT).
   g_minds[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[slot].score = absorptionScore;
   g_minds[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("pressure=%s effort=%.1f response=%.1f inefficiency=%.1f rejection=%.1f persistence=%.1f (streak=%d) score=%.1f below Inp_AbsorptionConfirmationThreshold=%.1f confidence=%.1f reliability=%.1f stability=%.1f",
         DirName(pressureSide), effort, response, inefficiency, rejection, persistence, g_curAbsorptionStreak,
         absorptionScore, Inp_AbsorptionConfirmationThreshold, confidence, reliability, stability);
  }

//--- 2026-09-16, M5 PARALLEL PIPELINE: straight duplicate of EvaluateAbsorptionMind() above, writing
//--- g_mindsM5[16] (id 18) instead of g_minds[16] - its one internal PERIOD_M1 CopyRates call retargeted
//--- to PERIOD_M5. This Mind's own persistence state (g_prevAbsorptionSide/g_prevAbsorptionStreak/
//--- g_curAbsorptionStreak) is SHARED/M1-scoped cross-cycle memory - reusing it here for M5 would
//--- corrupt the M1 Mind's own streak. This M5 duplicate is intentionally streak-less/self-contained
//--- per tick (persistence contribution fixed at 0, matching a first-ever/no-streak-yet reading) -
//--- everything else (pressure/effort/response/inefficiency/rejection/final score) is byte-identical.
void EvaluateAbsorptionMindM5()
  {
   const int slot = 16; // g_mindsM5[] array position for this Mind (id 18)
   g_mindsM5[slot].id = 18;
   g_mindsM5[slot].name = "Absorption";

   if(!Inp_AbsorptionEnabled)
     {
      g_mindsM5[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = "Inp_AbsorptionEnabled=false";
      return;
     }
   if(Inp_AbsorptionLookback < 2 || Inp_AbsorptionMinSamples < 1 || Inp_AbsorptionMinSamples > Inp_AbsorptionLookback)
     {
      g_mindsM5[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("invalid Absorption inputs (lookback=%d minSamples=%d)",
            Inp_AbsorptionLookback, Inp_AbsorptionMinSamples);
      return;
     }

   MqlRates ratesAbs[]; ArraySetAsSeries(ratesAbs, true);
   int nAbs = CopyRates(g_symbol, PERIOD_M5, 1, Inp_AbsorptionLookback, ratesAbs);
   if(nAbs < Inp_AbsorptionMinSamples)
     {
      g_mindsM5[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("insufficient closed-candle history (have=%d need>=%d)",
            nAbs, Inp_AbsorptionMinSamples);
      return;
     }

   if(TimeCurrent() - ratesAbs[0].time > 1500)  // 5x a 5-minute bar - M5 equivalent of the M1 Mind's 5-bar staleness guard
     {
      g_mindsM5[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("stale data - newest closed bar is %d seconds old", (int)(TimeCurrent() - ratesAbs[0].time));
      return;
     }

   double sumRange = 0.0, sumTickVol = 0.0;
   int upBars = 0, downBars = 0;
   for(int i = 0; i < nAbs; i++)
     {
      double bodyMove = ratesAbs[i].close - ratesAbs[i].open;
      double range = ratesAbs[i].high - ratesAbs[i].low;
      sumRange += range;
      sumTickVol += (double)ratesAbs[i].tick_volume;
      if(bodyMove > 0.0) upBars++; else if(bodyMove < 0.0) downBars++;
     }

   if(!MathIsValidNumber(sumRange) || sumRange <= 0.0)
     {
      g_mindsM5[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = "zero range over window - no valid observation";
      return;
     }

   ENUM_LITE_DIR pressureSide;
   if(upBars > downBars) pressureSide = LDIR_BUY;
   else if(downBars > upBars) pressureSide = LDIR_SELL;
   else pressureSide = LDIR_WAIT;

   if(pressureSide == LDIR_WAIT)
     {
      g_mindsM5[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("pressure=BALANCED (up=%d down=%d, n=%d) - no dominant side", upBars, downBars, nAbs);
      return;
     }

   double avgTickVol = sumTickVol / nAbs;
   double newestTickVol = (double)ratesAbs[0].tick_volume;
   if(!MathIsValidNumber(avgTickVol) || avgTickVol <= 0.0)
     {
      g_mindsM5[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = "zero/invalid tick_volume over window - cannot measure effort";
      return;
     }
   double effort = Clamp0to100((newestTickVol / (avgTickVol * 2.0)) * 100.0);

   if(effort < Inp_AbsorptionEffortThreshold)
     {
      g_mindsM5[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[slot].score = effort * 0.4;
      g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("effort=%.1f below Inp_AbsorptionEffortThreshold=%.1f (newestTickVol=%.0f avgTickVol=%.1f) - participation too thin",
            effort, Inp_AbsorptionEffortThreshold, newestTickVol, avgTickVol);
      return;
     }

   double avgRange = sumRange / nAbs;
   double newestBodyMove = ratesAbs[0].close - ratesAbs[0].open;
   double directionalMove = (pressureSide == LDIR_BUY) ? newestBodyMove : -newestBodyMove;
   double response = Clamp0to100(SafeDiv(directionalMove, avgRange, 0.0) * 100.0);

   double inefficiency = Clamp0to100(100.0 - response);

   if(inefficiency < Inp_AbsorptionInefficiencyThreshold)
     {
      g_mindsM5[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[slot].score = Clamp0to100(inefficiency * 0.5);
      g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("pressure=%s effort=%.1f response=%.1f inefficiency=%.1f below Inp_AbsorptionInefficiencyThreshold=%.1f - effort IS producing proportional price movement (healthy, not absorbed)",
            DirName(pressureSide), effort, response, inefficiency, Inp_AbsorptionInefficiencyThreshold);
      return;
     }

   double newestRange = ratesAbs[0].high - ratesAbs[0].low;
   double upperWickPct = SafeDiv(ratesAbs[0].high - MathMax(ratesAbs[0].open, ratesAbs[0].close), newestRange, 0.0) * 100.0;
   double lowerWickPct = SafeDiv(MathMin(ratesAbs[0].open, ratesAbs[0].close) - ratesAbs[0].low, newestRange, 0.0) * 100.0;
   double rejection = Clamp0to100((pressureSide == LDIR_BUY) ? upperWickPct : lowerWickPct);

   //--- Persistence: this M5 duplicate has no dedicated cross-tick M5 streak global (see header) - fixed
   //--- at a single-cycle-equivalent value (streak=1) rather than fabricating cross-tick memory.
   int curStreakM5 = 1;
   double persistence = Clamp0to100((curStreakM5 / (double)MathMax(1, Inp_AbsorptionPersistenceCycles)) * 100.0);

   double absorptionScore = Clamp0to100(effort * 0.40 + inefficiency * 0.30 + rejection * 0.20 + persistence * 0.10);

   double confidence = Clamp0to100((inefficiency + rejection) / 2.0);
   double reliability = Clamp0to100((nAbs / (double)Inp_AbsorptionLookback) * 100.0);
   double stability = persistence;

   double buyerAbsorptionScore = (pressureSide == LDIR_BUY) ? absorptionScore : 0.0;
   double sellerAbsorptionScore = (pressureSide == LDIR_SELL) ? absorptionScore : 0.0;

   if(absorptionScore >= Inp_AbsorptionConfirmationThreshold)
     {
      ENUM_LITE_DIR voteDir = (pressureSide == LDIR_BUY) ? LDIR_SELL : LDIR_BUY;
      string sideLabel = (pressureSide == LDIR_BUY) ? "BUYER" : "SELLER";
      string explanation = (pressureSide == LDIR_BUY)
            ? StringFormat("Buyer absorption: strong buying effort (%.1f) is producing weak upward price response (%.1f) with elevated upper rejection (%.1f).", effort, response, rejection)
            : StringFormat("Seller absorption: strong selling effort (%.1f) is producing weak downward price response (%.1f) with elevated lower rejection (%.1f).", effort, response, rejection);
      g_mindsM5[slot].direction = voteDir; g_mindsM5[slot].score = absorptionScore;
      g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("%s pressure=%s effort=%.1f response=%.1f inefficiency=%.1f rejection=%.1f persistence=%.1f (streak=%d) buyerAbsorption=%.1f sellerAbsorption=%.1f score=%.1f confidence=%.1f reliability=%.1f stability=%.1f state=%s_ABSORBED vote=%s",
            explanation, DirName(pressureSide), effort, response, inefficiency, rejection, persistence, curStreakM5,
            buyerAbsorptionScore, sellerAbsorptionScore, absorptionScore, confidence, reliability, stability, sideLabel, DirName(voteDir));
      return;
     }

   g_mindsM5[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[slot].score = absorptionScore;
   g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("pressure=%s effort=%.1f response=%.1f inefficiency=%.1f rejection=%.1f persistence=%.1f (streak=%d) score=%.1f below Inp_AbsorptionConfirmationThreshold=%.1f confidence=%.1f reliability=%.1f stability=%.1f",
         DirName(pressureSide), effort, response, inefficiency, rejection, persistence, curStreakM5,
         absorptionScore, Inp_AbsorptionConfirmationThreshold, confidence, reliability, stability);
  }

//--- 2026-09-23, M15 PARALLEL PIPELINE: straight duplicate of EvaluateAbsorptionMind()/EvaluateAbsorptionMindM5()
//--- above, writing g_mindsM15[16] (id 18) instead of g_minds[16]/g_mindsM5[16] - its one internal
//--- PERIOD_M1 CopyRates call retargeted to PERIOD_M15. This Mind's own persistence state
//--- (g_prevAbsorptionSide/g_prevAbsorptionStreak/g_curAbsorptionStreak) is SHARED/M1-scoped cross-cycle
//--- memory - reusing it here for M15 would corrupt the M1 Mind's own streak, same reasoning as the M5
//--- twin above - so this M15 duplicate is likewise streak-less/self-contained per tick (persistence
//--- contribution fixed at a single-cycle-equivalent value, streak=1). The staleness guard is scaled to
//--- M15's own bar size (5 x 15-minute bars = 4500 seconds), mirroring the M5 twin's "5x a 5-minute bar"
//--- (1500 seconds) convention. Everything else (pressure/effort/response/inefficiency/rejection/final
//--- score) is byte-identical.
void EvaluateAbsorptionMindM15()
  {
   const int slot = 16; // g_mindsM15[] array position for this Mind (id 18)
   g_mindsM15[slot].id = 18;
   g_mindsM15[slot].name = "Absorption";

   if(!Inp_AbsorptionEnabled)
     {
      g_mindsM15[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = "Inp_AbsorptionEnabled=false";
      return;
     }
   if(Inp_AbsorptionLookback < 2 || Inp_AbsorptionMinSamples < 1 || Inp_AbsorptionMinSamples > Inp_AbsorptionLookback)
     {
      g_mindsM15[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("invalid Absorption inputs (lookback=%d minSamples=%d)",
            Inp_AbsorptionLookback, Inp_AbsorptionMinSamples);
      return;
     }

   MqlRates ratesAbs[]; ArraySetAsSeries(ratesAbs, true);
   int nAbs = CopyRates(g_symbol, PERIOD_M15, 1, Inp_AbsorptionLookback, ratesAbs);
   if(nAbs < Inp_AbsorptionMinSamples)
     {
      g_mindsM15[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("insufficient closed-candle history (have=%d need>=%d)",
            nAbs, Inp_AbsorptionMinSamples);
      return;
     }

   if(TimeCurrent() - ratesAbs[0].time > 4500)  // 5x a 15-minute bar - M15 equivalent of the M1 Mind's 5-bar staleness guard
     {
      g_mindsM15[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("stale data - newest closed bar is %d seconds old", (int)(TimeCurrent() - ratesAbs[0].time));
      return;
     }

   double sumRange = 0.0, sumTickVol = 0.0;
   int upBars = 0, downBars = 0;
   for(int i = 0; i < nAbs; i++)
     {
      double bodyMove = ratesAbs[i].close - ratesAbs[i].open;
      double range = ratesAbs[i].high - ratesAbs[i].low;
      sumRange += range;
      sumTickVol += (double)ratesAbs[i].tick_volume;
      if(bodyMove > 0.0) upBars++; else if(bodyMove < 0.0) downBars++;
     }

   if(!MathIsValidNumber(sumRange) || sumRange <= 0.0)
     {
      g_mindsM15[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = "zero range over window - no valid observation";
      return;
     }

   ENUM_LITE_DIR pressureSide;
   if(upBars > downBars) pressureSide = LDIR_BUY;
   else if(downBars > upBars) pressureSide = LDIR_SELL;
   else pressureSide = LDIR_WAIT;

   if(pressureSide == LDIR_WAIT)
     {
      g_mindsM15[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("pressure=BALANCED (up=%d down=%d, n=%d) - no dominant side", upBars, downBars, nAbs);
      return;
     }

   double avgTickVol = sumTickVol / nAbs;
   double newestTickVol = (double)ratesAbs[0].tick_volume;
   if(!MathIsValidNumber(avgTickVol) || avgTickVol <= 0.0)
     {
      g_mindsM15[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = "zero/invalid tick_volume over window - cannot measure effort";
      return;
     }
   double effort = Clamp0to100((newestTickVol / (avgTickVol * 2.0)) * 100.0);

   if(effort < Inp_AbsorptionEffortThreshold)
     {
      g_mindsM15[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[slot].score = effort * 0.4;
      g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("effort=%.1f below Inp_AbsorptionEffortThreshold=%.1f (newestTickVol=%.0f avgTickVol=%.1f) - participation too thin",
            effort, Inp_AbsorptionEffortThreshold, newestTickVol, avgTickVol);
      return;
     }

   double avgRange = sumRange / nAbs;
   double newestBodyMove = ratesAbs[0].close - ratesAbs[0].open;
   double directionalMove = (pressureSide == LDIR_BUY) ? newestBodyMove : -newestBodyMove;
   double response = Clamp0to100(SafeDiv(directionalMove, avgRange, 0.0) * 100.0);

   double inefficiency = Clamp0to100(100.0 - response);

   if(inefficiency < Inp_AbsorptionInefficiencyThreshold)
     {
      g_mindsM15[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[slot].score = Clamp0to100(inefficiency * 0.5);
      g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("pressure=%s effort=%.1f response=%.1f inefficiency=%.1f below Inp_AbsorptionInefficiencyThreshold=%.1f - effort IS producing proportional price movement (healthy, not absorbed)",
            DirName(pressureSide), effort, response, inefficiency, Inp_AbsorptionInefficiencyThreshold);
      return;
     }

   double newestRange = ratesAbs[0].high - ratesAbs[0].low;
   double upperWickPct = SafeDiv(ratesAbs[0].high - MathMax(ratesAbs[0].open, ratesAbs[0].close), newestRange, 0.0) * 100.0;
   double lowerWickPct = SafeDiv(MathMin(ratesAbs[0].open, ratesAbs[0].close) - ratesAbs[0].low, newestRange, 0.0) * 100.0;
   double rejection = Clamp0to100((pressureSide == LDIR_BUY) ? upperWickPct : lowerWickPct);

   //--- Persistence: this M15 duplicate has no dedicated cross-tick M15 streak global (see header) - fixed
   //--- at a single-cycle-equivalent value (streak=1) rather than fabricating cross-tick memory.
   int curStreakM15 = 1;
   double persistence = Clamp0to100((curStreakM15 / (double)MathMax(1, Inp_AbsorptionPersistenceCycles)) * 100.0);

   double absorptionScore = Clamp0to100(effort * 0.40 + inefficiency * 0.30 + rejection * 0.20 + persistence * 0.10);

   double confidence = Clamp0to100((inefficiency + rejection) / 2.0);
   double reliability = Clamp0to100((nAbs / (double)Inp_AbsorptionLookback) * 100.0);
   double stability = persistence;

   double buyerAbsorptionScore = (pressureSide == LDIR_BUY) ? absorptionScore : 0.0;
   double sellerAbsorptionScore = (pressureSide == LDIR_SELL) ? absorptionScore : 0.0;

   if(absorptionScore >= Inp_AbsorptionConfirmationThreshold)
     {
      ENUM_LITE_DIR voteDir = (pressureSide == LDIR_BUY) ? LDIR_SELL : LDIR_BUY;
      string sideLabel = (pressureSide == LDIR_BUY) ? "BUYER" : "SELLER";
      string explanation = (pressureSide == LDIR_BUY)
            ? StringFormat("Buyer absorption: strong buying effort (%.1f) is producing weak upward price response (%.1f) with elevated upper rejection (%.1f).", effort, response, rejection)
            : StringFormat("Seller absorption: strong selling effort (%.1f) is producing weak downward price response (%.1f) with elevated lower rejection (%.1f).", effort, response, rejection);
      g_mindsM15[slot].direction = voteDir; g_mindsM15[slot].score = absorptionScore;
      g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("%s pressure=%s effort=%.1f response=%.1f inefficiency=%.1f rejection=%.1f persistence=%.1f (streak=%d) buyerAbsorption=%.1f sellerAbsorption=%.1f score=%.1f confidence=%.1f reliability=%.1f stability=%.1f state=%s_ABSORBED vote=%s",
            explanation, DirName(pressureSide), effort, response, inefficiency, rejection, persistence, curStreakM15,
            buyerAbsorptionScore, sellerAbsorptionScore, absorptionScore, confidence, reliability, stability, sideLabel, DirName(voteDir));
      return;
     }

   g_mindsM15[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[slot].score = absorptionScore;
   g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("pressure=%s effort=%.1f response=%.1f inefficiency=%.1f rejection=%.1f persistence=%.1f (streak=%d) score=%.1f below Inp_AbsorptionConfirmationThreshold=%.1f confidence=%.1f reliability=%.1f stability=%.1f",
         DirName(pressureSide), effort, response, inefficiency, rejection, persistence, curStreakM15,
         absorptionScore, Inp_AbsorptionConfirmationThreshold, confidence, reliability, stability);
  }

//--- 2026-08-31, explicit operator request (FAIR VALUE / VWAP MIND - PRODUCTION IMPLEMENTATION).
//--- Writes ONE Mind result into g_minds[17] (id 19).
//---
//--- PURPOSE: "where is price relative to volume-weighted fair value, and is the market ACCEPTING
//--- or REJECTING that value?" - a MARKET LOCATION/VALUE measurement, distinct from every existing
//--- Mind (see the duplication-audit note at the end of this header).
//---
//--- INDEPENDENCE (verified by construction): reads ONLY g_symbol/PERIOD_M1 CopyRates data (a
//--- fresh, dedicated window fetched right here) and TimeCurrent() (the broker/server clock every
//--- existing timestamp in this file already uses). Does NOT read g_dnaState, g_dnaScore, g_ci,
//--- scores[LDNA_*], g_mindsVoteDir, or any other g_minds[] slot (including Absorption - the two
//--- Minds are permitted, and expected, to disagree).
//---
//--- VOLUME SOURCE: MqlRates.tick_volume ONLY - this file's pre-implementation audit (see this
//--- Mind's own input-group header comment) confirmed real_volume is never used anywhere in this
//--- codebase. Reasoning strings below explicitly call this a "volume-weighted fair value proxy",
//--- never "institutional"/"centralized exchange" VWAP, per explicit instruction.
//---
//--- SESSION WINDOW: broker/server-time (TimeCurrent()) midnight-to-now, computed via
//--- TimeToStruct()/StructToTime() (standard MQL5 calendar math, not a new time library), bounded
//--- by Inp_FairValueLookback (a hard 1440-bar/24h safety cap regardless of how far past midnight
//--- the session has run) - recomputed FRESH from a bounded CopyRates window every cycle, never
//--- incrementally accumulated, so there is no persistent running-sum state that could go stale
//--- across an EA restart or session boundary (satisfies section 21/23's reset-safety requirement
//--- by construction, not by a separate reset-detection code path).
//---
//--- PIPELINE (8 stages, matching the spec's own structure):
//--- 1. FAIR VALUE - sessionVWAP = SUM(TypicalPrice*tick_volume)/SUM(tick_volume) over the session
//---    window, TypicalPrice=(High+Low+Close)/3 per bar.
//--- 2. LOCATION - currentPrice-VWAP, classified ABOVE_VALUE/BELOW_VALUE/AT_VALUE by comparison
//---    against Inp_FairValueNearThresholdATR (an ATR-normalized band, not a raw-price band).
//--- 3. NORMALIZED DISTANCE - |currentPrice-VWAP|/ATR (classic 14-period ATR, same formula EMA
//---    Trend Mind already uses, computed independently here from THIS function's own window -
//---    not a shared/duplicated "engine", just the same established inline pattern by value).
//--- 4. VWAP SLOPE - sessionVWAP now vs sessionVWAP computed over the SAME window one bar earlier
//---    (a second independent VWAP calc ending 1 bar back) - UP/DOWN/FLAT, SUPPORTING evidence
//---    only, never itself another EMA-Trend-style Mind.
//--- 5. ACCEPTANCE - how many of the last Inp_FairValueAcceptanceBars closed bars closed on the
//---    SAME side of VWAP as the current price, and whether that count meets
//---    Inp_FairValueConfirmationBars (the anti-chop gate - section 16/32's mandatory requirement).
//--- 6. REJECTION - opposite-side evidence: how many of those same bars closed on the OPPOSITE
//---    side of VWAP from the current price (crossing count) - high crossing = weak/ambiguous
//---    acceptance, directly distinguishes "price left value and stayed" from "price is chopping
//---    around value".
//--- 7. EXTENSION - normalizedDistance vs Inp_FairValueExtensionThresholdATR - NORMAL/EXTENDED,
//---    used only as a DAMPENER on the final bullish/bearish evidence tally (section 17/30/31 -
//---    "distance alone is not automatically bullish/bearish"), never a standalone vote driver.
//--- 8. PERSISTENCE - reuses the acceptance-bar count directly as its own 0..100 measure (the
//---    count already IS a persistence measure - not recalculated a second way, same convention
//---    Absorption Mind's own stability field already established).
//---
//--- DUPLICATION AUDIT: does NOT reduce to price>VWAP (see the explicit BUY/SELL logic below - both
//--- branches require acceptance+persistence+non-extreme distance, never location alone), EMA
//--- direction (Trend/EMA Trend Minds), candle color (buyingStrength/sellingStrength, unused
//--- here), momentum (Momentum/#1's shortSlope), simple breakout (Breakout/#12's 2-vs-N extreme),
//--- or MTF/Absorption's own mechanisms (cross-timeframe EMA agreement; effort-vs-response). Fair
//--- Value's decisive, unique ingredient is the VOLUME-WEIGHTED location itself (stage 1-2) gated
//--- by acceptance/rejection persistence (stage 5-6) - no other Mind in this file computes a
//--- volume-weighted price level at all.
void EvaluateFairValueMind()
  {
   const int slot = 17; // g_minds[] array position for this Mind (id 19)
   g_minds[slot].id = 19;
   g_minds[slot].name = "Fair Value";

   if(!Inp_FairValueEnabled)
     {
      g_minds[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_minds[slot].reasoning = "Inp_FairValueEnabled=false";
      return;
     }
   if(Inp_FairValueLookback < 2 || Inp_FairValueMinSamples < 2 || Inp_FairValueMinSamples > Inp_FairValueLookback ||
      Inp_FairValueAcceptanceBars < 1 || Inp_FairValueConfirmationBars < 1 || Inp_FairValueConfirmationBars > Inp_FairValueAcceptanceBars)
     {
      g_minds[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_minds[slot].reasoning = "invalid Fair Value inputs";
      return;
     }

   // --- SESSION WINDOW: broker/server-time midnight-to-now, bounded by Inp_FairValueLookback bars.
   MqlDateTime nowStruct;
   TimeToStruct(TimeCurrent(), nowStruct);
   nowStruct.hour = 0; nowStruct.min = 0; nowStruct.sec = 0;
   datetime sessionStart = StructToTime(nowStruct);

   // CLOSED candles only - CopyRates(...,1,...) starts at index 1, matching this file's existing
   // closed-candle convention. Fetch the CAPPED window first (cheap, bounded), then trim to the
   // actual session boundary below - this avoids ever requesting an unbounded historical range.
   MqlRates ratesFv[]; ArraySetAsSeries(ratesFv, true);
   int nFvRaw = CopyRates(g_symbol, PERIOD_M1, 1, Inp_FairValueLookback, ratesFv);
   if(nFvRaw < Inp_FairValueMinSamples)
     {
      g_minds[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_minds[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("insufficient closed-candle history (have=%d need>=%d)", nFvRaw, Inp_FairValueMinSamples);
      return;
     }

   // Trim to bars within TODAY's session (time >= sessionStart) - series-indexed, so this is a
   // simple prefix count from index 0 (newest) outward.
   int nFv = 0;
   while(nFv < nFvRaw && ratesFv[nFv].time >= sessionStart) nFv++;
   if(nFv < Inp_FairValueMinSamples)
     {
      g_minds[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_minds[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("insufficient TODAY-session history (have=%d need>=%d) - session started %s",
            nFv, Inp_FairValueMinSamples, DashIsoTime(sessionStart));
      return;
     }

   // --- STAGE 1: FAIR VALUE - session VWAP = SUM(TypicalPrice*tick_volume)/SUM(tick_volume).
   double sumPV = 0.0, sumV = 0.0;
   for(int i = 0; i < nFv; i++)
     {
      double typical = (ratesFv[i].high + ratesFv[i].low + ratesFv[i].close) / 3.0;
      double vol = (double)ratesFv[i].tick_volume;
      sumPV += typical * vol;
      sumV += vol;
     }
   if(!MathIsValidNumber(sumV) || sumV <= 0.0)
     {
      g_minds[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_minds[slot].reasoning = "zero/invalid session volume - cannot compute VWAP, refusing to fabricate one";
      return;
     }
   double vwap = sumPV / sumV;
   if(!MathIsValidNumber(vwap) || vwap <= 0.0)
     {
      g_minds[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_minds[slot].reasoning = "invalid VWAP result";
      return;
     }

   double currentPrice = ratesFv[0].close; // newest CLOSED bar's close - current market location, still closed-candle-safe

   // --- Local ATR (classic 14-period mean True Range, same formula EMA Trend Mind already uses,
   // computed independently here from THIS window - not shared state, no duplicate "engine").
   const int atrPeriod = 14;
   double atr = 0.0; int atrSamples = 0;
   for(int i = 0; i < atrPeriod && (i+1) < nFv; i++)
     {
      double highLow = ratesFv[i].high - ratesFv[i].low;
      double highPrev = MathAbs(ratesFv[i].high - ratesFv[i+1].close);
      double lowPrev = MathAbs(ratesFv[i].low - ratesFv[i+1].close);
      atr += MathMax(highLow, MathMax(highPrev, lowPrev)); atrSamples++;
     }
   if(atrSamples > 0) atr /= atrSamples;
   if(atrSamples < 2 || !MathIsValidNumber(atr) || atr <= 0.0)
     {
      g_minds[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_minds[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("VWAP=%.3f price=%.3f but ATR invalid/unavailable (samples=%d atr=%.5f) - cannot normalize distance", vwap, currentPrice, atrSamples, atr);
      return;
     }

   // --- STAGE 2/3: LOCATION + NORMALIZED DISTANCE.
   double distance = currentPrice - vwap;
   double normDistance = SafeDiv(MathAbs(distance), atr, 0.0);
   ENUM_LITE_DIR location; // ABOVE_VALUE=BUY-side, BELOW_VALUE=SELL-side, AT_VALUE=WAIT-side, reusing LDIR_* as a side label only (never a vote by itself)
   if(normDistance < Inp_FairValueNearThresholdATR) location = LDIR_WAIT; // AT_VALUE
   else location = (distance > 0.0) ? LDIR_BUY : LDIR_SELL;

   if(location == LDIR_WAIT)
     {
      g_minds[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[slot].score = Clamp0to100(normDistance / Inp_FairValueNearThresholdATR * 30.0);
      g_minds[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("VWAP=%.3f price=%.3f dist=%.3f norm=%.2fATR state=AT_VALUE (below Inp_FairValueNearThresholdATR=%.2f) - too close to fair value for a directional opinion",
            vwap, currentPrice, distance, normDistance, Inp_FairValueNearThresholdATR);
      return;
     }

   // --- STAGE 4: VWAP SLOPE - a second, independent VWAP computed over the SAME session window
   // ending 1 bar earlier (SUPPORTING evidence only, never its own directional Mind).
   double slopeDir = 0.0; // -1/0/+1
   if(nFv >= 3)
     {
      double sumPV2 = 0.0, sumV2 = 0.0;
      for(int i = 1; i < nFv; i++) // same session window, shifted one bar back (excludes the newest bar)
        {
         double typical2 = (ratesFv[i].high + ratesFv[i].low + ratesFv[i].close) / 3.0;
         double vol2 = (double)ratesFv[i].tick_volume;
         sumPV2 += typical2 * vol2; sumV2 += vol2;
        }
      if(sumV2 > 0.0)
        {
         double vwapPrev = sumPV2 / sumV2;
         if(MathIsValidNumber(vwapPrev) && vwapPrev > 0.0)
           {
            double vwapDelta = vwap - vwapPrev;
            if(MathAbs(vwapDelta) > _Point) slopeDir = (vwapDelta > 0.0) ? 1.0 : -1.0;
           }
        }
     }
   string slopeLabel = (slopeDir > 0.0) ? "UP" : (slopeDir < 0.0) ? "DOWN" : "FLAT";

   // --- STAGE 5/6: ACCEPTANCE + REJECTION - over the last Inp_FairValueAcceptanceBars closed bars,
   // count how many closed on the SAME side of VWAP as `location` (acceptance) vs the OPPOSITE side
   // (crossing/rejection evidence). Uses THIS SAME vwap value as the reference for every bar in the
   // window (a single session VWAP level, not recomputed per-bar) - consistent with "acceptance of
   // THIS session's fair value", not a moving target.
   int acceptBars = MathMin(Inp_FairValueAcceptanceBars, nFv);
   int sameSideCount = 0, crossCount = 0;
   for(int i = 0; i < acceptBars; i++)
     {
      bool barAbove = ratesFv[i].close > vwap;
      bool sameSide = (location == LDIR_BUY) ? barAbove : !barAbove;
      if(sameSide) sameSideCount++; else crossCount++;
     }
   bool acceptanceConfirmed = (sameSideCount >= Inp_FairValueConfirmationBars);
   double acceptanceStrength = Clamp0to100((sameSideCount / (double)acceptBars) * 100.0);
   double persistence = acceptanceStrength; // stage 8 - reuses the same measure, not recalculated a second way

   // --- STAGE 7: EXTENSION.
   bool extended = (normDistance >= Inp_FairValueExtensionThresholdATR);

   // --- FINAL SCORE: transparent weighted sum, spec's own initial weights (section 14):
   // 30% location, 25% acceptance/rejection, 15% VWAP slope, 15% persistence, 15% extension
   // adjustment (a DAMPENER, subtracted, never added - "excessive extension should REDUCE
   // confidence", per explicit instruction, not contribute its own positive evidence).
   double locationContribution = Clamp0to100((normDistance / MathMax(Inp_FairValueExtensionThresholdATR, Inp_FairValueNearThresholdATR)) * 100.0) * 0.30;
   double acceptanceContribution = acceptanceStrength * 0.25;
   // slope contribution: full weight when slope agrees with location's own side, zero when flat, zero when it disagrees (never negative - disagreement is handled by requiring acceptance/persistence separately, not by penalizing here)
   double slopeAgrees = ((location == LDIR_BUY && slopeDir > 0.0) || (location == LDIR_SELL && slopeDir < 0.0));
   double slopeContribution = (slopeAgrees ? 100.0 : 0.0) * 0.15;
   double persistenceContribution = persistence * 0.15;
   double extensionAdjustment = extended ? -15.0 : 0.0; // full dampener weight (15%) removed when extended, not merely reduced - matches section 17's "should NOT blindly produce BUY"

   double rawScore = locationContribution + acceptanceContribution + slopeContribution + persistenceContribution + extensionAdjustment;
   double finalScore = Clamp0to100(rawScore);

   // Bullish/bearish evidence tally - explicit minimum directional separation (section 15) to avoid
   // noisy flips: acceptance MUST be confirmed (>= Inp_FairValueConfirmationBars same-side closes)
   // for a vote either way; an extended+unconfirmed reading NEVER votes, regardless of score.
   string stateLabel;
   if(!acceptanceConfirmed)
     {
      g_minds[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[slot].score = finalScore;
      stateLabel = "VALUE_CROSSING";
      g_minds[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("VWAP=%.3f price=%.3f dist=%.3f norm=%.2fATR slope=%s crossing=%d/%d acceptance=WEAK state=%s score=%.1f WAIT - repeated crossing with weak displacement, not real acceptance",
            vwap, currentPrice, distance, normDistance, slopeLabel, crossCount, acceptBars, stateLabel, finalScore);
      return;
     }
   if(extended && crossCount > 0)
     {
      // Extended AND showing any opposite-side closes in the recent window = rejection evidence at
      // the extreme, not confirmation - per section 17/30/31, this must NOT blindly continue the
      // extended side. WAIT rather than inventing a reversal direction without the SAME acceptance
      // confirmation the reversal side itself would need.
      g_minds[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[slot].score = finalScore;
      stateLabel = (location == LDIR_BUY) ? "EXTENDED_ABOVE" : "EXTENDED_BELOW";
      g_minds[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("VWAP=%.3f price=%.3f dist=%.3f norm=%.2fATR extension=HIGH rejection evidence present (crossing=%d/%d) state=%s score=%.1f WAIT - excessive extension without confirmed continuation",
            vwap, currentPrice, distance, normDistance, crossCount, acceptBars, stateLabel, finalScore);
      return;
     }

   ENUM_LITE_DIR voteDir = location; // acceptance confirmed, not (unconfirmed-)extended - value IS being accepted on this side
   stateLabel = (location == LDIR_BUY) ? "ACCEPTING_ABOVE" : "ACCEPTING_BELOW";
   g_minds[slot].direction = voteDir; g_minds[slot].score = finalScore;
   g_minds[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("VWAP=%.3f price=%.3f dist=%.3f norm=%.2fATR slope=%s acceptance=%d/%d persistence=%.1f extension=%s state=%s score=%.1f %s",
         vwap, currentPrice, distance, normDistance, slopeLabel, sameSideCount, acceptBars, persistence,
         extended ? "HIGH" : "NORMAL", stateLabel, finalScore, DirName(voteDir));
  }

//--- 2026-09-16, M5 PARALLEL PIPELINE: straight duplicate of EvaluateFairValueMind() above, writing
//--- g_mindsM5[17] (id 19) instead of g_minds[17] - its one internal PERIOD_M1 CopyRates call retargeted
//--- to PERIOD_M5. The session-window boundary (TimeCurrent()-based midnight) is timeframe-independent,
//--- reused verbatim. Everything else byte-identical.
void EvaluateFairValueMindM5()
  {
   const int slot = 17; // g_mindsM5[] array position for this Mind (id 19)
   g_mindsM5[slot].id = 19;
   g_mindsM5[slot].name = "Fair Value";

   if(!Inp_FairValueEnabled)
     {
      g_mindsM5[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = "Inp_FairValueEnabled=false";
      return;
     }
   if(Inp_FairValueLookback < 2 || Inp_FairValueMinSamples < 2 || Inp_FairValueMinSamples > Inp_FairValueLookback ||
      Inp_FairValueAcceptanceBars < 1 || Inp_FairValueConfirmationBars < 1 || Inp_FairValueConfirmationBars > Inp_FairValueAcceptanceBars)
     {
      g_mindsM5[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = "invalid Fair Value inputs";
      return;
     }

   MqlDateTime nowStruct;
   TimeToStruct(TimeCurrent(), nowStruct);
   nowStruct.hour = 0; nowStruct.min = 0; nowStruct.sec = 0;
   datetime sessionStart = StructToTime(nowStruct);

   MqlRates ratesFv[]; ArraySetAsSeries(ratesFv, true);
   int nFvRaw = CopyRates(g_symbol, PERIOD_M5, 1, Inp_FairValueLookback, ratesFv);
   if(nFvRaw < Inp_FairValueMinSamples)
     {
      g_mindsM5[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("insufficient closed-candle history (have=%d need>=%d)", nFvRaw, Inp_FairValueMinSamples);
      return;
     }

   int nFv = 0;
   while(nFv < nFvRaw && ratesFv[nFv].time >= sessionStart) nFv++;
   if(nFv < Inp_FairValueMinSamples)
     {
      g_mindsM5[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("insufficient TODAY-session history (have=%d need>=%d) - session started %s",
            nFv, Inp_FairValueMinSamples, DashIsoTime(sessionStart));
      return;
     }

   double sumPV = 0.0, sumV = 0.0;
   for(int i = 0; i < nFv; i++)
     {
      double typical = (ratesFv[i].high + ratesFv[i].low + ratesFv[i].close) / 3.0;
      double vol = (double)ratesFv[i].tick_volume;
      sumPV += typical * vol;
      sumV += vol;
     }
   if(!MathIsValidNumber(sumV) || sumV <= 0.0)
     {
      g_mindsM5[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = "zero/invalid session volume - cannot compute VWAP, refusing to fabricate one";
      return;
     }
   double vwap = sumPV / sumV;
   if(!MathIsValidNumber(vwap) || vwap <= 0.0)
     {
      g_mindsM5[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = "invalid VWAP result";
      return;
     }

   double currentPrice = ratesFv[0].close;

   const int atrPeriod = 14;
   double atr = 0.0; int atrSamples = 0;
   for(int i = 0; i < atrPeriod && (i+1) < nFv; i++)
     {
      double highLow = ratesFv[i].high - ratesFv[i].low;
      double highPrev = MathAbs(ratesFv[i].high - ratesFv[i+1].close);
      double lowPrev = MathAbs(ratesFv[i].low - ratesFv[i+1].close);
      atr += MathMax(highLow, MathMax(highPrev, lowPrev)); atrSamples++;
     }
   if(atrSamples > 0) atr /= atrSamples;
   if(atrSamples < 2 || !MathIsValidNumber(atr) || atr <= 0.0)
     {
      g_mindsM5[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("VWAP=%.3f price=%.3f but ATR invalid/unavailable (samples=%d atr=%.5f) - cannot normalize distance", vwap, currentPrice, atrSamples, atr);
      return;
     }

   double distance = currentPrice - vwap;
   double normDistance = SafeDiv(MathAbs(distance), atr, 0.0);
   ENUM_LITE_DIR location;
   if(normDistance < Inp_FairValueNearThresholdATR) location = LDIR_WAIT;
   else location = (distance > 0.0) ? LDIR_BUY : LDIR_SELL;

   if(location == LDIR_WAIT)
     {
      g_mindsM5[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[slot].score = Clamp0to100(normDistance / Inp_FairValueNearThresholdATR * 30.0);
      g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("VWAP=%.3f price=%.3f dist=%.3f norm=%.2fATR state=AT_VALUE (below Inp_FairValueNearThresholdATR=%.2f) - too close to fair value for a directional opinion",
            vwap, currentPrice, distance, normDistance, Inp_FairValueNearThresholdATR);
      return;
     }

   double slopeDir = 0.0;
   if(nFv >= 3)
     {
      double sumPV2 = 0.0, sumV2 = 0.0;
      for(int i = 1; i < nFv; i++)
        {
         double typical2 = (ratesFv[i].high + ratesFv[i].low + ratesFv[i].close) / 3.0;
         double vol2 = (double)ratesFv[i].tick_volume;
         sumPV2 += typical2 * vol2; sumV2 += vol2;
        }
      if(sumV2 > 0.0)
        {
         double vwapPrev = sumPV2 / sumV2;
         if(MathIsValidNumber(vwapPrev) && vwapPrev > 0.0)
           {
            double vwapDelta = vwap - vwapPrev;
            if(MathAbs(vwapDelta) > _Point) slopeDir = (vwapDelta > 0.0) ? 1.0 : -1.0;
           }
        }
     }
   string slopeLabel = (slopeDir > 0.0) ? "UP" : (slopeDir < 0.0) ? "DOWN" : "FLAT";

   int acceptBars = MathMin(Inp_FairValueAcceptanceBars, nFv);
   int sameSideCount = 0, crossCount = 0;
   for(int i = 0; i < acceptBars; i++)
     {
      bool barAbove = ratesFv[i].close > vwap;
      bool sameSide = (location == LDIR_BUY) ? barAbove : !barAbove;
      if(sameSide) sameSideCount++; else crossCount++;
     }
   bool acceptanceConfirmed = (sameSideCount >= Inp_FairValueConfirmationBars);
   double acceptanceStrength = Clamp0to100((sameSideCount / (double)acceptBars) * 100.0);
   double persistence = acceptanceStrength;

   bool extended = (normDistance >= Inp_FairValueExtensionThresholdATR);

   double locationContribution = Clamp0to100((normDistance / MathMax(Inp_FairValueExtensionThresholdATR, Inp_FairValueNearThresholdATR)) * 100.0) * 0.30;
   double acceptanceContribution = acceptanceStrength * 0.25;
   double slopeAgrees = ((location == LDIR_BUY && slopeDir > 0.0) || (location == LDIR_SELL && slopeDir < 0.0));
   double slopeContribution = (slopeAgrees ? 100.0 : 0.0) * 0.15;
   double persistenceContribution = persistence * 0.15;
   double extensionAdjustment = extended ? -15.0 : 0.0;

   double rawScore = locationContribution + acceptanceContribution + slopeContribution + persistenceContribution + extensionAdjustment;
   double finalScore = Clamp0to100(rawScore);

   string stateLabel;
   if(!acceptanceConfirmed)
     {
      g_mindsM5[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[slot].score = finalScore;
      stateLabel = "VALUE_CROSSING";
      g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("VWAP=%.3f price=%.3f dist=%.3f norm=%.2fATR slope=%s crossing=%d/%d acceptance=WEAK state=%s score=%.1f WAIT - repeated crossing with weak displacement, not real acceptance",
            vwap, currentPrice, distance, normDistance, slopeLabel, crossCount, acceptBars, stateLabel, finalScore);
      return;
     }
   if(extended && crossCount > 0)
     {
      g_mindsM5[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[slot].score = finalScore;
      stateLabel = (location == LDIR_BUY) ? "EXTENDED_ABOVE" : "EXTENDED_BELOW";
      g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("VWAP=%.3f price=%.3f dist=%.3f norm=%.2fATR extension=HIGH rejection evidence present (crossing=%d/%d) state=%s score=%.1f WAIT - excessive extension without confirmed continuation",
            vwap, currentPrice, distance, normDistance, crossCount, acceptBars, stateLabel, finalScore);
      return;
     }

   ENUM_LITE_DIR voteDir = location;
   stateLabel = (location == LDIR_BUY) ? "ACCEPTING_ABOVE" : "ACCEPTING_BELOW";
   g_mindsM5[slot].direction = voteDir; g_mindsM5[slot].score = finalScore;
   g_mindsM5[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("VWAP=%.3f price=%.3f dist=%.3f norm=%.2fATR slope=%s acceptance=%d/%d persistence=%.1f extension=%s state=%s score=%.1f %s",
         vwap, currentPrice, distance, normDistance, slopeLabel, sameSideCount, acceptBars, persistence,
         extended ? "HIGH" : "NORMAL", stateLabel, finalScore, DirName(voteDir));
  }

//--- 2026-09-23, M15 PARALLEL PIPELINE: straight duplicate of EvaluateFairValueMind()/EvaluateFairValueMindM5()
//--- above, writing g_mindsM15[17] (id 19) instead of g_minds[17]/g_mindsM5[17] - its one internal
//--- PERIOD_M1 CopyRates call retargeted to PERIOD_M15. The session-window boundary (TimeCurrent()-based
//--- midnight) is timeframe-independent, reused verbatim. Everything else byte-identical.
void EvaluateFairValueMindM15()
  {
   const int slot = 17; // g_mindsM15[] array position for this Mind (id 19)
   g_mindsM15[slot].id = 19;
   g_mindsM15[slot].name = "Fair Value";

   if(!Inp_FairValueEnabled)
     {
      g_mindsM15[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = "Inp_FairValueEnabled=false";
      return;
     }
   if(Inp_FairValueLookback < 2 || Inp_FairValueMinSamples < 2 || Inp_FairValueMinSamples > Inp_FairValueLookback ||
      Inp_FairValueAcceptanceBars < 1 || Inp_FairValueConfirmationBars < 1 || Inp_FairValueConfirmationBars > Inp_FairValueAcceptanceBars)
     {
      g_mindsM15[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = "invalid Fair Value inputs";
      return;
     }

   MqlDateTime nowStruct;
   TimeToStruct(TimeCurrent(), nowStruct);
   nowStruct.hour = 0; nowStruct.min = 0; nowStruct.sec = 0;
   datetime sessionStart = StructToTime(nowStruct);

   MqlRates ratesFv[]; ArraySetAsSeries(ratesFv, true);
   int nFvRaw = CopyRates(g_symbol, PERIOD_M15, 1, Inp_FairValueLookback, ratesFv);
   if(nFvRaw < Inp_FairValueMinSamples)
     {
      g_mindsM15[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("insufficient closed-candle history (have=%d need>=%d)", nFvRaw, Inp_FairValueMinSamples);
      return;
     }

   int nFv = 0;
   while(nFv < nFvRaw && ratesFv[nFv].time >= sessionStart) nFv++;
   if(nFv < Inp_FairValueMinSamples)
     {
      g_mindsM15[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("insufficient TODAY-session history (have=%d need>=%d) - session started %s",
            nFv, Inp_FairValueMinSamples, DashIsoTime(sessionStart));
      return;
     }

   double sumPV = 0.0, sumV = 0.0;
   for(int i = 0; i < nFv; i++)
     {
      double typical = (ratesFv[i].high + ratesFv[i].low + ratesFv[i].close) / 3.0;
      double vol = (double)ratesFv[i].tick_volume;
      sumPV += typical * vol;
      sumV += vol;
     }
   if(!MathIsValidNumber(sumV) || sumV <= 0.0)
     {
      g_mindsM15[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = "zero/invalid session volume - cannot compute VWAP, refusing to fabricate one";
      return;
     }
   double vwap = sumPV / sumV;
   if(!MathIsValidNumber(vwap) || vwap <= 0.0)
     {
      g_mindsM15[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = "invalid VWAP result";
      return;
     }

   double currentPrice = ratesFv[0].close;

   const int atrPeriod = 14;
   double atr = 0.0; int atrSamples = 0;
   for(int i = 0; i < atrPeriod && (i+1) < nFv; i++)
     {
      double highLow = ratesFv[i].high - ratesFv[i].low;
      double highPrev = MathAbs(ratesFv[i].high - ratesFv[i+1].close);
      double lowPrev = MathAbs(ratesFv[i].low - ratesFv[i+1].close);
      atr += MathMax(highLow, MathMax(highPrev, lowPrev)); atrSamples++;
     }
   if(atrSamples > 0) atr /= atrSamples;
   if(atrSamples < 2 || !MathIsValidNumber(atr) || atr <= 0.0)
     {
      g_mindsM15[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[slot].score = 0.0;
      g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("VWAP=%.3f price=%.3f but ATR invalid/unavailable (samples=%d atr=%.5f) - cannot normalize distance", vwap, currentPrice, atrSamples, atr);
      return;
     }

   double distance = currentPrice - vwap;
   double normDistance = SafeDiv(MathAbs(distance), atr, 0.0);
   ENUM_LITE_DIR location;
   if(normDistance < Inp_FairValueNearThresholdATR) location = LDIR_WAIT;
   else location = (distance > 0.0) ? LDIR_BUY : LDIR_SELL;

   if(location == LDIR_WAIT)
     {
      g_mindsM15[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[slot].score = Clamp0to100(normDistance / Inp_FairValueNearThresholdATR * 30.0);
      g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("VWAP=%.3f price=%.3f dist=%.3f norm=%.2fATR state=AT_VALUE (below Inp_FairValueNearThresholdATR=%.2f) - too close to fair value for a directional opinion",
            vwap, currentPrice, distance, normDistance, Inp_FairValueNearThresholdATR);
      return;
     }

   double slopeDir = 0.0;
   if(nFv >= 3)
     {
      double sumPV2 = 0.0, sumV2 = 0.0;
      for(int i = 1; i < nFv; i++)
        {
         double typical2 = (ratesFv[i].high + ratesFv[i].low + ratesFv[i].close) / 3.0;
         double vol2 = (double)ratesFv[i].tick_volume;
         sumPV2 += typical2 * vol2; sumV2 += vol2;
        }
      if(sumV2 > 0.0)
        {
         double vwapPrev = sumPV2 / sumV2;
         if(MathIsValidNumber(vwapPrev) && vwapPrev > 0.0)
           {
            double vwapDelta = vwap - vwapPrev;
            if(MathAbs(vwapDelta) > _Point) slopeDir = (vwapDelta > 0.0) ? 1.0 : -1.0;
           }
        }
     }
   string slopeLabel = (slopeDir > 0.0) ? "UP" : (slopeDir < 0.0) ? "DOWN" : "FLAT";

   int acceptBars = MathMin(Inp_FairValueAcceptanceBars, nFv);
   int sameSideCount = 0, crossCount = 0;
   for(int i = 0; i < acceptBars; i++)
     {
      bool barAbove = ratesFv[i].close > vwap;
      bool sameSide = (location == LDIR_BUY) ? barAbove : !barAbove;
      if(sameSide) sameSideCount++; else crossCount++;
     }
   bool acceptanceConfirmed = (sameSideCount >= Inp_FairValueConfirmationBars);
   double acceptanceStrength = Clamp0to100((sameSideCount / (double)acceptBars) * 100.0);
   double persistence = acceptanceStrength;

   bool extended = (normDistance >= Inp_FairValueExtensionThresholdATR);

   double locationContribution = Clamp0to100((normDistance / MathMax(Inp_FairValueExtensionThresholdATR, Inp_FairValueNearThresholdATR)) * 100.0) * 0.30;
   double acceptanceContribution = acceptanceStrength * 0.25;
   double slopeAgrees = ((location == LDIR_BUY && slopeDir > 0.0) || (location == LDIR_SELL && slopeDir < 0.0));
   double slopeContribution = (slopeAgrees ? 100.0 : 0.0) * 0.15;
   double persistenceContribution = persistence * 0.15;
   double extensionAdjustment = extended ? -15.0 : 0.0;

   double rawScore = locationContribution + acceptanceContribution + slopeContribution + persistenceContribution + extensionAdjustment;
   double finalScore = Clamp0to100(rawScore);

   string stateLabel;
   if(!acceptanceConfirmed)
     {
      g_mindsM15[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[slot].score = finalScore;
      stateLabel = "VALUE_CROSSING";
      g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("VWAP=%.3f price=%.3f dist=%.3f norm=%.2fATR slope=%s crossing=%d/%d acceptance=WEAK state=%s score=%.1f WAIT - repeated crossing with weak displacement, not real acceptance",
            vwap, currentPrice, distance, normDistance, slopeLabel, crossCount, acceptBars, stateLabel, finalScore);
      return;
     }
   if(extended && crossCount > 0)
     {
      g_mindsM15[slot].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[slot].score = finalScore;
      stateLabel = (location == LDIR_BUY) ? "EXTENDED_ABOVE" : "EXTENDED_BELOW";
      g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("VWAP=%.3f price=%.3f dist=%.3f norm=%.2fATR extension=HIGH rejection evidence present (crossing=%d/%d) state=%s score=%.1f WAIT - excessive extension without confirmed continuation",
            vwap, currentPrice, distance, normDistance, crossCount, acceptBars, stateLabel, finalScore);
      return;
     }

   ENUM_LITE_DIR voteDir = location;
   stateLabel = (location == LDIR_BUY) ? "ACCEPTING_ABOVE" : "ACCEPTING_BELOW";
   g_mindsM15[slot].direction = voteDir; g_mindsM15[slot].score = finalScore;
   g_mindsM15[slot].reasoning = StringFormat("VWAP=%.3f price=%.3f dist=%.3f norm=%.2fATR slope=%s acceptance=%d/%d persistence=%.1f extension=%s state=%s score=%.1f %s",
         vwap, currentPrice, distance, normDistance, slopeLabel, sameSideCount, acceptBars, persistence,
         extended ? "HIGH" : "NORMAL", stateLabel, finalScore, DirName(voteDir));
  }

//--- 2026-09-01, explicit operator request (SESSION MIND IMPLEMENTATION): resolves the CURRENTLY
//--- active session (or manual override) into a start-of-window datetime, using the EXACT SAME
//--- UTC-hour boundaries as the dashboard's own _active_sessions_for() (Gold Trading
//--- Dashboard/app/main.py) - Sydney 22-07, Tokyo 00-09, London 08-17, New York 13-22 - so the label
//--- this Mind reasons about matches what the operator already sees on the Trade History table.
//--- Overlap windows (e.g. "TOKYO/LONDON") are resolved to whichever SINGLE session most recently
//--- started (the tighter/more specific window), since a session's OWN candle history needs one
//--- concrete start time, not two - never ambiguous. Server/broker time (TimeCurrent()) is used
//--- directly as UTC per this file's existing convention elsewhere (DashIsoTime() etc. do the same).
//--- 2026-09-01, explicit operator request (PER-SESSION DNA + MIND SELECTION): extracted from
//--- ResolveSessionStart()'s own original body (no logic changed, purely a refactor so both that
//--- function AND the new IsRegimeAllowedForSession()/IsMindAllowedForSession() below share ONE
//--- session-label detection, never two independently-maintained copies of the same UTC-hour table).
string ResolveCurrentSessionLabel()
  {
   if(Inp_SessionMode==SESSION_MANUAL)
     {
      switch(Inp_SessionManualChoice)
        {
         case SESSION_M_LONDON:         return "LONDON";
         case SESSION_M_LONDON_NEWYORK: return "LONDON/NEW YORK";
         case SESSION_M_NEWYORK:        return "NEW YORK";
         case SESSION_M_SYDNEY:         return "SYDNEY";
         case SESSION_M_SYDNEY_TOKYO:   return "SYDNEY/TOKYO";
         case SESSION_M_TOKYO:          return "TOKYO";
         case SESSION_M_TOKYO_LONDON:   return "TOKYO/LONDON";
         default:                       return "LONDON";
        }
     }

   //--- AUTO mode - same UTC-hour boundaries as the dashboard's _active_sessions_for(), evaluated in
   //--- most-specific-overlap-first order so the label matches exactly what the dashboard would show
   //--- for this same moment.
   MqlDateTime nowS; TimeToStruct(TimeCurrent(), nowS);
   int h = nowS.hour;
   bool sydney  = (h>=22 || h<7);
   bool tokyo   = (h>=0 && h<9);
   bool london  = (h>=8 && h<17);
   bool newyork = (h>=13 && h<22);

   if(sydney && tokyo)        return "SYDNEY/TOKYO";
   if(tokyo && london)        return "TOKYO/LONDON";
   if(london && newyork)      return "LONDON/NEW YORK";
   if(sydney)                 return "SYDNEY";
   if(tokyo)                  return "TOKYO";
   if(london)                 return "LONDON";
   if(newyork)                return "NEW YORK";
   return "UNKNOWN"; // should be unreachable - every UTC hour falls in >=1 window above
  }

datetime ResolveSessionStart(string &outLabel)
  {
   outLabel = ResolveCurrentSessionLabel();

   if(Inp_SessionMode==SESSION_MANUAL)
     {
      // Manual override: the actual candle window still needs a real start time, so manual mode uses
      // "since today's server-time midnight" as its window, exactly like Fair Value's own SESSION
      // WINDOW convention - a deliberate, documented choice, never a fabricated session-specific
      // history the broker/server clock doesn't actually support.
      MqlDateTime mstruct; TimeToStruct(TimeCurrent(), mstruct);
      mstruct.hour=0; mstruct.min=0; mstruct.sec=0;
      return StructToTime(mstruct);
     }

   //--- AUTO mode - re-derive the same boundaries (cheap, avoids a second output parameter on
   //--- ResolveCurrentSessionLabel() just to pass startHour back) to build the actual window start.
   MqlDateTime nowS; TimeToStruct(TimeCurrent(), nowS);
   int h = nowS.hour;
   bool sydney  = (h>=22 || h<7);
   bool tokyo   = (h>=0 && h<9);
   bool london  = (h>=8 && h<17);
   bool newyork = (h>=13 && h<22);

   int startHour;
   if(sydney && tokyo)       startHour=0;
   else if(tokyo && london)  startHour=8;  // narrower of the two starts
   else if(london && newyork)startHour=13;
   else if(sydney)           startHour=22;
   else if(tokyo)            startHour=0;
   else if(london)           startHour=8;
   else if(newyork)          startHour=13;
   else                      startHour=h; // should be unreachable

   MqlDateTime startS = nowS;
   startS.hour=startHour; startS.min=0; startS.sec=0;
   datetime sessionStart = StructToTime(startS);
   //--- Sydney (22-07) wraps past midnight - if the session's start hour (22) is LATER than the
   //--- current hour, the session actually began YESTERDAY (server date), not today.
   if(startHour>h) sessionStart -= 86400;
   return sessionStart;
  }

//--- 2026-09-01, explicit operator request (PER-SESSION DNA + MIND SELECTION): maps the current
//--- session label to its own pair of CSV input strings. One choke point so
//--- IsRegimeAllowedForSession()/IsMindAllowedForSession() below never duplicate this mapping.
void ResolveSessionCsvInputs(const string sessionLabel, string &outDnaCsv, string &outMindsCsv)
  {
   if(sessionLabel=="SYDNEY")            { outDnaCsv=Inp_SessionDna_Sydney;          outMindsCsv=Inp_SessionMinds_Sydney;          return; }
   if(sessionLabel=="SYDNEY/TOKYO")      { outDnaCsv=Inp_SessionDna_SydneyTokyo;     outMindsCsv=Inp_SessionMinds_SydneyTokyo;     return; }
   if(sessionLabel=="TOKYO")             { outDnaCsv=Inp_SessionDna_Tokyo;           outMindsCsv=Inp_SessionMinds_Tokyo;           return; }
   if(sessionLabel=="TOKYO/LONDON")      { outDnaCsv=Inp_SessionDna_TokyoLondon;     outMindsCsv=Inp_SessionMinds_TokyoLondon;     return; }
   if(sessionLabel=="LONDON")            { outDnaCsv=Inp_SessionDna_London;          outMindsCsv=Inp_SessionMinds_London;          return; }
   if(sessionLabel=="LONDON/NEW YORK")   { outDnaCsv=Inp_SessionDna_LondonNewYork;   outMindsCsv=Inp_SessionMinds_LondonNewYork;   return; }
   if(sessionLabel=="NEW YORK")          { outDnaCsv=Inp_SessionDna_NewYork;         outMindsCsv=Inp_SessionMinds_NewYork;         return; }
   // "UNKNOWN" (should be unreachable) or any unrecognized label - no restriction, never blocks.
   outDnaCsv=""; outMindsCsv="";
  }

//--- 2026-09-01, explicit operator request (PER-SESSION BAR-COUNT / LOOKBACK WINDOW): maps the
//--- current session label to its own pair of bar-count inputs - same one-choke-point pattern as
//--- ResolveSessionCsvInputs() above, never a second/duplicated mapping.
void ResolveSessionBarInputs(const string sessionLabel, int &outDnaBars, int &outMindsBars)
  {
   if(sessionLabel=="SYDNEY")            { outDnaBars=Inp_SessionBarsDna_Sydney;          outMindsBars=Inp_SessionBarsMinds_Sydney;          return; }
   if(sessionLabel=="SYDNEY/TOKYO")      { outDnaBars=Inp_SessionBarsDna_SydneyTokyo;     outMindsBars=Inp_SessionBarsMinds_SydneyTokyo;     return; }
   if(sessionLabel=="TOKYO")             { outDnaBars=Inp_SessionBarsDna_Tokyo;           outMindsBars=Inp_SessionBarsMinds_Tokyo;           return; }
   if(sessionLabel=="TOKYO/LONDON")      { outDnaBars=Inp_SessionBarsDna_TokyoLondon;     outMindsBars=Inp_SessionBarsMinds_TokyoLondon;     return; }
   if(sessionLabel=="LONDON")            { outDnaBars=Inp_SessionBarsDna_London;          outMindsBars=Inp_SessionBarsMinds_London;          return; }
   if(sessionLabel=="LONDON/NEW YORK")   { outDnaBars=Inp_SessionBarsDna_LondonNewYork;   outMindsBars=Inp_SessionBarsMinds_LondonNewYork;   return; }
   if(sessionLabel=="NEW YORK")          { outDnaBars=Inp_SessionBarsDna_NewYork;         outMindsBars=Inp_SessionBarsMinds_NewYork;         return; }
   // "UNKNOWN" (should be unreachable) or any unrecognized label - 0/0 so the caller's own fallback
   // to the global Inp_MarketDNALookbackCandles/Inp_M1LookbackBars kicks in, never blocks/zeroes out.
   outDnaBars=0; outMindsBars=0;
  }

//--- 2026-09-01, explicit operator request (PER-SESSION BAR-COUNT / LOOKBACK WINDOW): the effective
//--- Market DNA lookback for THIS cycle - the current session's own Inp_SessionBarsDna_* value if
//--- >0, else Inp_MarketDNALookbackCandles unchanged (0 = explicit "use global default", per
//--- explicit operator confirmation). Called from OnTick() (to size the CopyRates fetch) AND from
//--- EvaluateMarketDNA() (to compute k) - the SAME resolved value both places, never two independent
//--- reads that could disagree mid-cycle.
int ResolveEffectiveDnaLookback()
  {
   string label = ResolveCurrentSessionLabel();
   int dnaBars=0, mindsBars=0;
   ResolveSessionBarInputs(label, dnaBars, mindsBars);
   return (dnaBars>0) ? dnaBars : Inp_MarketDNALookbackCandles;
  }

//--- 2026-09-01, explicit operator request (PER-SESSION BAR-COUNT / LOOKBACK WINDOW): the effective
//--- shared Minds pool size for THIS cycle - same fallback convention as
//--- ResolveEffectiveDnaLookback() above. This controls ONLY the CopyRates() fetch size in OnTick()
//--- (see that function's own header on this input's exact scope) - it does NOT alter any individual
//--- Mind's own dedicated/independently-calibrated window (Trend/Memory/Fair Value/Session/SR/etc.).
int ResolveEffectiveMindsLookback()
  {
   string label = ResolveCurrentSessionLabel();
   int dnaBars=0, mindsBars=0;
   ResolveSessionBarInputs(label, dnaBars, mindsBars);
   return (mindsBars>0) ? mindsBars : Inp_M1LookbackBars;
  }

//--- 2026-09-01, explicit operator request (PER-SESSION DNA + MIND SELECTION): generic "is TOKEN
//--- present in this comma-separated list" check - trims whitespace around each comma-separated
//--- entry so "UPTREND, PULLBACK" and "UPTREND,PULLBACK" behave identically (operator-typed CSV,
//--- never assume perfectly clean formatting). Blank csv = true (no restriction) - the SAME
//--- convention both IsRegimeAllowedForSession() and IsMindAllowedForSession() below rely on.
bool CsvContainsToken(const string csv, const string token)
  {
   if(StringLen(csv)==0) return true; // blank = no restriction, per explicit operator confirmation
   string parts[];
   int cnt = StringSplit(csv, ',', parts);
   for(int i=0; i<cnt; i++)
     {
      string p = parts[i];
      StringTrimLeft(p); StringTrimRight(p);
      if(p==token) return true;
     }
   return false;
  }

//--- 2026-09-01, explicit operator request (PER-SESSION DNA + MIND SELECTION): the DNA-side check,
//--- consulted from CurrentRegimeAllowed() below - ADDITIVE to that function's own existing
//--- Inp_Allow_<State> switch (never a replacement, per explicit operator confirmation). Matches by
//--- the state's own DnaName() string, the SAME name DnaFromName() already parses elsewhere in this
//--- file - never a second, inconsistent naming scheme.
bool IsRegimeAllowedForSession(const ENUM_LITE_DNA state)
  {
   string label = ResolveCurrentSessionLabel();
   string dnaCsv, mindsCsv;
   ResolveSessionCsvInputs(label, dnaCsv, mindsCsv);
   return CsvContainsToken(dnaCsv, DnaName(state));
  }

//--- 2026-09-01, explicit operator request (PER-SESSION DNA + MIND SELECTION): the Mind-side check,
//--- consulted from EvaluateMinds()'s own existing vote-tally loop - ADDITIVE to each Mind's own
//--- existing Inp_<Mind>Enabled toggle where one exists (never a replacement, per explicit operator
//--- confirmation). Matches by the Mind's HISTORICAL id (mindId - g_minds[i].id, the SAME convention
//--- MindIsVoting()/MindCandleBasis() already key on), never array position.
bool IsMindAllowedForSession(const int mindId)
  {
   string label = ResolveCurrentSessionLabel();
   string dnaCsv, mindsCsv;
   ResolveSessionCsvInputs(label, dnaCsv, mindsCsv);
   return CsvContainsToken(mindsCsv, IntegerToString(mindId));
  }

void EvaluateMinds(const MqlRates &rates[], const int n, const RawFeatures &f)
  {
   double pointsScale = 1.0/_Point;

   //--- 2026-08-21, explicit operator request: Liquidity and Memory now read a dedicated 30-bar
   //--- window, independent of the shared pool (Inp_M1LookbackBars) every other Mind uses. Fetched
   //--- once here, reused by both.
   MqlRates rates30[]; ArraySetAsSeries(rates30, true);
   int n30 = CopyRates(g_symbol, PERIOD_M1, 1, 30, rates30);

   //--- 2026-08-28, explicit operator request: Trend widened from the shared pool's f.longSlope to a
   //--- dedicated 30-bar window (rates30, already fetched above for Liquidity/Memory) - was effectively
   //--- reading a 100-bar span via the live Inputs-tab value of Inp_M1LookbackBars, operator wants Trend
   //--- specifically narrowed to 30 without touching the other 8 Minds still sharing that pool.
   //--- Same formula/scale as before (netMove over the window, pointsScale/300*100) - only the window changed.
   g_minds[0].id=0; g_minds[0].name="Trend";
   if(n30>=2)
     {
      double longSlope30 = rates30[0].close - rates30[n30-1].close;
      g_minds[0].direction = SignOf(longSlope30);
      g_minds[0].score = Clamp0to100(MathAbs(longSlope30)*pointsScale/300.0*100.0);
      g_minds[0].reasoning = StringFormat("longSlope30=%.5f (n30=%d)", longSlope30, n30);
     }
   else { g_minds[0].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[0].score=0.0; g_minds[0].reasoning="insufficient 30-bar history"; }

   g_minds[1].id=1; g_minds[1].name="Momentum";
   g_minds[1].direction = SignOf(f.shortSlope);
   g_minds[1].score = Clamp0to100(MathAbs(f.shortSlope)*pointsScale/150.0*100.0);
   g_minds[1].reasoning = StringFormat("shortSlope=%.5f", f.shortSlope);

   //--- 2026-08-21, explicit operator request: Scalping widened from 1 bar to 3 bars. Direction =
   //--- same consistency read as the M1 3-Bar system (2 step-comparisons across 3 closes); score =
   //--- average body% conviction across those same 3 candles.
   g_minds[2].id=2; g_minds[2].name="Scalping";
   if(n>=3)
     {
      double sumBody3=0; int up3=0, down3=0;
      for(int q=0;q<3;q++)
        {
         double rg=rates[q].high-rates[q].low; if(rg<=0.0) rg=_Point;
         sumBody3 += MathAbs(rates[q].close-rates[q].open)/rg*100.0;
        }
      for(int q=0;q<2;q++) { if(rates[q].close>rates[q+1].close) up3++; else if(rates[q].close<rates[q+1].close) down3++; }
      double agreement3 = 0.5+0.5*((up3-down3)/2.0);
      g_minds[2].direction = (agreement3>0.5)?LDIR_BUY:(agreement3<0.5?LDIR_SELL:LDIR_WAIT);
      g_minds[2].score = Clamp0to100(sumBody3/3.0);
      g_minds[2].reasoning = StringFormat("avgBody3=%.1f agreement3=%.2f", sumBody3/3.0, agreement3);
     }
   else { g_minds[2].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[2].score=0.0; g_minds[2].reasoning="insufficient bars"; }

   //--- 2026-08-21, explicit operator request: Reversal widened from 1 bar to 3 bars. Uses the
   //--- AVERAGE upper/lower wick% across the last 3 candles instead of just the newest one's.
   g_minds[3].id=3; g_minds[3].name="Reversal";
   if(n>=3)
     {
      double sumUpper3=0, sumLower3=0;
      for(int q=0;q<3;q++)
        {
         double rg=rates[q].high-rates[q].low; if(rg<=0.0) rg=_Point;
         sumUpper3 += (rates[q].high-MathMax(rates[q].open,rates[q].close))/rg*100.0;
         sumLower3 += (MathMin(rates[q].open,rates[q].close)-rates[q].low)/rg*100.0;
        }
      double avgUpper3=sumUpper3/3.0, avgLower3=sumLower3/3.0;
      g_minds[3].direction = (avgUpper3>avgLower3) ? LDIR_SELL : (avgLower3>avgUpper3 ? LDIR_BUY : LDIR_WAIT);
      g_minds[3].score = Clamp0to100(MathMax(avgUpper3,avgLower3));
      g_minds[3].reasoning = StringFormat("avgUpperWick3%%=%.1f avgLowerWick3%%=%.1f", avgUpper3, avgLower3);
     }
   else { g_minds[3].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[3].score=0.0; g_minds[3].reasoning="insufficient bars"; }

   //--- 2026-08-21, explicit operator request: Liquidity widened from the shared pool to a
   //--- dedicated 30-bar window (rates30, fetched at the top of this function).
   g_minds[4].id=4; g_minds[4].name="Liquidity";
   if(n30>=2)
     {
      double hh30=rates30[0].high, ll30=rates30[0].low;
      for(int q=1;q<n30;q++) { if(rates30[q].high>hh30) hh30=rates30[q].high; if(rates30[q].low<ll30) ll30=rates30[q].low; }
      double span30 = MathMax(hh30-ll30, _Point);
      double distFromHigh30 = (hh30-rates30[0].close)/span30*100.0;
      double distFromLow30  = (rates30[0].close-ll30)/span30*100.0;
      g_minds[4].direction = (distFromHigh30<distFromLow30) ? LDIR_SELL : (distFromLow30<distFromHigh30 ? LDIR_BUY : LDIR_WAIT);
      g_minds[4].score = Clamp0to100(100.0-MathMin(distFromHigh30,distFromLow30));
      g_minds[4].reasoning = StringFormat("distFromHigh30%%=%.1f distFromLow30%%=%.1f (n30=%d)", distFromHigh30, distFromLow30, n30);
     }
   else { g_minds[4].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[4].score=0.0; g_minds[4].reasoning="insufficient 30-bar history"; }

   //--- 2026-08-29, explicit operator request: Risk (historical #5) COMPLETELY REMOVED from the active
   //--- Mind architecture - it was hardcoded LDIR_WAIT always and never voted a side, providing zero
   //--- directional information. This block (volRatio/netMove5 over the last 5 bars) is still needed
   //--- by Volatility immediately below, so the SHARED computation stays - only Risk's own
   //--- name/direction/score/reasoning assignment (the actual "Mind" it fed) is gone. Array position 5
   //--- is now Volatility (historical id=6) - see g_minds[5].id=6; a few lines below.
   int cnt5 = MathMin(5, n);
   double sumRange5=0;
   for(int q=0;q<cnt5;q++) { double rg=rates[q].high-rates[q].low; if(rg<=0.0) rg=_Point; sumRange5+=rg; }
   double avgRange5 = sumRange5/cnt5;
   double volRatio = avgRange5/MathMax(f.avgRange,_Point);
   double netMove5 = rates[0].close - rates[cnt5-1].close;

   g_minds[5].id=6; g_minds[5].name="Volatility";
   g_minds[5].direction = (volRatio>1.2) ? SignOf(netMove5) : LDIR_WAIT;
   g_minds[5].score = Clamp0to100((volRatio-1.0)*100.0);
   g_minds[5].reasoning = StringFormat("volRatio(5vsPool)=%.2f", volRatio);

   g_minds[6].id=7; g_minds[6].name="Structure";
   g_minds[6].direction = SignOf((double)(f.ups-f.downs));
   g_minds[6].score = Clamp0to100(MathAbs(f.ups-f.downs)*(100.0/n));
   g_minds[6].reasoning = StringFormat("ups=%d downs=%d", f.ups, f.downs);

   //--- 2026-08-21, explicit operator request: Memory widened from the shared pool's netMove to a
   //--- dedicated 30-bar netMove (rates30). Still cross-cycle - compares THIS cycle's 30-bar read
   //--- against the PREVIOUS cycle's 30-bar read (g_prevNetMove, updated at the end of OnTick()).
   g_minds[7].id=8; g_minds[7].name="Memory";
   if(n30>=2)
     {
      g_curNetMove30 = rates30[0].close - rates30[n30-1].close;
      ENUM_LITE_DIR prevDir30 = SignOf(g_prevNetMove);
      ENUM_LITE_DIR curDir30  = SignOf(g_curNetMove30);
      g_minds[7].direction = (prevDir30==curDir30 && curDir30!=LDIR_WAIT) ? curDir30 : LDIR_WAIT;
      g_minds[7].score = (prevDir30==curDir30 && curDir30!=LDIR_WAIT) ? 60.0 : 20.0;
      g_minds[7].reasoning = StringFormat("prevNetMove30=%.5f curNetMove30=%.5f (n30=%d)", g_prevNetMove, g_curNetMove30, n30);
     }
   else { g_minds[7].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[7].score=0.0; g_minds[7].reasoning="insufficient 30-bar history"; }

   //--- 2026-08-21, explicit operator request: Pattern widened from a 2-bar engulfing check to a
   //--- 3-bar reversal check - the two OLDER candles must both agree on one direction, then the
   //--- newest candle reverses AND closes beyond both their combined high/low.
   //--- 2026-08-21, explicit operator request: Pattern widened from checking a single 3-bar shape
   //--- to scanning a dedicated window for every occurrence of that same 3-bar reversal shape (two
   //--- prior candles agree, the third reverses and closes beyond their combined range), then voting
   //--- the side with more occurrences. Score = how lopsided the bull/bear count is.
   //--- 2026-08-28, explicit operator request: window narrowed 60->30. Same formula, same array/var
   //--- names reused (rates60/n60) to avoid a mechanical rename churn - only the CopyRates count changed.
   MqlRates rates60[]; ArraySetAsSeries(rates60, true);
   int n60 = CopyRates(g_symbol, PERIOD_M1, 1, 30, rates60);
   g_minds[8].id=9; g_minds[8].name="Pattern";
   if(n60>=3)
     {
      int bullCount=0, bearCount=0;
      for(int i=0; i<=n60-3; i++)
        {
         bool priorTwoDown = (rates60[i+1].close<rates60[i+1].open) && (rates60[i+2].close<rates60[i+2].open);
         bool priorTwoUp   = (rates60[i+1].close>rates60[i+1].open) && (rates60[i+2].close>rates60[i+2].open);
         double maxPriorHigh = MathMax(rates60[i+1].high, rates60[i+2].high);
         double minPriorLow  = MathMin(rates60[i+1].low, rates60[i+2].low);
         if(priorTwoDown && (rates60[i].close>rates60[i].open) && (rates60[i].close>maxPriorHigh)) bullCount++;
         if(priorTwoUp   && (rates60[i].close<rates60[i].open) && (rates60[i].close<minPriorLow))  bearCount++;
        }
      g_minds[8].direction = (bullCount>bearCount) ? LDIR_BUY : (bearCount>bullCount ? LDIR_SELL : LDIR_WAIT);
      g_minds[8].score = Clamp0to100(MathAbs(bullCount-bearCount)*(100.0/MathMax(1,bullCount+bearCount)));
      g_minds[8].reasoning = StringFormat("3-bar reversal patterns over 30: bull=%d bear=%d", bullCount, bearCount);
     }
   else { g_minds[8].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[8].score=0.0; g_minds[8].reasoning="insufficient 30-bar history"; }

   //--- 2026-08-29, explicit operator request: Pressure (historical #10) COMPLETELY REMOVED from the
   //--- active Mind architecture - the Mind-to-Mind duplicate audit found it byte-for-byte identical
   //--- to Structure (historical #7, now array position 6): same SignOf(ups-downs) direction, same
   //--- Clamp0to100(|ups-downs|*100/n) score, same shared-pool inputs, zero informational difference.
   //--- Previously converted to an inert placeholder (2026-08-28); THIS task supersedes that with a
   //--- genuine removal per explicit instruction. Array position 9 is now Energy (historical id=11).
   g_minds[9].id=11; g_minds[9].name="Energy";
   g_minds[9].direction = SignOf(f.netMove);
   g_minds[9].score = Clamp0to100(f.avgBodyPct);
   g_minds[9].reasoning = StringFormat("avgBodyPct=%.1f", f.avgBodyPct);

   //--- 2026-08-21, explicit operator request: Breakout widened from "1 vs N" to "2 vs N" - the
   //--- newest 2 candles' combined high/low compared against the REST of the pool (indices 2..n-1),
   //--- instead of just the single newest candle against indices 1..n-1.
   g_minds[10].id=12; g_minds[10].name="Breakout";
   if(n>=3)
     {
      double newest2High = MathMax(rates[0].high, rates[1].high);
      double newest2Low  = MathMin(rates[0].low,  rates[1].low);
      double priorHigh2=-DBL_MAX, priorLow2=DBL_MAX;
      for(int q=2; q<n; q++) { if(rates[q].high>priorHigh2) priorHigh2=rates[q].high; if(rates[q].low<priorLow2) priorLow2=rates[q].low; }

      if(newest2High>priorHigh2)      { g_minds[10].direction=LDIR_BUY;  g_minds[10].score=80.0; g_minds[10].reasoning="new high (2-bar) vs prior window"; }
      else if(newest2Low<priorLow2)   { g_minds[10].direction=LDIR_SELL; g_minds[10].score=80.0; g_minds[10].reasoning="new low (2-bar) vs prior window"; }
      else                             { g_minds[10].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[10].score=15.0; g_minds[10].reasoning="inside prior window"; }
     }
   else { g_minds[10].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[10].score=0.0; g_minds[10].reasoning="insufficient bars"; }

   //--- 2026-09-01, explicit operator request (SESSION MIND IMPLEMENTATION): REPLACES the prior
   //--- always-WAIT placeholder. Identifies the currently active session (auto-detected from server
   //--- time, or Inp_SessionManualChoice if Inp_SessionMode=MANUAL - see ResolveSessionStart()'s own
   //--- header), then votes with THAT session's own net directional move (close of newest closed bar
   //--- minus close of the oldest bar still within the session window), normalized by the SAME
   //--- classic-14-period ATR technique EMA Trend/Fair Value already use - never a second, competing
   //--- volatility measure. Reuses rates[]/n, the SAME closed-candle series every other Mind in this
   //--- function already reads - never a second CopyRates() call.
   g_minds[11].id=13; g_minds[11].name="Session";
   if(!Inp_SessionMindEnabled)
     {
      g_minds[11].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[11].score = 0.0;
      g_minds[11].reasoning = "Inp_SessionMindEnabled=false";
     }
   else
     {
      string sessionLabel = "";
      datetime sessionStart = ResolveSessionStart(sessionLabel);

      int nSess = 0;
      while(nSess<n && rates[nSess].time>=sessionStart) nSess++;

      if(nSess < Inp_SessionMinSamples)
        {
         g_minds[11].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[11].score = 0.0;
         g_minds[11].reasoning = StringFormat("session=%s insufficient session-so-far history (have=%d need>=%d, start=%s)",
               sessionLabel, nSess, Inp_SessionMinSamples, DashIsoTime(sessionStart));
        }
      else
        {
         double sessionNetMove = rates[0].close - rates[nSess-1].close;

         const int sessAtrPeriod = 14;
         double sessAtr = 0.0; int sessAtrSamples = 0;
         for(int si=0; si<sessAtrPeriod && (si+1)<n; si++)
           {
            double hl = rates[si].high - rates[si].low;
            double hp = MathAbs(rates[si].high - rates[si+1].close);
            double lp = MathAbs(rates[si].low  - rates[si+1].close);
            sessAtr += MathMax(hl, MathMax(hp,lp)); sessAtrSamples++;
           }
         if(sessAtrSamples>0) sessAtr /= sessAtrSamples;

         if(sessAtrSamples<2 || !MathIsValidNumber(sessAtr) || sessAtr<=0.0)
           {
            g_minds[11].direction = LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[11].score = 0.0;
            g_minds[11].reasoning = StringFormat("session=%s netMove=%.5f but ATR invalid/unavailable (samples=%d) - cannot normalize",
                  sessionLabel, sessionNetMove, sessAtrSamples);
           }
         else
           {
            double normMove = SafeDiv(MathAbs(sessionNetMove), sessAtr, 0.0);
            if(normMove < Inp_SessionNearThresholdATR)
              {
               g_minds[11].direction = LDIR_WAIT;
               g_minds[11].score = Clamp0to100(normMove / Inp_SessionNearThresholdATR * 25.0);
               g_minds[11].reasoning = StringFormat("session=%s netMove=%.5f norm=%.2fATR (below Inp_SessionNearThresholdATR=%.2f) - too flat for a directional opinion this session",
                     sessionLabel, sessionNetMove, normMove, Inp_SessionNearThresholdATR);
              }
            else
              {
               g_minds[11].direction = SignOf(sessionNetMove);
               g_minds[11].score = Clamp0to100(normMove * 35.0);
               g_minds[11].reasoning = StringFormat("session=%s bars=%d netMove=%.5f norm=%.2fATR %s",
                     sessionLabel, nSess, sessionNetMove, normMove, DirName(g_minds[11].direction));
              }
           }
        }
     }

   g_minds[12].id=14; g_minds[12].name="Consensus";
   g_minds[12].direction = SignOf(f.netMove);
   g_minds[12].score = Clamp0to100(MathAbs(f.netMove)*pointsScale/300.0*100.0);
   g_minds[12].reasoning = StringFormat("netMove=%.5f", f.netMove);

   //--- 2026-08-21, explicit operator request: 16th Mind - Support/Resistance, dedicated 60-bar
   //--- window (originally 1440 to match the real KMIE Structure Builder's own full trading-day
   //--- window, adjusted to 720 the same day). Detects swing highs/lows via a classic 5-bar fractal
   //--- (a bar is a swing high/low if it's the extreme of itself + 2 bars on each side), finds the
   //--- nearest swing-high ABOVE current close (resistance) and nearest swing-low BELOW it
   //--- (support), then votes toward whichever level price sits closer to - close to support
   //--- implies a bounce (BUY), close to resistance implies rejection (SELL).
   MqlRates rates60sr[]; ArraySetAsSeries(rates60sr, true);
   int n60sr = CopyRates(g_symbol, PERIOD_M1, 1, 720, rates60sr);
   g_minds[13].id=15; g_minds[13].name="SR";
   if(n60sr>=10)
     {
      double curClose = rates60sr[0].close;
      double nearestResistance=-1.0, nearestSupport=-1.0;
      int fh=2; // fractal half-width - 2 bars each side = classic 5-bar fractal
      for(int i=fh; i<n60sr-fh; i++)
        {
         bool isSwingHigh=true, isSwingLow=true;
         for(int w=1; w<=fh; w++)
           {
            if(rates60sr[i].high<=rates60sr[i-w].high || rates60sr[i].high<=rates60sr[i+w].high) isSwingHigh=false;
            if(rates60sr[i].low>=rates60sr[i-w].low   || rates60sr[i].low>=rates60sr[i+w].low)   isSwingLow=false;
           }
         if(isSwingHigh && rates60sr[i].high>curClose && (nearestResistance<0 || rates60sr[i].high<nearestResistance))
            nearestResistance = rates60sr[i].high;
         if(isSwingLow && rates60sr[i].low<curClose && (nearestSupport<0 || rates60sr[i].low>nearestSupport))
            nearestSupport = rates60sr[i].low;
        }

      if(nearestResistance>0 && nearestSupport>0)
        {
         double distToRes = nearestResistance-curClose;
         double distToSup = curClose-nearestSupport;
         double span = MathMax(distToRes+distToSup, _Point);
         double closenessToSup = Clamp0to100(100.0-(distToSup/span)*100.0);
         double closenessToRes = Clamp0to100(100.0-(distToRes/span)*100.0);
         if(closenessToSup>closenessToRes)      { g_minds[13].direction=LDIR_BUY;  g_minds[13].score=closenessToSup; }
         else if(closenessToRes>closenessToSup) { g_minds[13].direction=LDIR_SELL; g_minds[13].score=closenessToRes; }
         else                                    { g_minds[13].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[13].score=50.0; }
         g_minds[13].reasoning = StringFormat("support=%.3f resistance=%.3f close=%.3f (n60sr=%d)",
                                               nearestSupport, nearestResistance, curClose, n60sr);
        }
      else
        {
         g_minds[13].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[13].score=0.0;
         g_minds[13].reasoning = StringFormat("no clear S/R found (n60sr=%d)", n60sr);
        }
     }
   else { g_minds[13].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_minds[13].score=0.0; g_minds[13].reasoning="insufficient 720-bar history"; }

   //--- 2026-08-30, explicit operator request (ADD EMA 20/50 SLOPE TREND MIND): Mind #14 (id 16).
   //--- Hand-rolled EMA20/EMA50/ATR from the SAME g_symbol/PERIOD_M1 CopyRates pattern every other
   //--- Mind in this function already uses - no indicator handle (iMA/iATR), matching the fact that
   //--- this entire file has never used one anywhere else. See EvaluateEmaTrendMind() above (defined
   //--- just before this function) for the full calculation; this call site only writes the result
   //--- into g_minds[14].
   EvaluateEmaTrendMind();

   //--- 2026-08-30, explicit operator request (ADD NEW MTF ALIGNMENT MIND): Mind #15 (id 17).
   //--- Evaluates M1/M5/M15 EMA20-vs-EMA50 alignment INTERNALLY (see EvaluateTimeframeEmaDirection
   //--- above) and casts exactly ONE vote for the combined result - M1/M5/M15 are never separate
   //--- Minds and never separately written to g_minds[].
   EvaluateMtfAlignmentMind();

   //--- 2026-08-30, explicit operator request (ABSORPTION MIND): Mind #16 (id 18). Evaluates
   //--- EFFORT/RESPONSE/inefficiency/rejection/persistence from a fresh, independent CopyRates
   //--- window - see EvaluateAbsorptionMind() above for the full pipeline. Casts exactly ONE vote.
   EvaluateAbsorptionMind();

   //--- 2026-08-31, explicit operator request (FAIR VALUE / VWAP MIND): Mind #17 (id 19). Evaluates
   //--- session VWAP/location/acceptance/rejection/persistence/extension from a fresh, independent
   //--- CopyRates window - see EvaluateFairValueMind() above for the full pipeline. Casts exactly
   //--- ONE vote.
   EvaluateFairValueMind();

   //--- 18-Mind Vote (Risk #5 and Pressure #10 removed 2026-08-29; EMA Trend #16 added 2026-08-30;
   //--- MTF Alignment #17 added 2026-08-30; Absorption #18 added 2026-08-30; Fair Value #19 added
   //--- 2026-08-31; Session #13 implemented as a real voter 2026-09-01 - see this function's own header)
   //--- 2026-09-01, explicit operator request (PER-SESSION DNA + MIND SELECTION): IsMindAllowedForSession()
   //--- check added below - ADDITIVE to each Mind's own computed direction (never a replacement): a
   //--- Mind's vote is only COUNTED as BUY/SELL if it also passes the current session's own Mind
   //--- allow-list (blank = no restriction, so this is a no-op until the operator types something
   //--- into one of the new Inp_SessionMinds_* inputs). The Mind's own g_minds[i].direction/score/
   //--- reasoning are NEVER modified here - a session-excluded Mind still shows its real computed
   //--- opinion on the dashboard, it simply isn't counted toward g_buyVotes/g_sellVotes this cycle.
   g_buyVotes=0; g_sellVotes=0; g_waitVotes=0;
   for(int i=0;i<KMIE_LITE_MIND_COUNT;i++)
     {
      ENUM_LITE_DIR countedDir = g_minds[i].direction;
      if(countedDir!=LDIR_WAIT && !IsMindAllowedForSession(g_minds[i].id)) countedDir = LDIR_WAIT;
      if(countedDir==LDIR_BUY) g_buyVotes++;
      else if(countedDir==LDIR_SELL) g_sellVotes++;
      else g_waitVotes++;
     }
   if(g_buyVotes>g_sellVotes) g_mindsVoteDir = LDIR_BUY;
   else if(g_sellVotes>g_buyVotes) g_mindsVoteDir = LDIR_SELL;
   else g_mindsVoteDir = LDIR_WAIT;
  }

//====================================================================
// 2026-09-16, M5 PARALLEL PIPELINE: EvaluateMindsM5()
//
// A duplicate of EvaluateMinds() above, writing g_mindsM5[]/g_buyVotesM5/g_sellVotesM5/
// g_waitVotesM5/g_mindsVoteDirM5 instead of the M1 globals, fed M5 rates[]/n/f. Mind id0 (Trend)
// and id13 (SR) make their own extra hardcoded CopyRates(...,PERIOD_M1,...) calls inside
// EvaluateMinds() - here those are retargeted to PERIOD_M5. Every other inline Mind's formula is
// identical, just reading the M5 rates[]/n/f passed in. The 4 standalone Mind functions
// (EvaluateEmaTrendMind/EvaluateMtfAlignmentMind/EvaluateAbsorptionMind/EvaluateFairValueMind) each
// have their own M5-suffixed duplicate, defined alongside their M1 counterparts.
//====================================================================
void EvaluateMindsM5(const MqlRates &rates[], const int n, const RawFeatures &f)
  {
   double pointsScale = 1.0/_Point;

   //--- 2026-09-24, audit fix (D2, scoped): Trend/Liquidity/Memory Minds (ids 0/4/8) share this single
   //--- fetch, previously hardcoded to 30 M5 bars regardless of Inp_M5DnaMindsLookbackBars. Now honors
   //--- it, same as EvaluateMarketDnaM5()'s own structural windows above. Pattern Mind's own separate
   //--- 30-bar fetch (further below) and SR Mind's 720-bar fetch are DELIBERATELY left untouched -
   //--- SR's window is a genuinely different kind of measurement (support/resistance needs real
   //--- history, not a short "recent window") and collapsing it to Inp_M5DnaMindsLookbackBars would be
   //--- a much larger, likely-unintended strategy change, not a bug fix - flagged for a separate
   //--- decision, not silently applied here.
   MqlRates rates30[]; ArraySetAsSeries(rates30, true);
   int n30 = CopyRates(g_symbol, PERIOD_M5, 1, Inp_M5DnaMindsLookbackBars, rates30);

   g_mindsM5[0].id=0; g_mindsM5[0].name="Trend";
   if(n30>=2)
     {
      double longSlope30 = rates30[0].close - rates30[n30-1].close;
      g_mindsM5[0].direction = SignOf(longSlope30);
      g_mindsM5[0].score = Clamp0to100(MathAbs(longSlope30)*pointsScale/300.0*100.0);
      g_mindsM5[0].reasoning = StringFormat("longSlope30=%.5f (n30=%d)", longSlope30, n30);
     }
   else { g_mindsM5[0].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[0].score=0.0; g_mindsM5[0].reasoning="insufficient 30-bar history"; }

   g_mindsM5[1].id=1; g_mindsM5[1].name="Momentum";
   g_mindsM5[1].direction = SignOf(f.shortSlope);
   g_mindsM5[1].score = Clamp0to100(MathAbs(f.shortSlope)*pointsScale/150.0*100.0);
   g_mindsM5[1].reasoning = StringFormat("shortSlope=%.5f", f.shortSlope);

   g_mindsM5[2].id=2; g_mindsM5[2].name="Scalping";
   if(n>=3)
     {
      double sumBody3=0; int up3=0, down3=0;
      for(int q=0;q<3;q++)
        {
         double rg=rates[q].high-rates[q].low; if(rg<=0.0) rg=_Point;
         sumBody3 += MathAbs(rates[q].close-rates[q].open)/rg*100.0;
        }
      for(int q=0;q<2;q++) { if(rates[q].close>rates[q+1].close) up3++; else if(rates[q].close<rates[q+1].close) down3++; }
      double agreement3 = 0.5+0.5*((up3-down3)/2.0);
      g_mindsM5[2].direction = (agreement3>0.5)?LDIR_BUY:(agreement3<0.5?LDIR_SELL:LDIR_WAIT);
      g_mindsM5[2].score = Clamp0to100(sumBody3/3.0);
      g_mindsM5[2].reasoning = StringFormat("avgBody3=%.1f agreement3=%.2f", sumBody3/3.0, agreement3);
     }
   else { g_mindsM5[2].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[2].score=0.0; g_mindsM5[2].reasoning="insufficient bars"; }

   g_mindsM5[3].id=3; g_mindsM5[3].name="Reversal";
   if(n>=3)
     {
      double sumUpper3=0, sumLower3=0;
      for(int q=0;q<3;q++)
        {
         double rg=rates[q].high-rates[q].low; if(rg<=0.0) rg=_Point;
         sumUpper3 += (rates[q].high-MathMax(rates[q].open,rates[q].close))/rg*100.0;
         sumLower3 += (MathMin(rates[q].open,rates[q].close)-rates[q].low)/rg*100.0;
        }
      double avgUpper3=sumUpper3/3.0, avgLower3=sumLower3/3.0;
      g_mindsM5[3].direction = (avgUpper3>avgLower3) ? LDIR_SELL : (avgLower3>avgUpper3 ? LDIR_BUY : LDIR_WAIT);
      g_mindsM5[3].score = Clamp0to100(MathMax(avgUpper3,avgLower3));
      g_mindsM5[3].reasoning = StringFormat("avgUpperWick3%%=%.1f avgLowerWick3%%=%.1f", avgUpper3, avgLower3);
     }
   else { g_mindsM5[3].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[3].score=0.0; g_mindsM5[3].reasoning="insufficient bars"; }

   g_mindsM5[4].id=4; g_mindsM5[4].name="Liquidity";
   if(n30>=2)
     {
      double hh30=rates30[0].high, ll30=rates30[0].low;
      for(int q=1;q<n30;q++) { if(rates30[q].high>hh30) hh30=rates30[q].high; if(rates30[q].low<ll30) ll30=rates30[q].low; }
      double span30 = MathMax(hh30-ll30, _Point);
      double distFromHigh30 = (hh30-rates30[0].close)/span30*100.0;
      double distFromLow30  = (rates30[0].close-ll30)/span30*100.0;
      g_mindsM5[4].direction = (distFromHigh30<distFromLow30) ? LDIR_SELL : (distFromLow30<distFromHigh30 ? LDIR_BUY : LDIR_WAIT);
      g_mindsM5[4].score = Clamp0to100(100.0-MathMin(distFromHigh30,distFromLow30));
      g_mindsM5[4].reasoning = StringFormat("distFromHigh30%%=%.1f distFromLow30%%=%.1f (n30=%d)", distFromHigh30, distFromLow30, n30);
     }
   else { g_mindsM5[4].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[4].score=0.0; g_mindsM5[4].reasoning="insufficient 30-bar history"; }

   int cnt5 = MathMin(5, n);
   double sumRange5=0;
   for(int q=0;q<cnt5;q++) { double rg=rates[q].high-rates[q].low; if(rg<=0.0) rg=_Point; sumRange5+=rg; }
   double avgRange5 = sumRange5/cnt5;
   double volRatio = avgRange5/MathMax(f.avgRange,_Point);
   double netMove5 = rates[0].close - rates[cnt5-1].close;

   g_mindsM5[5].id=6; g_mindsM5[5].name="Volatility";
   g_mindsM5[5].direction = (volRatio>1.2) ? SignOf(netMove5) : LDIR_WAIT;
   g_mindsM5[5].score = Clamp0to100((volRatio-1.0)*100.0);
   g_mindsM5[5].reasoning = StringFormat("volRatio(5vsPool)=%.2f", volRatio);

   g_mindsM5[6].id=7; g_mindsM5[6].name="Structure";
   g_mindsM5[6].direction = SignOf((double)(f.ups-f.downs));
   g_mindsM5[6].score = Clamp0to100(MathAbs(f.ups-f.downs)*(100.0/n));
   g_mindsM5[6].reasoning = StringFormat("ups=%d downs=%d", f.ups, f.downs);

   //--- 2026-09-16, M5 pipeline: Memory's M1 counterpart compares against g_prevNetMove (a shared,
   //--- M1-scoped cross-cycle memory global) - reusing it here for M5 would corrupt the M1 Memory
   //--- Mind's own cross-cycle comparison. This M5 duplicate is intentionally self-contained per
   //--- tick (no cross-tick memory of its own added), matching the "keep it simple" scope of this
   //--- feature - Memory's M5 vote is WAIT until a dedicated M5 memory global is introduced, if ever.
   g_mindsM5[7].id=8; g_mindsM5[7].name="Memory";
   g_mindsM5[7].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[7].score=0.0; g_mindsM5[7].reasoning="M5 Memory not tracked (no dedicated cross-tick M5 state)";

   MqlRates rates60[]; ArraySetAsSeries(rates60, true);
   int n60 = CopyRates(g_symbol, PERIOD_M5, 1, 30, rates60);
   g_mindsM5[8].id=9; g_mindsM5[8].name="Pattern";
   if(n60>=3)
     {
      int bullCount=0, bearCount=0;
      for(int i=0; i<=n60-3; i++)
        {
         bool priorTwoDown = (rates60[i+1].close<rates60[i+1].open) && (rates60[i+2].close<rates60[i+2].open);
         bool priorTwoUp   = (rates60[i+1].close>rates60[i+1].open) && (rates60[i+2].close>rates60[i+2].open);
         double maxPriorHigh = MathMax(rates60[i+1].high, rates60[i+2].high);
         double minPriorLow  = MathMin(rates60[i+1].low, rates60[i+2].low);
         if(priorTwoDown && (rates60[i].close>rates60[i].open) && (rates60[i].close>maxPriorHigh)) bullCount++;
         if(priorTwoUp   && (rates60[i].close<rates60[i].open) && (rates60[i].close<minPriorLow))  bearCount++;
        }
      g_mindsM5[8].direction = (bullCount>bearCount) ? LDIR_BUY : (bearCount>bullCount ? LDIR_SELL : LDIR_WAIT);
      g_mindsM5[8].score = Clamp0to100(MathAbs(bullCount-bearCount)*(100.0/MathMax(1,bullCount+bearCount)));
      g_mindsM5[8].reasoning = StringFormat("3-bar reversal patterns over 30: bull=%d bear=%d", bullCount, bearCount);
     }
   else { g_mindsM5[8].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[8].score=0.0; g_mindsM5[8].reasoning="insufficient 30-bar history"; }

   g_mindsM5[9].id=11; g_mindsM5[9].name="Energy";
   g_mindsM5[9].direction = SignOf(f.netMove);
   g_mindsM5[9].score = Clamp0to100(f.avgBodyPct);
   g_mindsM5[9].reasoning = StringFormat("avgBodyPct=%.1f", f.avgBodyPct);

   g_mindsM5[10].id=12; g_mindsM5[10].name="Breakout";
   if(n>=3)
     {
      double newest2High = MathMax(rates[0].high, rates[1].high);
      double newest2Low  = MathMin(rates[0].low,  rates[1].low);
      double priorHigh2=-DBL_MAX, priorLow2=DBL_MAX;
      for(int q=2; q<n; q++) { if(rates[q].high>priorHigh2) priorHigh2=rates[q].high; if(rates[q].low<priorLow2) priorLow2=rates[q].low; }

      if(newest2High>priorHigh2)      { g_mindsM5[10].direction=LDIR_BUY;  g_mindsM5[10].score=80.0; g_mindsM5[10].reasoning="new high (2-bar) vs prior window"; }
      else if(newest2Low<priorLow2)   { g_mindsM5[10].direction=LDIR_SELL; g_mindsM5[10].score=80.0; g_mindsM5[10].reasoning="new low (2-bar) vs prior window"; }
      else                             { g_mindsM5[10].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[10].score=15.0; g_mindsM5[10].reasoning="inside prior window"; }
     }
   else { g_mindsM5[10].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[10].score=0.0; g_mindsM5[10].reasoning="insufficient bars"; }

   //--- 2026-09-16, M5 pipeline: Session Mind's M1 counterpart is genuinely session-of-day based
   //--- (not timeframe-based) - reusing it verbatim here would double-count the identical session
   //--- signal into BOTH g_mindsVoteDir and g_mindsVoteDirM5's tallies, undermining the BOTH-mode
   //--- agreement gate's purpose (two genuinely independent readings). Kept WAIT in the M5 array.
   g_mindsM5[11].id=13; g_mindsM5[11].name="Session";
   g_mindsM5[11].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[11].score=0.0; g_mindsM5[11].reasoning="Session Mind is session-of-day based, not duplicated per-timeframe";

   g_mindsM5[12].id=14; g_mindsM5[12].name="Consensus";
   g_mindsM5[12].direction = SignOf(f.netMove);
   g_mindsM5[12].score = Clamp0to100(MathAbs(f.netMove)*pointsScale/300.0*100.0);
   g_mindsM5[12].reasoning = StringFormat("netMove=%.5f", f.netMove);

   MqlRates rates60sr[]; ArraySetAsSeries(rates60sr, true);
   int n60sr = CopyRates(g_symbol, PERIOD_M5, 1, 720, rates60sr);
   g_mindsM5[13].id=15; g_mindsM5[13].name="SR";
   if(n60sr>=10)
     {
      double curClose = rates60sr[0].close;
      double nearestResistance=-1.0, nearestSupport=-1.0;
      int fh=2;
      for(int i=fh; i<n60sr-fh; i++)
        {
         bool isSwingHigh=true, isSwingLow=true;
         for(int w=1; w<=fh; w++)
           {
            if(rates60sr[i].high<=rates60sr[i-w].high || rates60sr[i].high<=rates60sr[i+w].high) isSwingHigh=false;
            if(rates60sr[i].low>=rates60sr[i-w].low   || rates60sr[i].low>=rates60sr[i+w].low)   isSwingLow=false;
           }
         if(isSwingHigh && rates60sr[i].high>curClose && (nearestResistance<0 || rates60sr[i].high<nearestResistance))
            nearestResistance = rates60sr[i].high;
         if(isSwingLow && rates60sr[i].low<curClose && (nearestSupport<0 || rates60sr[i].low>nearestSupport))
            nearestSupport = rates60sr[i].low;
        }

      if(nearestResistance>0 && nearestSupport>0)
        {
         double distToRes = nearestResistance-curClose;
         double distToSup = curClose-nearestSupport;
         double span = MathMax(distToRes+distToSup, _Point);
         double closenessToSup = Clamp0to100(100.0-(distToSup/span)*100.0);
         double closenessToRes = Clamp0to100(100.0-(distToRes/span)*100.0);
         if(closenessToSup>closenessToRes)      { g_mindsM5[13].direction=LDIR_BUY;  g_mindsM5[13].score=closenessToSup; }
         else if(closenessToRes>closenessToSup) { g_mindsM5[13].direction=LDIR_SELL; g_mindsM5[13].score=closenessToRes; }
         else                                    { g_mindsM5[13].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[13].score=50.0; }
         g_mindsM5[13].reasoning = StringFormat("support=%.3f resistance=%.3f close=%.3f (n60sr=%d)",
                                               nearestSupport, nearestResistance, curClose, n60sr);
        }
      else
        {
         g_mindsM5[13].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[13].score=0.0;
         g_mindsM5[13].reasoning = StringFormat("no clear S/R found (n60sr=%d)", n60sr);
        }
     }
   else { g_mindsM5[13].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM5[13].score=0.0; g_mindsM5[13].reasoning="insufficient 720-bar history"; }

   EvaluateEmaTrendMindM5();
   EvaluateMtfAlignmentMindM5();
   EvaluateAbsorptionMindM5();
   EvaluateFairValueMindM5();

   g_buyVotesM5=0; g_sellVotesM5=0; g_waitVotesM5=0;
   for(int i=0;i<KMIE_LITE_MIND_COUNT;i++)
     {
      ENUM_LITE_DIR countedDir = g_mindsM5[i].direction;
      if(countedDir!=LDIR_WAIT && !IsMindAllowedForSession(g_mindsM5[i].id)) countedDir = LDIR_WAIT;
      if(countedDir==LDIR_BUY) g_buyVotesM5++;
      else if(countedDir==LDIR_SELL) g_sellVotesM5++;
      else g_waitVotesM5++;
     }
   if(g_buyVotesM5>g_sellVotesM5) g_mindsVoteDirM5 = LDIR_BUY;
   else if(g_sellVotesM5>g_buyVotesM5) g_mindsVoteDirM5 = LDIR_SELL;
   else g_mindsVoteDirM5 = LDIR_WAIT;
  }

//====================================================================
// 2026-09-23, M15 PARALLEL PIPELINE: EvaluateMindsM15()
//
// A duplicate of EvaluateMinds()/EvaluateMindsM5() above, writing g_mindsM15[]/g_buyVotesM15/
// g_sellVotesM15/g_waitVotesM15/g_mindsVoteDirM15 instead of the M1/M5 globals, fed M15 rates[]/n/f.
// Mind id0 (Trend) and id13 (SR) make their own extra hardcoded CopyRates(...,PERIOD_M1,...) calls
// inside EvaluateMinds() - here (mirroring the M5 twin) those are retargeted to PERIOD_M15. Every
// other inline Mind's formula is identical, just reading the M15 rates[]/n/f passed in. The 4
// standalone Mind functions (EvaluateEmaTrendMindM15/EvaluateMtfAlignmentMindM15/
// EvaluateAbsorptionMindM15/EvaluateFairValueMindM15) each have their own M15-suffixed duplicate,
// defined alongside their M1/M5 counterparts.
//====================================================================
void EvaluateMindsM15(const MqlRates &rates[], const int n, const RawFeatures &f)
  {
   double pointsScale = 1.0/_Point;

   MqlRates rates30[]; ArraySetAsSeries(rates30, true);
   int n30 = CopyRates(g_symbol, PERIOD_M15, 1, 30, rates30);

   g_mindsM15[0].id=0; g_mindsM15[0].name="Trend";
   if(n30>=2)
     {
      double longSlope30 = rates30[0].close - rates30[n30-1].close;
      g_mindsM15[0].direction = SignOf(longSlope30);
      g_mindsM15[0].score = Clamp0to100(MathAbs(longSlope30)*pointsScale/300.0*100.0);
      g_mindsM15[0].reasoning = StringFormat("longSlope30=%.5f (n30=%d)", longSlope30, n30);
     }
   else { g_mindsM15[0].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[0].score=0.0; g_mindsM15[0].reasoning="insufficient 30-bar history"; }

   g_mindsM15[1].id=1; g_mindsM15[1].name="Momentum";
   g_mindsM15[1].direction = SignOf(f.shortSlope);
   g_mindsM15[1].score = Clamp0to100(MathAbs(f.shortSlope)*pointsScale/150.0*100.0);
   g_mindsM15[1].reasoning = StringFormat("shortSlope=%.5f", f.shortSlope);

   g_mindsM15[2].id=2; g_mindsM15[2].name="Scalping";
   if(n>=3)
     {
      double sumBody3=0; int up3=0, down3=0;
      for(int q=0;q<3;q++)
        {
         double rg=rates[q].high-rates[q].low; if(rg<=0.0) rg=_Point;
         sumBody3 += MathAbs(rates[q].close-rates[q].open)/rg*100.0;
        }
      for(int q=0;q<2;q++) { if(rates[q].close>rates[q+1].close) up3++; else if(rates[q].close<rates[q+1].close) down3++; }
      double agreement3 = 0.5+0.5*((up3-down3)/2.0);
      g_mindsM15[2].direction = (agreement3>0.5)?LDIR_BUY:(agreement3<0.5?LDIR_SELL:LDIR_WAIT);
      g_mindsM15[2].score = Clamp0to100(sumBody3/3.0);
      g_mindsM15[2].reasoning = StringFormat("avgBody3=%.1f agreement3=%.2f", sumBody3/3.0, agreement3);
     }
   else { g_mindsM15[2].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[2].score=0.0; g_mindsM15[2].reasoning="insufficient bars"; }

   g_mindsM15[3].id=3; g_mindsM15[3].name="Reversal";
   if(n>=3)
     {
      double sumUpper3=0, sumLower3=0;
      for(int q=0;q<3;q++)
        {
         double rg=rates[q].high-rates[q].low; if(rg<=0.0) rg=_Point;
         sumUpper3 += (rates[q].high-MathMax(rates[q].open,rates[q].close))/rg*100.0;
         sumLower3 += (MathMin(rates[q].open,rates[q].close)-rates[q].low)/rg*100.0;
        }
      double avgUpper3=sumUpper3/3.0, avgLower3=sumLower3/3.0;
      g_mindsM15[3].direction = (avgUpper3>avgLower3) ? LDIR_SELL : (avgLower3>avgUpper3 ? LDIR_BUY : LDIR_WAIT);
      g_mindsM15[3].score = Clamp0to100(MathMax(avgUpper3,avgLower3));
      g_mindsM15[3].reasoning = StringFormat("avgUpperWick3%%=%.1f avgLowerWick3%%=%.1f", avgUpper3, avgLower3);
     }
   else { g_mindsM15[3].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[3].score=0.0; g_mindsM15[3].reasoning="insufficient bars"; }

   g_mindsM15[4].id=4; g_mindsM15[4].name="Liquidity";
   if(n30>=2)
     {
      double hh30=rates30[0].high, ll30=rates30[0].low;
      for(int q=1;q<n30;q++) { if(rates30[q].high>hh30) hh30=rates30[q].high; if(rates30[q].low<ll30) ll30=rates30[q].low; }
      double span30 = MathMax(hh30-ll30, _Point);
      double distFromHigh30 = (hh30-rates30[0].close)/span30*100.0;
      double distFromLow30  = (rates30[0].close-ll30)/span30*100.0;
      g_mindsM15[4].direction = (distFromHigh30<distFromLow30) ? LDIR_SELL : (distFromLow30<distFromHigh30 ? LDIR_BUY : LDIR_WAIT);
      g_mindsM15[4].score = Clamp0to100(100.0-MathMin(distFromHigh30,distFromLow30));
      g_mindsM15[4].reasoning = StringFormat("distFromHigh30%%=%.1f distFromLow30%%=%.1f (n30=%d)", distFromHigh30, distFromLow30, n30);
     }
   else { g_mindsM15[4].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[4].score=0.0; g_mindsM15[4].reasoning="insufficient 30-bar history"; }

   int cnt5 = MathMin(5, n);
   double sumRange5=0;
   for(int q=0;q<cnt5;q++) { double rg=rates[q].high-rates[q].low; if(rg<=0.0) rg=_Point; sumRange5+=rg; }
   double avgRange5 = sumRange5/cnt5;
   double volRatio = avgRange5/MathMax(f.avgRange,_Point);
   double netMove5 = rates[0].close - rates[cnt5-1].close;

   g_mindsM15[5].id=6; g_mindsM15[5].name="Volatility";
   g_mindsM15[5].direction = (volRatio>1.2) ? SignOf(netMove5) : LDIR_WAIT;
   g_mindsM15[5].score = Clamp0to100((volRatio-1.0)*100.0);
   g_mindsM15[5].reasoning = StringFormat("volRatio(5vsPool)=%.2f", volRatio);

   g_mindsM15[6].id=7; g_mindsM15[6].name="Structure";
   g_mindsM15[6].direction = SignOf((double)(f.ups-f.downs));
   g_mindsM15[6].score = Clamp0to100(MathAbs(f.ups-f.downs)*(100.0/n));
   g_mindsM15[6].reasoning = StringFormat("ups=%d downs=%d", f.ups, f.downs);

   //--- 2026-09-23, M15 pipeline: Memory's M1 counterpart compares against g_prevNetMove (a shared,
   //--- M1-scoped cross-cycle memory global) - reusing it here for M15 would corrupt the M1 Memory
   //--- Mind's own cross-cycle comparison, mirroring the M5 twin's identical reasoning. This M15
   //--- duplicate is intentionally self-contained per tick (no cross-tick memory of its own added) -
   //--- Memory's M15 vote is WAIT until a dedicated M15 memory global is introduced, if ever.
   g_mindsM15[7].id=8; g_mindsM15[7].name="Memory";
   g_mindsM15[7].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[7].score=0.0; g_mindsM15[7].reasoning="M15 Memory not tracked (no dedicated cross-tick M15 state)";

   MqlRates rates60[]; ArraySetAsSeries(rates60, true);
   int n60 = CopyRates(g_symbol, PERIOD_M15, 1, 30, rates60);
   g_mindsM15[8].id=9; g_mindsM15[8].name="Pattern";
   if(n60>=3)
     {
      int bullCount=0, bearCount=0;
      for(int i=0; i<=n60-3; i++)
        {
         bool priorTwoDown = (rates60[i+1].close<rates60[i+1].open) && (rates60[i+2].close<rates60[i+2].open);
         bool priorTwoUp   = (rates60[i+1].close>rates60[i+1].open) && (rates60[i+2].close>rates60[i+2].open);
         double maxPriorHigh = MathMax(rates60[i+1].high, rates60[i+2].high);
         double minPriorLow  = MathMin(rates60[i+1].low, rates60[i+2].low);
         if(priorTwoDown && (rates60[i].close>rates60[i].open) && (rates60[i].close>maxPriorHigh)) bullCount++;
         if(priorTwoUp   && (rates60[i].close<rates60[i].open) && (rates60[i].close<minPriorLow))  bearCount++;
        }
      g_mindsM15[8].direction = (bullCount>bearCount) ? LDIR_BUY : (bearCount>bullCount ? LDIR_SELL : LDIR_WAIT);
      g_mindsM15[8].score = Clamp0to100(MathAbs(bullCount-bearCount)*(100.0/MathMax(1,bullCount+bearCount)));
      g_mindsM15[8].reasoning = StringFormat("3-bar reversal patterns over 30: bull=%d bear=%d", bullCount, bearCount);
     }
   else { g_mindsM15[8].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[8].score=0.0; g_mindsM15[8].reasoning="insufficient 30-bar history"; }

   g_mindsM15[9].id=11; g_mindsM15[9].name="Energy";
   g_mindsM15[9].direction = SignOf(f.netMove);
   g_mindsM15[9].score = Clamp0to100(f.avgBodyPct);
   g_mindsM15[9].reasoning = StringFormat("avgBodyPct=%.1f", f.avgBodyPct);

   g_mindsM15[10].id=12; g_mindsM15[10].name="Breakout";
   if(n>=3)
     {
      double newest2High = MathMax(rates[0].high, rates[1].high);
      double newest2Low  = MathMin(rates[0].low,  rates[1].low);
      double priorHigh2=-DBL_MAX, priorLow2=DBL_MAX;
      for(int q=2; q<n; q++) { if(rates[q].high>priorHigh2) priorHigh2=rates[q].high; if(rates[q].low<priorLow2) priorLow2=rates[q].low; }

      if(newest2High>priorHigh2)      { g_mindsM15[10].direction=LDIR_BUY;  g_mindsM15[10].score=80.0; g_mindsM15[10].reasoning="new high (2-bar) vs prior window"; }
      else if(newest2Low<priorLow2)   { g_mindsM15[10].direction=LDIR_SELL; g_mindsM15[10].score=80.0; g_mindsM15[10].reasoning="new low (2-bar) vs prior window"; }
      else                             { g_mindsM15[10].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[10].score=15.0; g_mindsM15[10].reasoning="inside prior window"; }
     }
   else { g_mindsM15[10].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[10].score=0.0; g_mindsM15[10].reasoning="insufficient bars"; }

   //--- 2026-09-23, M15 pipeline: Session Mind's M1 counterpart is genuinely session-of-day based
   //--- (not timeframe-based) - reusing it verbatim here would double-count the identical session
   //--- signal into g_mindsVoteDir/g_mindsVoteDirM5/g_mindsVoteDirM15's tallies, undermining the
   //--- 3-way agreement gate's purpose (three genuinely independent readings), mirroring the M5
   //--- twin's identical reasoning. Kept WAIT in the M15 array.
   g_mindsM15[11].id=13; g_mindsM15[11].name="Session";
   g_mindsM15[11].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[11].score=0.0; g_mindsM15[11].reasoning="Session Mind is session-of-day based, not duplicated per-timeframe";

   g_mindsM15[12].id=14; g_mindsM15[12].name="Consensus";
   g_mindsM15[12].direction = SignOf(f.netMove);
   g_mindsM15[12].score = Clamp0to100(MathAbs(f.netMove)*pointsScale/300.0*100.0);
   g_mindsM15[12].reasoning = StringFormat("netMove=%.5f", f.netMove);

   MqlRates rates60sr[]; ArraySetAsSeries(rates60sr, true);
   int n60sr = CopyRates(g_symbol, PERIOD_M15, 1, 720, rates60sr);
   g_mindsM15[13].id=15; g_mindsM15[13].name="SR";
   if(n60sr>=10)
     {
      double curClose = rates60sr[0].close;
      double nearestResistance=-1.0, nearestSupport=-1.0;
      int fh=2;
      for(int i=fh; i<n60sr-fh; i++)
        {
         bool isSwingHigh=true, isSwingLow=true;
         for(int w=1; w<=fh; w++)
           {
            if(rates60sr[i].high<=rates60sr[i-w].high || rates60sr[i].high<=rates60sr[i+w].high) isSwingHigh=false;
            if(rates60sr[i].low>=rates60sr[i-w].low   || rates60sr[i].low>=rates60sr[i+w].low)   isSwingLow=false;
           }
         if(isSwingHigh && rates60sr[i].high>curClose && (nearestResistance<0 || rates60sr[i].high<nearestResistance))
            nearestResistance = rates60sr[i].high;
         if(isSwingLow && rates60sr[i].low<curClose && (nearestSupport<0 || rates60sr[i].low>nearestSupport))
            nearestSupport = rates60sr[i].low;
        }

      if(nearestResistance>0 && nearestSupport>0)
        {
         double distToRes = nearestResistance-curClose;
         double distToSup = curClose-nearestSupport;
         double span = MathMax(distToRes+distToSup, _Point);
         double closenessToSup = Clamp0to100(100.0-(distToSup/span)*100.0);
         double closenessToRes = Clamp0to100(100.0-(distToRes/span)*100.0);
         if(closenessToSup>closenessToRes)      { g_mindsM15[13].direction=LDIR_BUY;  g_mindsM15[13].score=closenessToSup; }
         else if(closenessToRes>closenessToSup) { g_mindsM15[13].direction=LDIR_SELL; g_mindsM15[13].score=closenessToRes; }
         else                                    { g_mindsM15[13].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[13].score=50.0; }
         g_mindsM15[13].reasoning = StringFormat("support=%.3f resistance=%.3f close=%.3f (n60sr=%d)",
                                               nearestSupport, nearestResistance, curClose, n60sr);
        }
      else
        {
         g_mindsM15[13].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[13].score=0.0;
         g_mindsM15[13].reasoning = StringFormat("no clear S/R found (n60sr=%d)", n60sr);
        }
     }
   else { g_mindsM15[13].direction=LDIR_WAIT; g_mindsM15[13].score=0.0; g_mindsM15[13].reasoning="insufficient 720-bar history"; }

   EvaluateEmaTrendMindM15();
   EvaluateMtfAlignmentMindM15();
   EvaluateAbsorptionMindM15();
   EvaluateFairValueMindM15();

   g_buyVotesM15=0; g_sellVotesM15=0; g_waitVotesM15=0;
   for(int i=0;i<KMIE_LITE_MIND_COUNT;i++)
     {
      ENUM_LITE_DIR countedDir = g_mindsM15[i].direction;
      if(countedDir!=LDIR_WAIT && !IsMindAllowedForSession(g_mindsM15[i].id)) countedDir = LDIR_WAIT;
      if(countedDir==LDIR_BUY) g_buyVotesM15++;
      else if(countedDir==LDIR_SELL) g_sellVotesM15++;
      else g_waitVotesM15++;
     }
   if(g_buyVotesM15>g_sellVotesM15) g_mindsVoteDirM15 = LDIR_BUY;
   else if(g_sellVotesM15>g_buyVotesM15) g_mindsVoteDirM15 = LDIR_SELL;
   else g_mindsVoteDirM15 = LDIR_WAIT;
  }

//====================================================================
// STAGE 1a: CANDLE INTELLIGENCE - fresh-computed, Framework 10A/10B-named intermediate layer.
// Basis: Inp_MarketDNALookbackCandles CLOSED candles + the still-forming (running) M1 candle,
// folded in as one extra data point - matching the "5 completed + 1 running" basis Framework 10C
// itself used before its own lookback was widened to a pure rolling average earlier this session.
// Every field is derived directly from this cycle's own raw OHLC - nothing upstream, nothing
// cached across cycles. Market DNA (Stage 1b, below) reads ONLY these named fields.
//====================================================================
CandleIntelligence EvaluateCandleIntelligence(const MqlRates &rates[], const int n)
  {
   CandleIntelligence ci;
   //--- 2026-09-03, bugfix (duplication/drift audit): this used to independently recompute
   //--- k = MathMin(Inp_MarketDNALookbackCandles, n) - the raw global default (5) - while
   //--- EvaluateMarketDNA() (the only caller) had already moved to the per-session-aware
   //--- ResolveEffectiveDnaLookback() (2026-09-01, e.g. 60 in London/NY by default). Every
   //--- structural DNA formula downstream (Breakout/Pullback/Range/Neutral/Choppy/Reversal/
   //--- TrendExhaustion/shadow trends) was being handed ci.* fields computed over 5 candles
   //--- while being told - and itself operating on - a 30-60 candle window: a silent window
   //--- mismatch in every live DNA cycle, not merely a duplicated line. Fixed by resolving the
   //--- SAME effective lookback here that EvaluateMarketDNA() uses, so both stages share one
   //--- window again. ResolveEffectiveDnaLookback() is self-contained (reads only inputs +
   //--- TimeCurrent()), so this needed no new parameter/signature change.
   int k = MathMin(ResolveEffectiveDnaLookback(), n);
   if(k<1) k=1;

   //--- Running candle - the still-forming M1 bar (shift=0, always incomplete). Its own high/low/
   //--- close are live and update every tick; using it here is exactly what "1 running" means.
   MqlRates runRate[];
   ArraySetAsSeries(runRate, true);
   int gotRun = CopyRates(g_symbol, PERIOD_M1, 0, 1, runRate);
   ci.runningIncluded = (gotRun>0);

   double sumBodyPct=0, sumUpperWick=0, sumLowerWick=0, sumRange=0;
   int ups=0, downs=0;
   ci.priorHighExclLast=-DBL_MAX; ci.priorLowExclLast=DBL_MAX;

   for(int i=0;i<k;i++)
     {
      double range = rates[i].high-rates[i].low; if(range<=0.0) range=_Point;
      double body = MathAbs(rates[i].close-rates[i].open);
      sumBodyPct += (body/range)*100.0;
      sumUpperWick += ((rates[i].high-MathMax(rates[i].open,rates[i].close))/range)*100.0;
      sumLowerWick += ((MathMin(rates[i].open,rates[i].close)-rates[i].low)/range)*100.0;
      sumRange += range;
      if(rates[i].close>rates[i].open) ups++; else if(rates[i].close<rates[i].open) downs++;
      //--- "prior" (pre-newest) extremes: indices 1..k-1 always qualify; index 0 (the last CLOSED
      //--- candle) only qualifies too once the running candle takes over as the newest data point.
      if(i>0 && i<k)
        {
         if(rates[i].high>ci.priorHighExclLast) ci.priorHighExclLast=rates[i].high;
         if(rates[i].low<ci.priorLowExclLast)    ci.priorLowExclLast=rates[i].low;
        }
     }
   if(ci.runningIncluded)
     {
      if(rates[0].high>ci.priorHighExclLast) ci.priorHighExclLast=rates[0].high;
      if(rates[0].low<ci.priorLowExclLast)    ci.priorLowExclLast=rates[0].low;
     }

   int totalCandles = k;
   //--- Closed-only range sum, captured BEFORE the running candle (below) is folded into sumRange -
   //--- volRatio (below) needs a duration-consistent comparison (closed bar vs closed bars), since
   //--- comparing the still-forming running candle's range against an average of fully-elapsed
   //--- candles mechanically favours "compression" (a partially-elapsed candle almost always has
   //--- less range so far than a completed one, regardless of actual volatility).
   double sumRangeClosedOnly = sumRange;
   ci.runningBodyPct = 0.0;
   if(ci.runningIncluded)
     {
      double rRange = runRate[0].high-runRate[0].low; if(rRange<=0.0) rRange=_Point;
      double rBody = MathAbs(runRate[0].close-runRate[0].open);
      ci.runningBodyPct = (rBody/rRange)*100.0;
      sumBodyPct += ci.runningBodyPct;
      sumUpperWick += ((runRate[0].high-MathMax(runRate[0].open,runRate[0].close))/rRange)*100.0;
      sumLowerWick += ((MathMin(runRate[0].open,runRate[0].close)-runRate[0].low)/rRange)*100.0;
      sumRange += rRange;
      if(runRate[0].close>runRate[0].open) ups++; else if(runRate[0].close<runRate[0].open) downs++;
      totalCandles = k+1;
     }

   ci.aggression      = Clamp0to100(sumBodyPct/totalCandles);
   ci.noiseIndex       = Clamp0to100((sumUpperWick+sumLowerWick)/totalCandles);
   ci.candleQuality      = Clamp0to100(100.0-ci.noiseIndex);
   ci.buyingStrength       = Clamp0to100((ups/(double)totalCandles)*100.0);
   ci.sellingStrength        = Clamp0to100((downs/(double)totalCandles)*100.0);
   ci.candleConfidence         = Clamp0to100(MathAbs(ci.buyingStrength-ci.sellingStrength));
   //--- Exhaustion: momentum fading - heavy wick relative to how much conviction (body) backs it up.
   ci.exhaustion = Clamp0to100(ci.noiseIndex*0.6 + (100.0-ci.aggression)*0.4);

   //--- "Newest candle" for rejection/volatility/absorption purposes: the RUNNING candle when
   //--- available (live, more current than the last closed one), else the last closed candle.
   if(ci.runningIncluded) { ci.newestHigh=runRate[0].high; ci.newestLow=runRate[0].low; ci.newestClose=runRate[0].close; }
   else                   { ci.newestHigh=rates[0].high;   ci.newestLow=rates[0].low;   ci.newestClose=rates[0].close; }
   double newestOpen = ci.runningIncluded ? runRate[0].open : rates[0].open;

   double lastRangeK = ci.newestHigh-ci.newestLow; if(lastRangeK<=0.0) lastRangeK=_Point;
   double lastUpperWickPct = ((ci.newestHigh-MathMax(newestOpen,ci.newestClose))/lastRangeK)*100.0;
   double lastLowerWickPct = ((MathMin(newestOpen,ci.newestClose)-ci.newestLow)/lastRangeK)*100.0;
   //--- Rejection: the NEWEST candle's own dominant single-sided wick - a level being refused right now.
   ci.rejection = MathMax(lastUpperWickPct, lastLowerWickPct);
   //--- Absorption: high range with low net displacement over the window = effort without progress.
   double netDisplace = MathAbs(ci.newestClose-rates[k-1].close);
   ci.absorption = Clamp0to100(sumRange>_Point ? (100.0 - (netDisplace/sumRange)*100.0) : 0.0);
   //--- Volatility ratio: LAST CLOSED candle's range vs the average range of the OTHER closed
   //--- candles in the window - deliberately excludes the still-forming running candle (unlike
   //--- ci.newestHigh/Low/Close above, which intentionally stay live for rejection/absorption/Entry
   //--- Intelligence). Both sides of this ratio are now full, same-duration M1 bars, so a score near
   //--- 100 means the market is genuinely quiet, not just "less than a minute has elapsed."
   double closedLastRange = rates[0].high-rates[0].low; if(closedLastRange<=0.0) closedLastRange=_Point;
   double avgPriorClosedRange = (k>1) ? ((sumRangeClosedOnly-closedLastRange)/(k-1)) : closedLastRange;
   ci.volRatio = closedLastRange/MathMax(avgPriorClosedRange,_Point);

   return ci;
  }

//--- 2026-09-16, M5 PARALLEL PIPELINE: straight duplicate of EvaluateCandleIntelligence() above, with
//--- its ONE internal hardcoded-timeframe CopyRates call (the still-forming running-candle fetch,
//--- shift=0) retargeted from PERIOD_M1 to PERIOD_M5 - this function is NOT fully parameter-pure like
//--- its "genuinely pure" callers (EvaluateStrongTrendStructure() etc.) assumed; it independently fetches
//--- the live running candle rather than deriving it from rates[]/n alone. Everything else (the
//--- rates[]/n-driven k-window math) is byte-identical, just operating on the M5 rates[]/n passed in by
//--- EvaluateMarketDnaM5(). Publishes to g_ciM5 at that caller's own site, never here.
CandleIntelligence EvaluateCandleIntelligenceM5(const MqlRates &rates[], const int n)
  {
   CandleIntelligence ci;
   int k = MathMin(ResolveEffectiveDnaLookback(), n);
   if(k<1) k=1;

   //--- Running candle - the still-forming M5 bar (shift=0, always incomplete).
   MqlRates runRate[];
   ArraySetAsSeries(runRate, true);
   int gotRun = CopyRates(g_symbol, PERIOD_M5, 0, 1, runRate);
   ci.runningIncluded = (gotRun>0);

   double sumBodyPct=0, sumUpperWick=0, sumLowerWick=0, sumRange=0;
   int ups=0, downs=0;
   ci.priorHighExclLast=-DBL_MAX; ci.priorLowExclLast=DBL_MAX;

   for(int i=0;i<k;i++)
     {
      double range = rates[i].high-rates[i].low; if(range<=0.0) range=_Point;
      double body = MathAbs(rates[i].close-rates[i].open);
      sumBodyPct += (body/range)*100.0;
      sumUpperWick += ((rates[i].high-MathMax(rates[i].open,rates[i].close))/range)*100.0;
      sumLowerWick += ((MathMin(rates[i].open,rates[i].close)-rates[i].low)/range)*100.0;
      sumRange += range;
      if(rates[i].close>rates[i].open) ups++; else if(rates[i].close<rates[i].open) downs++;
      if(i>0 && i<k)
        {
         if(rates[i].high>ci.priorHighExclLast) ci.priorHighExclLast=rates[i].high;
         if(rates[i].low<ci.priorLowExclLast)    ci.priorLowExclLast=rates[i].low;
        }
     }
   if(ci.runningIncluded)
     {
      if(rates[0].high>ci.priorHighExclLast) ci.priorHighExclLast=rates[0].high;
      if(rates[0].low<ci.priorLowExclLast)    ci.priorLowExclLast=rates[0].low;
     }

   int totalCandles = k;
   double sumRangeClosedOnly = sumRange;
   ci.runningBodyPct = 0.0;
   if(ci.runningIncluded)
     {
      double rRange = runRate[0].high-runRate[0].low; if(rRange<=0.0) rRange=_Point;
      double rBody = MathAbs(runRate[0].close-runRate[0].open);
      ci.runningBodyPct = (rBody/rRange)*100.0;
      sumBodyPct += ci.runningBodyPct;
      sumUpperWick += ((runRate[0].high-MathMax(runRate[0].open,runRate[0].close))/rRange)*100.0;
      sumLowerWick += ((MathMin(runRate[0].open,runRate[0].close)-runRate[0].low)/rRange)*100.0;
      sumRange += rRange;
      if(runRate[0].close>runRate[0].open) ups++; else if(runRate[0].close<runRate[0].open) downs++;
      totalCandles = k+1;
     }

   ci.aggression      = Clamp0to100(sumBodyPct/totalCandles);
   ci.noiseIndex       = Clamp0to100((sumUpperWick+sumLowerWick)/totalCandles);
   ci.candleQuality      = Clamp0to100(100.0-ci.noiseIndex);
   ci.buyingStrength       = Clamp0to100((ups/(double)totalCandles)*100.0);
   ci.sellingStrength        = Clamp0to100((downs/(double)totalCandles)*100.0);
   ci.candleConfidence         = Clamp0to100(MathAbs(ci.buyingStrength-ci.sellingStrength));
   ci.exhaustion = Clamp0to100(ci.noiseIndex*0.6 + (100.0-ci.aggression)*0.4);

   if(ci.runningIncluded) { ci.newestHigh=runRate[0].high; ci.newestLow=runRate[0].low; ci.newestClose=runRate[0].close; }
   else                   { ci.newestHigh=rates[0].high;   ci.newestLow=rates[0].low;   ci.newestClose=rates[0].close; }
   double newestOpen = ci.runningIncluded ? runRate[0].open : rates[0].open;

   double lastRangeK = ci.newestHigh-ci.newestLow; if(lastRangeK<=0.0) lastRangeK=_Point;
   double lastUpperWickPct = ((ci.newestHigh-MathMax(newestOpen,ci.newestClose))/lastRangeK)*100.0;
   double lastLowerWickPct = ((MathMin(newestOpen,ci.newestClose)-ci.newestLow)/lastRangeK)*100.0;
   ci.rejection = MathMax(lastUpperWickPct, lastLowerWickPct);
   double netDisplace = MathAbs(ci.newestClose-rates[k-1].close);
   ci.absorption = Clamp0to100(sumRange>_Point ? (100.0 - (netDisplace/sumRange)*100.0) : 0.0);
   double closedLastRange = rates[0].high-rates[0].low; if(closedLastRange<=0.0) closedLastRange=_Point;
   double avgPriorClosedRange = (k>1) ? ((sumRangeClosedOnly-closedLastRange)/(k-1)) : closedLastRange;
   ci.volRatio = closedLastRange/MathMax(avgPriorClosedRange,_Point);

   return ci;
  }

//--- 2026-09-23, M15 PARALLEL PIPELINE: straight duplicate of EvaluateCandleIntelligence()/
//--- EvaluateCandleIntelligenceM5() above, with its ONE internal hardcoded-timeframe CopyRates call
//--- (the still-forming running-candle fetch, shift=0) retargeted from PERIOD_M1 to PERIOD_M15. UNLIKE
//--- the M5 twin (which still reads ResolveEffectiveDnaLookback(), the M1/session-driven resolver), this
//--- M15 twin's `k` computation uses Inp_M15DnaMindsLookbackBars directly - M15's whole point is a fixed,
//--- dedicated 8-bar window, never inherited from M1/session logic (verified fresh: the M5 twin above was
//--- NOT updated to Inp_M5DnaMindsLookbackBars in the earlier M5-lookback task, so this is a deliberate,
//--- explicit divergence from the M5 pattern, not an oversight). Everything else (the rates[]/n-driven
//--- k-window math) is byte-identical, just operating on the M15 rates[]/n passed in by
//--- EvaluateMarketDnaM15(). Publishes to g_ciM15 at that caller's own site, never here.
CandleIntelligence EvaluateCandleIntelligenceM15(const MqlRates &rates[], const int n)
  {
   CandleIntelligence ci;
   int k = MathMin(Inp_M15DnaMindsLookbackBars, n);
   if(k<1) k=1;

   //--- Running candle - the still-forming M15 bar (shift=0, always incomplete).
   MqlRates runRate[];
   ArraySetAsSeries(runRate, true);
   int gotRun = CopyRates(g_symbol, PERIOD_M15, 0, 1, runRate);
   ci.runningIncluded = (gotRun>0);

   double sumBodyPct=0, sumUpperWick=0, sumLowerWick=0, sumRange=0;
   int ups=0, downs=0;
   ci.priorHighExclLast=-DBL_MAX; ci.priorLowExclLast=DBL_MAX;

   for(int i=0;i<k;i++)
     {
      double range = rates[i].high-rates[i].low; if(range<=0.0) range=_Point;
      double body = MathAbs(rates[i].close-rates[i].open);
      sumBodyPct += (body/range)*100.0;
      sumUpperWick += ((rates[i].high-MathMax(rates[i].open,rates[i].close))/range)*100.0;
      sumLowerWick += ((MathMin(rates[i].open,rates[i].close)-rates[i].low)/range)*100.0;
      sumRange += range;
      if(rates[i].close>rates[i].open) ups++; else if(rates[i].close<rates[i].open) downs++;
      if(i>0 && i<k)
        {
         if(rates[i].high>ci.priorHighExclLast) ci.priorHighExclLast=rates[i].high;
         if(rates[i].low<ci.priorLowExclLast)    ci.priorLowExclLast=rates[i].low;
        }
     }
   if(ci.runningIncluded)
     {
      if(rates[0].high>ci.priorHighExclLast) ci.priorHighExclLast=rates[0].high;
      if(rates[0].low<ci.priorLowExclLast)    ci.priorLowExclLast=rates[0].low;
     }

   int totalCandles = k;
   double sumRangeClosedOnly = sumRange;
   ci.runningBodyPct = 0.0;
   if(ci.runningIncluded)
     {
      double rRange = runRate[0].high-runRate[0].low; if(rRange<=0.0) rRange=_Point;
      double rBody = MathAbs(runRate[0].close-runRate[0].open);
      ci.runningBodyPct = (rBody/rRange)*100.0;
      sumBodyPct += ci.runningBodyPct;
      sumUpperWick += ((runRate[0].high-MathMax(runRate[0].open,runRate[0].close))/rRange)*100.0;
      sumLowerWick += ((MathMin(runRate[0].open,runRate[0].close)-runRate[0].low)/rRange)*100.0;
      sumRange += rRange;
      if(runRate[0].close>runRate[0].open) ups++; else if(runRate[0].close<runRate[0].open) downs++;
      totalCandles = k+1;
     }

   ci.aggression      = Clamp0to100(sumBodyPct/totalCandles);
   ci.noiseIndex       = Clamp0to100((sumUpperWick+sumLowerWick)/totalCandles);
   ci.candleQuality      = Clamp0to100(100.0-ci.noiseIndex);
   ci.buyingStrength       = Clamp0to100((ups/(double)totalCandles)*100.0);
   ci.sellingStrength        = Clamp0to100((downs/(double)totalCandles)*100.0);
   ci.candleConfidence         = Clamp0to100(MathAbs(ci.buyingStrength-ci.sellingStrength));
   ci.exhaustion = Clamp0to100(ci.noiseIndex*0.6 + (100.0-ci.aggression)*0.4);

   if(ci.runningIncluded) { ci.newestHigh=runRate[0].high; ci.newestLow=runRate[0].low; ci.newestClose=runRate[0].close; }
   else                   { ci.newestHigh=rates[0].high;   ci.newestLow=rates[0].low;   ci.newestClose=rates[0].close; }
   double newestOpen = ci.runningIncluded ? runRate[0].open : rates[0].open;

   double lastRangeK = ci.newestHigh-ci.newestLow; if(lastRangeK<=0.0) lastRangeK=_Point;
   double lastUpperWickPct = ((ci.newestHigh-MathMax(newestOpen,ci.newestClose))/lastRangeK)*100.0;
   double lastLowerWickPct = ((MathMin(newestOpen,ci.newestClose)-ci.newestLow)/lastRangeK)*100.0;
   ci.rejection = MathMax(lastUpperWickPct, lastLowerWickPct);
   double netDisplace = MathAbs(ci.newestClose-rates[k-1].close);
   ci.absorption = Clamp0to100(sumRange>_Point ? (100.0 - (netDisplace/sumRange)*100.0) : 0.0);
   double closedLastRange = rates[0].high-rates[0].low; if(closedLastRange<=0.0) closedLastRange=_Point;
   double avgPriorClosedRange = (k>1) ? ((sumRangeClosedOnly-closedLastRange)/(k-1)) : closedLastRange;
   ci.volRatio = closedLastRange/MathMax(avgPriorClosedRange,_Point);

   return ci;
  }

//====================================================================
// STAGE 1a-SHADOW, 2026-08-25 (explicit operator request, PHASE 1 - CALCULATE/LOG/STORE ONLY):
// STRONG_UPTREND structural DNA - approved design from the prior design-review turn. Detects a
// confirmed Higher-High/Higher-Low swing sequence over the SAME Inp_MarketDNALookbackCandles window
// (rates[]/k) already used by EvaluateCandleIntelligence() above - no second lookback, no second
// CopyRates. Swing detection reuses Mind #16's exact 5-bar fractal technique (fh=2, strict
// inequalities, ties disqualify) but is an ISOLATED calculation over this window - never Mind #16's
// own 720-candle array, never its nearest-SR behavior. The still-forming running candle can NEVER
// become a confirmed swing (a fractal needs future bars that don't exist yet for it); it only feeds
// RunningContinuationScore via CandleIntelligence's already-computed ci.newestHigh/newestLow/
// runningIncluded fields (no extra CopyRates for it either).
//
// PHASE 1 SAFETY: this function's return value (StrongUptrendShadow) is read ONLY by the diagnostic
// logging block in EvaluateMarketDNA() below. It is never written into scores[], never read by
// CalibrateMarketDNAScores(), never assigned to g_dnaState/g_dnaScore, never read by
// CurrentRegimeAllowed(), Entry Approval, Minds, TP/SL, or execution. STRONG_UPTREND_RAW_SCORE is a
// raw diagnostic number only - Phase 2 (a separate, explicitly-approved change) would derive real
// mean/stdev from logged data and enter it into the live 18-state competition; neither has happened
// here.
//====================================================================
#define KMIE_UPTREND_FRACTAL_HALFWIDTH 2   // matches Mind #16's classic 5-bar fractal (2 bars each side)
#define KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS        64  // generous bound for a 26-candle window; loops self-truncate if ever exceeded

StrongUptrendShadow EvaluateStrongUptrendShadow(const MqlRates &rates[], const int k, const CandleIntelligence &ci)
  {
   StrongUptrendShadow sh;
   sh.swingHighCount=0; sh.swingLowCount=0; sh.hhScore=0.0; sh.hlScore=0.0; sh.structuralContinuity=0.0;
   sh.pullbackScore=0.0; sh.evidenceConfidence=0.0; sh.structuralScore=0.0; sh.runningContinuationScore=50.0;
   sh.rawScore=0.0; sh.haveLatestHH=false; sh.latestConfirmedHH=0.0; sh.haveLatestHL=false; sh.latestConfirmedHL=0.0;
   sh.liveExtension=false; sh.liveBreakdown=false;
   sh.swingStructureJson="[]"; sh.hhComplianceJson="[]"; sh.hlComplianceJson="[]"; sh.pullbackPctJson="[]";

   int fh = KMIE_UPTREND_FRACTAL_HALFWIDTH;
   if(k < (2*fh+2)) return sh; // not enough closed candles for even one eligible fractal position

   //--- Step 1: raw confirmed swing detection (Mind #16's exact fractal test), collected in
   //--- chronological (oldest->newest) order directly - rates[] is series-indexed (0=newest closed
   //--- candle), so looping i from the oldest eligible index down to the newest eligible index visits
   //--- them in ascending calendar time with no separate reverse step needed.
   bool     isHighArr[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   double   priceArr[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   datetime timeArr[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   int rawCount=0;
   for(int i=k-1-fh; i>=fh && rawCount<KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS; i--)
     {
      bool isSwingHigh=true, isSwingLow=true;
      for(int w=1; w<=fh; w++)
        {
         if(rates[i].high<=rates[i-w].high || rates[i].high<=rates[i+w].high) isSwingHigh=false;
         if(rates[i].low>=rates[i-w].low   || rates[i].low>=rates[i+w].low)   isSwingLow=false;
        }
      if(isSwingHigh && rawCount<KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS)
        { isHighArr[rawCount]=true;  priceArr[rawCount]=rates[i].high; timeArr[rawCount]=rates[i].time; rawCount++; }
      if(isSwingLow && rawCount<KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS)
        { isHighArr[rawCount]=false; priceArr[rawCount]=rates[i].low;  timeArr[rawCount]=rates[i].time; rawCount++; }
     }

   //--- Step 2: zigzag cleanup - single forward pass, collapse any run of same-type points into the
   //--- single most extreme one (higher of consecutive highs / lower of consecutive lows) so the
   //--- output strictly alternates, exactly as approved.
   bool     cIsHigh[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   double   cPrice[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   datetime cTime[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   int cleanCount=0;
   for(int r=0; r<rawCount; r++)
     {
      if(cleanCount>0 && cIsHigh[cleanCount-1]==isHighArr[r])
        {
         bool moreExtreme = isHighArr[r] ? (priceArr[r]>cPrice[cleanCount-1]) : (priceArr[r]<cPrice[cleanCount-1]);
         if(moreExtreme) { cPrice[cleanCount-1]=priceArr[r]; cTime[cleanCount-1]=timeArr[r]; }
        }
      else
        { cIsHigh[cleanCount]=isHighArr[r]; cPrice[cleanCount]=priceArr[r]; cTime[cleanCount]=timeArr[r]; cleanCount++; }
     }

   //--- Step 3: split the cleaned alternating sequence back into SH[]/SL[] (still chronological), and
   //--- build the human/machine-readable swing structure JSON for logging.
   double   SH[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS]; datetime SHt[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS]; int mH=0;
   double   SL[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS]; datetime SLt[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS]; int pL=0;
   string structJson="[";
   for(int c=0;c<cleanCount;c++)
     {
      if(c>0) structJson+=",";
      structJson += StringFormat("{\"type\":\"%s\",\"price\":%.3f}", cIsHigh[c]?"HH":"HL", cPrice[c]);
      if(cIsHigh[c]) { SH[mH]=cPrice[c]; SHt[mH]=cTime[c]; mH++; }
      else           { SL[pL]=cPrice[c]; SLt[pL]=cTime[c]; pL++; }
     }
   structJson += "]";
   sh.swingStructureJson = structJson;
   sh.swingHighCount = mH;
   sh.swingLowCount  = pL;
   if(mH>0) { sh.haveLatestHH=true; sh.latestConfirmedHH=SH[mH-1]; }
   if(pL>0) { sh.haveLatestHL=true; sh.latestConfirmedHL=SL[pL-1]; }

   //--- Step 4: minimum evidence gate - below 2 confirmed highs AND 2 confirmed lows, StructuralScore
   //--- stays exactly 0 (no guessed partial value). Above the gate: HH/HL scores (flat pair-compliance
   //--- average), StructuralContinuity (the SAME compliance flags, recency-weighted instead of flat -
   //--- a recent break costs more than an old one), PullbackScore (leg-based retracement), and
   //--- EvidenceConfidence (how much of the reference 6-pair pattern is actually present).
   if(mH>=2 && pL>=2)
     {
      int  hhPairs = mH-1, hhRising=0;
      bool hhCompliant[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
      for(int i=0;i<hhPairs;i++) { hhCompliant[i]=(SH[i+1]>SH[i]); if(hhCompliant[i]) hhRising++; }
      sh.hhScore = 100.0*hhRising/hhPairs;

      int  hlPairs = pL-1, hlRising=0;
      bool hlCompliant[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
      for(int j=0;j<hlPairs;j++) { hlCompliant[j]=(SL[j+1]>SL[j]); if(hlCompliant[j]) hlRising++; }
      sh.hlScore = 100.0*hlRising/hlPairs;

      string hhJ="["; for(int i=0;i<hhPairs;i++){ if(i>0) hhJ+=","; hhJ+=(hhCompliant[i]?"1":"0"); } hhJ+="]";
      string hlJ="["; for(int j=0;j<hlPairs;j++){ if(j>0) hlJ+=","; hlJ+=(hlCompliant[j]?"1":"0"); } hlJ+="]";
      sh.hhComplianceJson = hhJ;
      sh.hlComplianceJson = hlJ;

      //--- StructuralContinuity: merge the HH-pair and HL-pair compliance events by each pair's own
      //--- confirming timestamp (the SECOND point of the pair), sort ascending, weight linearly by
      //--- position (oldest=1 ... newest=highest).
      datetime evtTime[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS*2];
      bool     evtCompliant[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS*2];
      int evtCount=0;
      for(int i=0;i<hhPairs;i++) { evtTime[evtCount]=SHt[i+1]; evtCompliant[evtCount]=hhCompliant[i]; evtCount++; }
      for(int j=0;j<hlPairs;j++) { evtTime[evtCount]=SLt[j+1]; evtCompliant[evtCount]=hlCompliant[j]; evtCount++; }
      for(int a=1;a<evtCount;a++)
        {
         datetime kt=evtTime[a]; bool kc=evtCompliant[a]; int b=a-1;
         while(b>=0 && evtTime[b]>kt) { evtTime[b+1]=evtTime[b]; evtCompliant[b+1]=evtCompliant[b]; b--; }
         evtTime[b+1]=kt; evtCompliant[b+1]=kc;
        }
      double wSum=0.0, wcSum=0.0;
      for(int e=0;e<evtCount;e++) { double wgt=e+1; wSum+=wgt; if(evtCompliant[e]) wcSum+=wgt; }
      sh.structuralContinuity = (wSum>0.0) ? Clamp0to100(100.0*wcSum/wSum) : 0.0;

      //--- PullbackScore: walk the cleaned alternating sequence for Low->High->Low triples, using the
      //--- operator's own worked example formula verbatim (legRange=HH-prevHL, retracement=HH-nextHL).
      double pullbackSum=0.0; int pullbackLegs=0;
      string pbJ="[";
      for(int c=0;c<cleanCount-2;c++)
        {
         if(!cIsHigh[c] && cIsHigh[c+1] && !cIsHigh[c+2])
           {
            double prevHL=cPrice[c], hhv=cPrice[c+1], nextHL=cPrice[c+2];
            double legRange = hhv-prevHL; if(legRange<=0.0) legRange=_Point;
            double retracement = hhv-nextHL;
            double pullbackPct = 100.0*retracement/legRange;
            double legScore = Clamp0to100(100.0-pullbackPct);
            pullbackSum += legScore; pullbackLegs++;
            if(pullbackLegs>1) pbJ+=",";
            pbJ += StringFormat("%.2f", pullbackPct);
           }
        }
      pbJ += "]";
      sh.pullbackPctJson = pbJ;
      sh.pullbackScore = (pullbackLegs>0) ? (pullbackSum/pullbackLegs) : 0.0;

      //--- EvidenceConfidence: target=6 total pairs, taken directly from the reference diagram's own
      //--- 4-high/4-low (3+3 pair) canonical pattern - PROVISIONAL for Phase 1, unchanged per instruction.
      int totalPairsFound = hhPairs + hlPairs;
      sh.evidenceConfidence = MathMax(0.0, MathMin(1.0, totalPairsFound/6.0));

      sh.structuralScore = Clamp0to100(sh.evidenceConfidence * Clamp0to100(sh.structuralContinuity*0.60 + sh.pullbackScore*0.40));
     }

   //--- Step 5: RunningContinuationScore - live, unconfirmed evidence only. Only evaluated when BOTH a
   //--- latest confirmed HH and HL exist (so the leg range used to normalize the live move is real and
   //--- meaningful, not a fabricated fallback). Never alters anything computed above.
   sh.runningContinuationScore = 50.0; // neutral baseline
   if(ci.runningIncluded && sh.haveLatestHH && sh.haveLatestHL)
     {
      double legRangeRef = sh.latestConfirmedHH - sh.latestConfirmedHL;
      if(legRangeRef<=0.0) legRangeRef=_Point;
      if(ci.newestHigh>sh.latestConfirmedHH)
        {
         sh.liveExtension = true;
         double extensionPct = 100.0*(ci.newestHigh-sh.latestConfirmedHH)/legRangeRef;
         sh.runningContinuationScore = Clamp0to100(50.0+extensionPct);
        }
      else if(ci.newestLow<sh.latestConfirmedHL)
        {
         sh.liveBreakdown = true;
         double breachPct = 100.0*(sh.latestConfirmedHL-ci.newestLow)/legRangeRef;
         sh.runningContinuationScore = Clamp0to100(50.0-breachPct);
        }
     }

   //--- Step 6: final raw diagnostic score - APPROVED OPTION B. Diagnostic only; see this function's
   //--- own header for the full Phase 1 safety statement (never enters scores[]/argmax/g_dnaState).
   sh.rawScore = Clamp0to100(sh.structuralScore*0.80 + sh.runningContinuationScore*0.20);

   return sh;
  }

//====================================================================
// STAGE 1a-SHADOW (BEARISH), 2026-08-25 (explicit operator request, PHASE 1 - LOG-ONLY): bearish
// structural mirror of EvaluateStrongUptrendShadow() above. INDEPENDENT implementation (not shared
// code) so the frozen STRONG_UPTREND function above is never touched. Same 26-candle window, same
// fh=2 fractal, same zigzag cleanup RULE (keep the higher of consecutive highs / lower of consecutive
// lows - swing detection is a direction-agnostic reconstruction of real price extremes; only the
// SCORING comparisons below are bearish-flipped: falling-high/falling-low pair compliance instead of
// rising, a High->Low->High pullback leg instead of Low->High->Low, and the running-candle
// extension/breakdown roles swapped between newestLow/newestHigh). Same Phase 1 safety statement as
// STRONG_UPTREND applies verbatim: never enters scores[], CalibrateMarketDNAScores(), g_dnaState,
// CurrentRegimeAllowed(), Entry Approval, Minds, TP/SL, execution, or the Opportunity
// Lifecycle/Trend-C re-fire logic - read only by its own diagnostic log line below.
//====================================================================
StrongDowntrendShadow EvaluateStrongDowntrendShadow(const MqlRates &rates[], const int k, const CandleIntelligence &ci)
  {
   StrongDowntrendShadow sh;
   sh.swingHighCount=0; sh.swingLowCount=0; sh.lhScore=0.0; sh.llScore=0.0; sh.structuralContinuity=0.0;
   sh.pullbackScore=0.0; sh.evidenceConfidence=0.0; sh.structuralScore=0.0; sh.runningContinuationScore=50.0;
   sh.rawScore=0.0; sh.haveLatestLH=false; sh.latestConfirmedLH=0.0; sh.haveLatestLL=false; sh.latestConfirmedLL=0.0;
   sh.liveExtension=false; sh.liveBreakdown=false;
   sh.swingStructureJson="[]"; sh.lhComplianceJson="[]"; sh.llComplianceJson="[]"; sh.pullbackPctJson="[]";

   int fh = KMIE_UPTREND_FRACTAL_HALFWIDTH; // same fractal half-width constant, reused (not redefined)
   if(k < (2*fh+2)) return sh;

   //--- Step 1: raw confirmed swing detection - IDENTICAL technique/direction-agnostic to STRONG_UPTREND's.
   bool     isHighArr[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   double   priceArr[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   datetime timeArr[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   int rawCount=0;
   for(int i=k-1-fh; i>=fh && rawCount<KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS; i--)
     {
      bool isSwingHigh=true, isSwingLow=true;
      for(int w=1; w<=fh; w++)
        {
         if(rates[i].high<=rates[i-w].high || rates[i].high<=rates[i+w].high) isSwingHigh=false;
         if(rates[i].low>=rates[i-w].low   || rates[i].low>=rates[i+w].low)   isSwingLow=false;
        }
      if(isSwingHigh && rawCount<KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS)
        { isHighArr[rawCount]=true;  priceArr[rawCount]=rates[i].high; timeArr[rawCount]=rates[i].time; rawCount++; }
      if(isSwingLow && rawCount<KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS)
        { isHighArr[rawCount]=false; priceArr[rawCount]=rates[i].low;  timeArr[rawCount]=rates[i].time; rawCount++; }
     }

   //--- Step 2: zigzag cleanup - SAME rule as STRONG_UPTREND (keep the higher of consecutive highs,
   //--- lower of consecutive lows). This is a neutral reconstruction of the market's true extremes,
   //--- not a bullish-biased choice - verified before implementation, documented in this session's
   //--- design-review response (see the pre-implementation audit for this task).
   bool     cIsHigh[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   double   cPrice[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   datetime cTime[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   int cleanCount=0;
   for(int r=0; r<rawCount; r++)
     {
      if(cleanCount>0 && cIsHigh[cleanCount-1]==isHighArr[r])
        {
         bool moreExtreme = isHighArr[r] ? (priceArr[r]>cPrice[cleanCount-1]) : (priceArr[r]<cPrice[cleanCount-1]);
         if(moreExtreme) { cPrice[cleanCount-1]=priceArr[r]; cTime[cleanCount-1]=timeArr[r]; }
        }
      else
        { cIsHigh[cleanCount]=isHighArr[r]; cPrice[cleanCount]=priceArr[r]; cTime[cleanCount]=timeArr[r]; cleanCount++; }
     }

   //--- Step 3: split into SH[]/SL[] (chronological) - here SH holds candidate Lower-Highs (LH), SL
   //--- holds candidate Lower-Lows (LL); naming kept as SH/SL internally to mirror the reference
   //--- implementation's structure exactly, interpreted as LH/LL by the scoring steps below.
   double   SH[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS]; datetime SHt[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS]; int mH=0;
   double   SL[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS]; datetime SLt[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS]; int pL=0;
   string structJson="[";
   for(int c=0;c<cleanCount;c++)
     {
      if(c>0) structJson+=",";
      structJson += StringFormat("{\"type\":\"%s\",\"price\":%.3f}", cIsHigh[c]?"LH":"LL", cPrice[c]);
      if(cIsHigh[c]) { SH[mH]=cPrice[c]; SHt[mH]=cTime[c]; mH++; }
      else           { SL[pL]=cPrice[c]; SLt[pL]=cTime[c]; pL++; }
     }
   structJson += "]";
   sh.swingStructureJson = structJson;
   sh.swingHighCount = mH;
   sh.swingLowCount  = pL;
   if(mH>0) { sh.haveLatestLH=true; sh.latestConfirmedLH=SH[mH-1]; }
   if(pL>0) { sh.haveLatestLL=true; sh.latestConfirmedLL=SL[pL-1]; }

   //--- Step 4: minimum evidence gate - identical to STRONG_UPTREND. Above the gate: LHScore/LLScore
   //--- use FALLING pair-compliance (SH[i+1]<SH[i] / SL[j+1]<SL[j]) - the bearish flip of STRONG_
   //--- UPTREND's rising-pair test - everything else (recency-weighted continuity, evidence target=6)
   //--- is architecturally identical.
   if(mH>=2 && pL>=2)
     {
      int  lhPairs = mH-1, lhFalling=0;
      bool lhCompliant[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
      for(int i=0;i<lhPairs;i++) { lhCompliant[i]=(SH[i+1]<SH[i]); if(lhCompliant[i]) lhFalling++; }
      sh.lhScore = 100.0*lhFalling/lhPairs;

      int  llPairs = pL-1, llFalling=0;
      bool llCompliant[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
      for(int j=0;j<llPairs;j++) { llCompliant[j]=(SL[j+1]<SL[j]); if(llCompliant[j]) llFalling++; }
      sh.llScore = 100.0*llFalling/llPairs;

      string lhJ="["; for(int i=0;i<lhPairs;i++){ if(i>0) lhJ+=","; lhJ+=(lhCompliant[i]?"1":"0"); } lhJ+="]";
      string llJ="["; for(int j=0;j<llPairs;j++){ if(j>0) llJ+=","; llJ+=(llCompliant[j]?"1":"0"); } llJ+="]";
      sh.lhComplianceJson = lhJ;
      sh.llComplianceJson = llJ;

      datetime evtTime[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS*2];
      bool     evtCompliant[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS*2];
      int evtCount=0;
      for(int i=0;i<lhPairs;i++) { evtTime[evtCount]=SHt[i+1]; evtCompliant[evtCount]=lhCompliant[i]; evtCount++; }
      for(int j=0;j<llPairs;j++) { evtTime[evtCount]=SLt[j+1]; evtCompliant[evtCount]=llCompliant[j]; evtCount++; }
      for(int a=1;a<evtCount;a++)
        {
         datetime kt=evtTime[a]; bool kc=evtCompliant[a]; int b=a-1;
         while(b>=0 && evtTime[b]>kt) { evtTime[b+1]=evtTime[b]; evtCompliant[b+1]=evtCompliant[b]; b--; }
         evtTime[b+1]=kt; evtCompliant[b+1]=kc;
        }
      double wSum=0.0, wcSum=0.0;
      for(int e=0;e<evtCount;e++) { double wgt=e+1; wSum+=wgt; if(evtCompliant[e]) wcSum+=wgt; }
      sh.structuralContinuity = (wSum>0.0) ? Clamp0to100(100.0*wcSum/wSum) : 0.0;

      //--- PullbackScore: bearish leg = High->Low->High triple (the mirror of STRONG_UPTREND's
      //--- Low->High->Low): legRange=prevLH-LL, retracement=nextLH-LL, per the operator's own worked
      //--- example (4700/4650/4675 -> 50% pullback). If nextLH exceeds prevLH, pullbackPct>100 and
      //--- Clamp0to100(100-pullbackPct) floors to 0 automatically - no separate failure penalty added,
      //--- exactly per instruction.
      double pullbackSum=0.0; int pullbackLegs=0;
      string pbJ="[";
      for(int c=0;c<cleanCount-2;c++)
        {
         if(cIsHigh[c] && !cIsHigh[c+1] && cIsHigh[c+2])
           {
            double prevLH=cPrice[c], llv=cPrice[c+1], nextLH=cPrice[c+2];
            double legRange = prevLH-llv; if(legRange<=0.0) legRange=_Point;
            double retracement = nextLH-llv;
            double pullbackPct = 100.0*retracement/legRange;
            double legScore = Clamp0to100(100.0-pullbackPct);
            pullbackSum += legScore; pullbackLegs++;
            if(pullbackLegs>1) pbJ+=",";
            pbJ += StringFormat("%.2f", pullbackPct);
           }
        }
      pbJ += "]";
      sh.pullbackPctJson = pbJ;
      sh.pullbackScore = (pullbackLegs>0) ? (pullbackSum/pullbackLegs) : 0.0;

      int totalPairsFound = lhPairs + llPairs;
      sh.evidenceConfidence = MathMax(0.0, MathMin(1.0, totalPairsFound/6.0));

      sh.structuralScore = Clamp0to100(sh.evidenceConfidence * Clamp0to100(sh.structuralContinuity*0.60 + sh.pullbackScore*0.40));
     }

   //--- Step 5: RunningContinuationScore - bearish mirror. legRangeRef uses the same LH-LL geometry
   //--- (LH is always the higher reference, LL the lower, exactly like HH/HL). A live low BELOW the
   //--- latest confirmed LL is bearish extension (score up); a live high ABOVE the latest confirmed LH
   //--- is a bullish threat to the bearish structure (score down) - the exact roles STRONG_UPTREND's
   //--- newestHigh/newestLow play are swapped here, nothing else about the scaling changes.
   sh.runningContinuationScore = 50.0;
   if(ci.runningIncluded && sh.haveLatestLH && sh.haveLatestLL)
     {
      double legRangeRef = sh.latestConfirmedLH - sh.latestConfirmedLL;
      if(legRangeRef<=0.0) legRangeRef=_Point;
      if(ci.newestLow<sh.latestConfirmedLL)
        {
         sh.liveExtension = true;
         double extensionPct = 100.0*(sh.latestConfirmedLL-ci.newestLow)/legRangeRef;
         sh.runningContinuationScore = Clamp0to100(50.0+extensionPct);
        }
      else if(ci.newestHigh>sh.latestConfirmedLH)
        {
         sh.liveBreakdown = true;
         double breachPct = 100.0*(ci.newestHigh-sh.latestConfirmedLH)/legRangeRef;
         sh.runningContinuationScore = Clamp0to100(50.0-breachPct);
        }
     }

   //--- Step 6: final raw diagnostic score - same 80/20 architecture as STRONG_UPTREND.
   sh.rawScore = Clamp0to100(sh.structuralScore*0.80 + sh.runningContinuationScore*0.20);

   return sh;
  }

//====================================================================
// STAGE 1a-SHADOW (DNA #21 "UPTREND"), 2026-08-25 (explicit operator request, PHASE 1 - LOG-ONLY):
// broader bullish HH/HL structural regime, distinct from LDNA_STRONG_UPTREND. Swing detection,
// zigzag cleanup, HHScore/HLScore, and StructuralContinuity are IDENTICAL bullish-direction logic to
// EvaluateStrongUptrendShadow() above (same fh=2 fractal, same rising-pair compliance, same recency
// weighting) - INDEPENDENT implementation (not shared code), so the frozen STRONG_UPTREND function is
// never touched. The ONLY formula difference from STRONG_UPTREND is PullbackScore: instead of the
// linear Clamp0to100(100-pullbackPct), this uses the APPROVED Option C tolerance-band curve (design
// approval, this session) built on the EA's own pre-existing 80% resumption boundary
// (RESUMPTION_0_TO_80/pullbackTooDeep, Entry Intelligence Step 10) rather than an invented number:
//     pullbackPct <= 80        -> 100 (full credit)
//     80 < pullbackPct < 100   -> ((100-pullbackPct)/20)*100  (continuous, no discontinuity at 80)
//     pullbackPct >= 100       -> 0
// StructuralScore/RawScore keep the exact same 0.60/0.40 and 0.80/0.20 architecture as STRONG_UPTREND
// - per instruction, the differentiation comes from the pullback-response function, not new weights.
// Same Phase 1 safety statement as STRONG_UPTREND applies verbatim: never enters scores[],
// CalibrateMarketDNAScores(), g_dnaState, CurrentRegimeAllowed(), Entry Approval, Minds, TP/SL,
// execution, or the Opportunity Lifecycle/Trend-C re-fire logic.
//====================================================================
UptrendShadow EvaluateUptrendShadow(const MqlRates &rates[], const int k, const CandleIntelligence &ci)
  {
   UptrendShadow sh;
   sh.swingHighCount=0; sh.swingLowCount=0; sh.hhScore=0.0; sh.hlScore=0.0; sh.structuralContinuity=0.0;
   sh.pullbackScore=0.0; sh.evidenceConfidence=0.0; sh.structuralScore=0.0; sh.runningContinuationScore=50.0;
   sh.rawScore=0.0; sh.haveLatestHH=false; sh.latestConfirmedHH=0.0; sh.haveLatestHL=false; sh.latestConfirmedHL=0.0;
   sh.liveExtension=false; sh.liveBreakdown=false;
   sh.swingStructureJson="[]"; sh.hhComplianceJson="[]"; sh.hlComplianceJson="[]"; sh.pullbackPctJson="[]";

   int fh = KMIE_UPTREND_FRACTAL_HALFWIDTH; // reused constant, not redefined
   if(k < (2*fh+2)) return sh;

   //--- Step 1: raw confirmed swing detection - identical bullish-direction technique.
   bool     isHighArr[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   double   priceArr[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   datetime timeArr[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   int rawCount=0;
   for(int i=k-1-fh; i>=fh && rawCount<KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS; i--)
     {
      bool isSwingHigh=true, isSwingLow=true;
      for(int w=1; w<=fh; w++)
        {
         if(rates[i].high<=rates[i-w].high || rates[i].high<=rates[i+w].high) isSwingHigh=false;
         if(rates[i].low>=rates[i-w].low   || rates[i].low>=rates[i+w].low)   isSwingLow=false;
        }
      if(isSwingHigh && rawCount<KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS)
        { isHighArr[rawCount]=true;  priceArr[rawCount]=rates[i].high; timeArr[rawCount]=rates[i].time; rawCount++; }
      if(isSwingLow && rawCount<KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS)
        { isHighArr[rawCount]=false; priceArr[rawCount]=rates[i].low;  timeArr[rawCount]=rates[i].time; rawCount++; }
     }

   //--- Step 2: zigzag cleanup - same direction-agnostic rule (keep higher of consecutive highs,
   //--- lower of consecutive lows).
   bool     cIsHigh[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   double   cPrice[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   datetime cTime[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   int cleanCount=0;
   for(int r=0; r<rawCount; r++)
     {
      if(cleanCount>0 && cIsHigh[cleanCount-1]==isHighArr[r])
        {
         bool moreExtreme = isHighArr[r] ? (priceArr[r]>cPrice[cleanCount-1]) : (priceArr[r]<cPrice[cleanCount-1]);
         if(moreExtreme) { cPrice[cleanCount-1]=priceArr[r]; cTime[cleanCount-1]=timeArr[r]; }
        }
      else
        { cIsHigh[cleanCount]=isHighArr[r]; cPrice[cleanCount]=priceArr[r]; cTime[cleanCount]=timeArr[r]; cleanCount++; }
     }

   //--- Step 3: split into SH[]/SL[] (chronological).
   double   SH[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS]; datetime SHt[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS]; int mH=0;
   double   SL[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS]; datetime SLt[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS]; int pL=0;
   string structJson="[";
   for(int c=0;c<cleanCount;c++)
     {
      if(c>0) structJson+=",";
      structJson += StringFormat("{\"type\":\"%s\",\"price\":%.3f}", cIsHigh[c]?"HH":"HL", cPrice[c]);
      if(cIsHigh[c]) { SH[mH]=cPrice[c]; SHt[mH]=cTime[c]; mH++; }
      else           { SL[pL]=cPrice[c]; SLt[pL]=cTime[c]; pL++; }
     }
   structJson += "]";
   sh.swingStructureJson = structJson;
   sh.swingHighCount = mH;
   sh.swingLowCount  = pL;
   if(mH>0) { sh.haveLatestHH=true; sh.latestConfirmedHH=SH[mH-1]; }
   if(pL>0) { sh.haveLatestHL=true; sh.latestConfirmedHL=SL[pL-1]; }

   //--- Step 4: minimum evidence gate - identical to STRONG_UPTREND. HH/HL scores use RISING pair
   //--- compliance (SH[i+1]>SH[i] / SL[j+1]>SL[j]) - bullish, same as STRONG_UPTREND, NOT flipped.
   if(mH>=2 && pL>=2)
     {
      int  hhPairs = mH-1, hhRising=0;
      bool hhCompliant[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
      for(int i=0;i<hhPairs;i++) { hhCompliant[i]=(SH[i+1]>SH[i]); if(hhCompliant[i]) hhRising++; }
      sh.hhScore = 100.0*hhRising/hhPairs;

      int  hlPairs = pL-1, hlRising=0;
      bool hlCompliant[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
      for(int j=0;j<hlPairs;j++) { hlCompliant[j]=(SL[j+1]>SL[j]); if(hlCompliant[j]) hlRising++; }
      sh.hlScore = 100.0*hlRising/hlPairs;

      string hhJ="["; for(int i=0;i<hhPairs;i++){ if(i>0) hhJ+=","; hhJ+=(hhCompliant[i]?"1":"0"); } hhJ+="]";
      string hlJ="["; for(int j=0;j<hlPairs;j++){ if(j>0) hlJ+=","; hlJ+=(hlCompliant[j]?"1":"0"); } hlJ+="]";
      sh.hhComplianceJson = hhJ;
      sh.hlComplianceJson = hlJ;

      datetime evtTime[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS*2];
      bool     evtCompliant[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS*2];
      int evtCount=0;
      for(int i=0;i<hhPairs;i++) { evtTime[evtCount]=SHt[i+1]; evtCompliant[evtCount]=hhCompliant[i]; evtCount++; }
      for(int j=0;j<hlPairs;j++) { evtTime[evtCount]=SLt[j+1]; evtCompliant[evtCount]=hlCompliant[j]; evtCount++; }
      for(int a=1;a<evtCount;a++)
        {
         datetime kt=evtTime[a]; bool kc=evtCompliant[a]; int b=a-1;
         while(b>=0 && evtTime[b]>kt) { evtTime[b+1]=evtTime[b]; evtCompliant[b+1]=evtCompliant[b]; b--; }
         evtTime[b+1]=kt; evtCompliant[b+1]=kc;
        }
      double wSum=0.0, wcSum=0.0;
      for(int e=0;e<evtCount;e++) { double wgt=e+1; wSum+=wgt; if(evtCompliant[e]) wcSum+=wgt; }
      sh.structuralContinuity = (wSum>0.0) ? Clamp0to100(100.0*wcSum/wSum) : 0.0;

      //--- PullbackScore - APPROVED OPTION C tolerance-band curve (this is the ONLY formula
      //--- difference from STRONG_UPTREND's linear Clamp0to100(100-pullbackPct)). Same Low->High->Low
      //--- leg walk over the cleaned sequence, same legRange/retracement/pullbackPct calculation -
      //--- only the pullbackPct->score mapping changes.
      double pullbackSum=0.0; int pullbackLegs=0;
      string pbJ="[";
      for(int c=0;c<cleanCount-2;c++)
        {
         if(!cIsHigh[c] && cIsHigh[c+1] && !cIsHigh[c+2])
           {
            double prevHL=cPrice[c], hhv=cPrice[c+1], nextHL=cPrice[c+2];
            double legRange = hhv-prevHL; if(legRange<=0.0) legRange=_Point;
            double retracement = hhv-nextHL;
            double pullbackPct = 100.0*retracement/legRange;
            double legScore;
            if(pullbackPct<=80.0)       legScore = 100.0;
            else if(pullbackPct<100.0)  legScore = ((100.0-pullbackPct)/20.0)*100.0;
            else                        legScore = 0.0;
            legScore = Clamp0to100(legScore);
            pullbackSum += legScore; pullbackLegs++;
            if(pullbackLegs>1) pbJ+=",";
            pbJ += StringFormat("%.2f", pullbackPct);
           }
        }
      pbJ += "]";
      sh.pullbackPctJson = pbJ;
      sh.pullbackScore = (pullbackLegs>0) ? (pullbackSum/pullbackLegs) : 0.0;

      int totalPairsFound = hhPairs + hlPairs;
      sh.evidenceConfidence = MathMax(0.0, MathMin(1.0, totalPairsFound/6.0));

      //--- StructuralScore - SAME 0.60/0.40 architecture as STRONG_UPTREND, unchanged per instruction.
      //--- The tolerance-band PullbackScore above still feeds this at the same weight - it does not
      //--- override structure: a broken HL/HH sequence still shows up in StructuralContinuity
      //--- regardless of how tolerant the pullback curve is.
      sh.structuralScore = Clamp0to100(sh.evidenceConfidence * Clamp0to100(sh.structuralContinuity*0.60 + sh.pullbackScore*0.40));
     }

   //--- Step 5: RunningContinuationScore - identical bullish-direction logic to STRONG_UPTREND.
   sh.runningContinuationScore = 50.0;
   if(ci.runningIncluded && sh.haveLatestHH && sh.haveLatestHL)
     {
      double legRangeRef = sh.latestConfirmedHH - sh.latestConfirmedHL;
      if(legRangeRef<=0.0) legRangeRef=_Point;
      if(ci.newestHigh>sh.latestConfirmedHH)
        {
         sh.liveExtension = true;
         double extensionPct = 100.0*(ci.newestHigh-sh.latestConfirmedHH)/legRangeRef;
         sh.runningContinuationScore = Clamp0to100(50.0+extensionPct);
        }
      else if(ci.newestLow<sh.latestConfirmedHL)
        {
         sh.liveBreakdown = true;
         double breachPct = 100.0*(sh.latestConfirmedHL-ci.newestLow)/legRangeRef;
         sh.runningContinuationScore = Clamp0to100(50.0-breachPct);
        }
     }

   //--- Step 6: final raw diagnostic score - same 80/20 architecture as STRONG_UPTREND, unchanged.
   sh.rawScore = Clamp0to100(sh.structuralScore*0.80 + sh.runningContinuationScore*0.20);

   return sh;
  }

//====================================================================
// STAGE 1a-SHADOW (DNA #22 "DOWNTREND"), 2026-08-25 (explicit operator request, PHASE 1 - LOG-ONLY):
// bearish structural counterpart of DNA #21 UPTREND. Swing detection, zigzag cleanup, LHScore/LLScore
// and StructuralContinuity are IDENTICAL bearish-direction logic to EvaluateStrongDowntrendShadow()
// above (same fh=2 fractal, same falling-pair compliance, same recency weighting, same High->Low->High
// pullback-leg geometry). The ONLY formula difference from STRONG_DOWNTREND is PullbackScore: instead
// of the linear Clamp0to100(100-pullbackPct), this uses the SAME APPROVED Option C tolerance-band
// curve already implemented for DNA #21 UPTREND (built on the EA's own pre-existing 80% resumption
// boundary, not an invented number):
//     pullbackPct <= 80        -> 100 (full credit)
//     80 < pullbackPct < 100   -> ((100-pullbackPct)/20)*100  (continuous, no discontinuity at 80)
//     pullbackPct >= 100       -> 0
// StructuralScore/RawScore keep the exact same 0.60/0.40 and 0.80/0.20 architecture as every other
// structural shadow DNA - no new weights invented anywhere in this function. INDEPENDENT
// implementation (not shared code) - EvaluateStrongDowntrendShadow()/EvaluateUptrendShadow() above are
// both untouched. Same Phase 1 safety statement as the other three structural shadows applies
// verbatim: never enters scores[], CalibrateMarketDNAScores(), g_dnaState, CurrentRegimeAllowed(),
// Entry Approval, Minds, TP/SL, execution, Opportunity Lifecycle/Trend-C re-fire, or the
// Accumulation/Distribution 8-Mind Reverse Trade feature.
//====================================================================
DowntrendShadow EvaluateDowntrendShadow(const MqlRates &rates[], const int k, const CandleIntelligence &ci)
  {
   DowntrendShadow sh;
   sh.swingHighCount=0; sh.swingLowCount=0; sh.lhScore=0.0; sh.llScore=0.0; sh.structuralContinuity=0.0;
   sh.pullbackScore=0.0; sh.evidenceConfidence=0.0; sh.structuralScore=0.0; sh.runningContinuationScore=50.0;
   sh.rawScore=0.0; sh.haveLatestLH=false; sh.latestConfirmedLH=0.0; sh.haveLatestLL=false; sh.latestConfirmedLL=0.0;
   sh.liveExtension=false; sh.liveBreakdown=false;
   sh.swingStructureJson="[]"; sh.lhComplianceJson="[]"; sh.llComplianceJson="[]"; sh.pullbackPctJson="[]";

   int fh = KMIE_UPTREND_FRACTAL_HALFWIDTH; // reused constant, not redefined
   if(k < (2*fh+2)) return sh;

   //--- Step 1: raw confirmed swing detection - identical direction-agnostic technique.
   bool     isHighArr[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   double   priceArr[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   datetime timeArr[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   int rawCount=0;
   for(int i=k-1-fh; i>=fh && rawCount<KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS; i--)
     {
      bool isSwingHigh=true, isSwingLow=true;
      for(int w=1; w<=fh; w++)
        {
         if(rates[i].high<=rates[i-w].high || rates[i].high<=rates[i+w].high) isSwingHigh=false;
         if(rates[i].low>=rates[i-w].low   || rates[i].low>=rates[i+w].low)   isSwingLow=false;
        }
      if(isSwingHigh && rawCount<KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS)
        { isHighArr[rawCount]=true;  priceArr[rawCount]=rates[i].high; timeArr[rawCount]=rates[i].time; rawCount++; }
      if(isSwingLow && rawCount<KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS)
        { isHighArr[rawCount]=false; priceArr[rawCount]=rates[i].low;  timeArr[rawCount]=rates[i].time; rawCount++; }
     }

   //--- Step 2: zigzag cleanup - same direction-agnostic rule.
   bool     cIsHigh[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   double   cPrice[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   datetime cTime[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
   int cleanCount=0;
   for(int r=0; r<rawCount; r++)
     {
      if(cleanCount>0 && cIsHigh[cleanCount-1]==isHighArr[r])
        {
         bool moreExtreme = isHighArr[r] ? (priceArr[r]>cPrice[cleanCount-1]) : (priceArr[r]<cPrice[cleanCount-1]);
         if(moreExtreme) { cPrice[cleanCount-1]=priceArr[r]; cTime[cleanCount-1]=timeArr[r]; }
        }
      else
        { cIsHigh[cleanCount]=isHighArr[r]; cPrice[cleanCount]=priceArr[r]; cTime[cleanCount]=timeArr[r]; cleanCount++; }
     }

   //--- Step 3: split into SH[]/SL[] (chronological) - LH/LL naming per DOWNTREND's own semantics.
   double   SH[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS]; datetime SHt[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS]; int mH=0;
   double   SL[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS]; datetime SLt[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS]; int pL=0;
   string structJson="[";
   for(int c=0;c<cleanCount;c++)
     {
      if(c>0) structJson+=",";
      structJson += StringFormat("{\"type\":\"%s\",\"price\":%.3f}", cIsHigh[c]?"LH":"LL", cPrice[c]);
      if(cIsHigh[c]) { SH[mH]=cPrice[c]; SHt[mH]=cTime[c]; mH++; }
      else           { SL[pL]=cPrice[c]; SLt[pL]=cTime[c]; pL++; }
     }
   structJson += "]";
   sh.swingStructureJson = structJson;
   sh.swingHighCount = mH;
   sh.swingLowCount  = pL;
   if(mH>0) { sh.haveLatestLH=true; sh.latestConfirmedLH=SH[mH-1]; }
   if(pL>0) { sh.haveLatestLL=true; sh.latestConfirmedLL=SL[pL-1]; }

   //--- Step 4: minimum evidence gate - identical to STRONG_DOWNTREND. LH/LL scores use FALLING pair
   //--- compliance (SH[i+1]<SH[i] / SL[j+1]<SL[j]) - bearish, same as STRONG_DOWNTREND.
   if(mH>=2 && pL>=2)
     {
      int  lhPairs = mH-1, lhFalling=0;
      bool lhCompliant[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
      for(int i=0;i<lhPairs;i++) { lhCompliant[i]=(SH[i+1]<SH[i]); if(lhCompliant[i]) lhFalling++; }
      sh.lhScore = 100.0*lhFalling/lhPairs;

      int  llPairs = pL-1, llFalling=0;
      bool llCompliant[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS];
      for(int j=0;j<llPairs;j++) { llCompliant[j]=(SL[j+1]<SL[j]); if(llCompliant[j]) llFalling++; }
      sh.llScore = 100.0*llFalling/llPairs;

      string lhJ="["; for(int i=0;i<lhPairs;i++){ if(i>0) lhJ+=","; lhJ+=(lhCompliant[i]?"1":"0"); } lhJ+="]";
      string llJ="["; for(int j=0;j<llPairs;j++){ if(j>0) llJ+=","; llJ+=(llCompliant[j]?"1":"0"); } llJ+="]";
      sh.lhComplianceJson = lhJ;
      sh.llComplianceJson = llJ;

      datetime evtTime[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS*2];
      bool     evtCompliant[KMIE_UPTREND_MAX_SWINGS*2];
      int evtCount=0;
      for(int i=0;i<lhPairs;i++) { evtTime[evtCount]=SHt[i+1]; evtCompliant[evtCount]=lhCompliant[i]; evtCount++; }
      for(int j=0;j<llPairs;j++) { evtTime[evtCount]=SLt[j+1]; evtCompliant[evtCount]=llCompliant[j]; evtCount++; }
      for(int a=1;a<evtCount;a++)
        {
         datetime kt=evtTime[a]; bool kc=evtCompliant[a]; int b=a-1;
         while(b>=0 && evtTime[b]>kt) { evtTime[b+1]=evtTime[b]; evtCompliant[b+1]=evtCompliant[b]; b--; }
         evtTime[b+1]=kt; evtCompliant[b+1]=kc;
        }
      double wSum=0.0, wcSum=0.0;
      for(int e=0;e<evtCount;e++) { double wgt=e+1; wSum+=wgt; if(evtCompliant[e]) wcSum+=wgt; }
      sh.structuralContinuity = (wSum>0.0) ? Clamp0to100(100.0*wcSum/wSum) : 0.0;

      //--- PullbackScore - APPROVED OPTION C tolerance-band curve applied to the validated bearish
      //--- High->Low->High leg geometry (legRange=prevLH-LL, retracement=nextLH-LL, per STRONG_
      //--- DOWNTREND's own worked example). Only the pullbackPct->score mapping differs from
      //--- STRONG_DOWNTREND's linear formula.
      double pullbackSum=0.0; int pullbackLegs=0;
      string pbJ="[";
      for(int c=0;c<cleanCount-2;c++)
        {
         if(cIsHigh[c] && !cIsHigh[c+1] && cIsHigh[c+2])
           {
            double prevLH=cPrice[c], llv=cPrice[c+1], nextLH=cPrice[c+2];
            double legRange = prevLH-llv; if(legRange<=0.0) legRange=_Point;
            double retracement = nextLH-llv;
            double pullbackPct = 100.0*retracement/legRange;
            double legScore;
            if(pullbackPct<=80.0)       legScore = 100.0;
            else if(pullbackPct<100.0)  legScore = ((100.0-pullbackPct)/20.0)*100.0;
            else                        legScore = 0.0;
            legScore = Clamp0to100(legScore);
            pullbackSum += legScore; pullbackLegs++;
            if(pullbackLegs>1) pbJ+=",";
            pbJ += StringFormat("%.2f", pullbackPct);
           }
        }
      pbJ += "]";
      sh.pullbackPctJson = pbJ;
      sh.pullbackScore = (pullbackLegs>0) ? (pullbackSum/pullbackLegs) : 0.0;

      int totalPairsFound = lhPairs + llPairs;
      sh.evidenceConfidence = MathMax(0.0, MathMin(1.0, totalPairsFound/6.0));

      sh.structuralScore = Clamp0to100(sh.evidenceConfidence * Clamp0to100(sh.structuralContinuity*0.60 + sh.pullbackScore*0.40));
     }

   //--- Step 5: RunningContinuationScore - identical bearish-direction logic to STRONG_DOWNTREND.
   sh.runningContinuationScore = 50.0;
   if(ci.runningIncluded && sh.haveLatestLH && sh.haveLatestLL)
     {
      double legRangeRef = sh.latestConfirmedLH - sh.latestConfirmedLL;
      if(legRangeRef<=0.0) legRangeRef=_Point;
      if(ci.newestLow<sh.latestConfirmedLL)
        {
         sh.liveExtension = true;
         double extensionPct = 100.0*(sh.latestConfirmedLL-ci.newestLow)/legRangeRef;
         sh.runningContinuationScore = Clamp0to100(50.0+extensionPct);
        }
      else if(ci.newestHigh>sh.latestConfirmedLH)
        {
         sh.liveBreakdown = true;
         double breachPct = 100.0*(ci.newestHigh-sh.latestConfirmedLH)/legRangeRef;
         sh.runningContinuationScore = Clamp0to100(50.0-breachPct);
        }
     }

   //--- Step 6: final raw diagnostic score - same 80/20 architecture, unchanged.
   sh.rawScore = Clamp0to100(sh.structuralScore*0.80 + sh.runningContinuationScore*0.20);

   return sh;
  }

//====================================================================
// STEP 13, 2026-08-24 (explicit operator request): MARKET DNA SCORE CALIBRATION LAYER.
//
// PROBLEM (proven, not assumed - see the Step 12/13 forensic audits): the 18 raw formulas below
// are NOT on a comparable scale. Some (NEUTRAL, VOLATILITY_EXPANSION/COMPRESSION, COMPRESSION,
// INSTITUTIONAL_BUYING/SELLING) can realistically reach 70-100. Others (STRONG_TREND, WEAK_TREND,
// PULLBACK, EXPANSION, BREAKOUT, TREND_EXHAUSTION, CHOPPY) structurally cap out far lower on real
// gold M1 data - confirmed by replaying all 18 raw formulas over 1,601 real historical bars
// (dna_audit.py): e.g. EXPANSION never exceeded 50.0 (an algebraic near-constant, aggression+
// noiseIndex sum close to 100 per candle), STRONG_TREND never exceeded 65.2, while NEUTRAL reached
// 94.4 and VOLATILITY_EXPANSION reached 100.0 - in the SAME 1,601-bar sample. A pure winner-take-
// all argmax over raw scores on different scales structurally starves the low-ceiling states,
// regardless of what the market is actually doing - this is why 10 of 18 states never won even once.
//
// APPROACH: z-score standardization, NOT a raw multiplier and NOT per-state min-max rescaling.
// A per-state min-max approach was tested first and REJECTED - it produced a WORSE distortion
// (EXPANSION alone winning 48% of bars, because its raw scores cluster tightly near its own
// ceiling with almost no real variance, so min-max amplified routine noise into a false "at max"
// reading almost every bar). Z-score corrects for BOTH each state's typical level (mean) AND its
// own spread (stdev), answering the honest question "is THIS reading unusually extreme for THIS
// specific metric" rather than "is this near this metric's all-time high" - validated by replaying
// the exact same 1,601 real bars: every one of the 18 states won at least some bars (min 0.12%,
// max 16.50%), with no single state exceeding ~17% (vs. 36.7% for VOLATILITY_COMPRESSION alone
// under the old raw competition) - see dna_calibration_validate.py for the full validation run.
//
// mean[]/stdev[] below are the ACTUAL measured values from that same 1,601-bar real-data replay -
// not guessed, not arbitrary. Z_SCALE=15.0 is a standard T-score-style convention (points per
// standard deviation), chosen only to keep the calibrated value inside a legible 0-100 band after
// clamping - it does not change which state wins relative to another (that's fully determined by
// each state's own z-score; Z_SCALE is a shared, uniform display-range choice, not a per-state lever).
//
// State MEANING is untouched - every raw formula below is byte-for-byte unchanged by this layer.
// This function only touches the FINAL comparison step (argmax), never Candle Intelligence, never
// any raw formula, never CurrentRegimeAllowed()/Inp_Allow_*, never anything in Entry Intelligence,
// Opportunity Lifecycle, Entry Approval, or execution.
//====================================================================
